/* Generado automáticamente — contenido del Módulo 4 (B2+) */
window.M1DATA={"topics":[{"n":1,"title":"First Conditionals","es":"Primer condicional","cover":"u:photo-1521791136064-7986c2920216","parts":[{"id":"t1p1","topic":1,"part":1,"title":"If, unless & real possibilities","es":"If, unless y posibilidades reales","acts":["learn","fc1DominoChain","fill","quizShow","unscramble","speak"],"tip":"<p>El <b>primer condicional</b> habla de situaciones <b>reales o muy probables</b> en el presente o el futuro.</p>\n<p>📐 <b>If + presente simple, will / imperativo / modal + verbo</b><br><i>If it <b>rains</b>, we<b>'ll stay</b> in.</i> · <i>If the client calls, <b>tell</b> him I'm busy.</i> · <i>If you don't back up your files, you <b>could</b> lose everything.</i></p>\n<p>🚫 <b>Unless</b> = <i>if … not</i> (a menos que): <i>Unless we leave now, we'll miss the train</i> = <i>If we don't leave now…</i></p>\n<p>⏱️ Con <b>when, as soon as, before, after, until</b> también usamos <b>presente</b> para hablar del futuro: <i>I'll call you <b>as soon as I land</b>.</i></p>\n<p>✍️ Si la oración empieza con <b>if</b>, pon <b>coma</b>; si el <i>if</i> va en medio, no hace falta: <i>We'll stay in if it rains.</i></p>","tips":["Nunca uses <b>will</b> después de <b>if</b>: ❌ <i>If it will rain</i> → ✅ <i>If it rains</i>.","<b>Unless</b> ya es negativo: ❌ <i>unless you don't call</i> → ✅ <i>unless you call</i>.","En la conversación se contrae: <i>If you're late, <b>I'll</b> start without you</i> (suena <i>áil</i>)."],"vocab":[{"en":"unless","es":"a menos que","img":"u:photo-1565972933193-fbc0aa3894a9","v":"m","au":"f61bb9b3f7"},{"en":"as soon as","es":"tan pronto como","img":"u:photo-1653762379954-8943c787e78b","v":"f","au":"12712650c0"},{"en":"miss the deadline","es":"incumplir el plazo","img":"u:photo-1541199249251-f713e6145474","v":"m","au":"4556fc0cf2"},{"en":"meet the deadline","es":"cumplir con el plazo","img":"u:photo-1758691737138-7b9b1884b1db","v":"f","au":"86c3939683"},{"en":"run late","es":"ir con retraso","img":"u:photo-1623975522495-82ea8c48de56","v":"m","au":"0a3610ee57"},{"en":"call it off","es":"cancelarlo / suspenderlo","img":"u:photo-1634223506693-c1c46608791c","v":"f","au":"a3f514cf2e"},{"en":"get stuck in traffic","es":"quedarse atascado en el tráfico","img":"u:photo-1611147533125-9ca445f32036","v":"m","au":"8acb9f5e7a"},{"en":"the odds are","es":"lo más probable es que","img":"u:photo-1778534013714-e7ebe440558c","v":"f","au":"9530dcb87c"},{"en":"If in doubt, ask.","es":"Si tienes dudas, pregunta.","img":"u:photo-1498192467103-290f567eb3a3","v":"f","au":"b7d56bf9f9"},{"en":"weather permitting","es":"si el clima lo permite","img":"u:photo-1654275201618-a767d2b7317c","v":"m","au":"e99ed96541"},{"en":"follow up","es":"hacer seguimiento","img":"u:photo-1543269866-487350d6fa5e","v":"f","au":"546cfec658"},{"en":"back up your files","es":"hacer copia de seguridad","img":"u:photo-1769311483086-bf6be274a143","v":"m","au":"96b6853448"}],"sentences":[{"en":"If you miss the deadline, the client will walk away.","es":"Si incumples el plazo, el cliente se irá.","img":"u:photo-1541199249251-f713e6145474","v":"m","au":"33835f6d36"},{"en":"Unless we leave now, we'll get stuck in traffic.","es":"A menos que salgamos ya, nos quedaremos atascados en el tráfico.","img":"u:photo-1611147533125-9ca445f32036","v":"f","au":"c93064f9f2"},{"en":"If the flight is delayed, text me.","es":"Si el vuelo se retrasa, escríbeme.","img":"u:photo-1764251105292-7a495215a398","v":"f","au":"94df974523"},{"en":"I'll call you as soon as I land.","es":"Te llamaré tan pronto como aterrice.","img":"u:photo-1653762379954-8943c787e78b","v":"m","au":"015db8e900"},{"en":"If you feel sick, you should stay home.","es":"Si te sientes enfermo, deberías quedarte en casa.","img":"u:photo-1550792404-f62d4ce3bb3e","v":"f","au":"1973e7188f"},{"en":"We might call off the picnic if it rains.","es":"Puede que suspendamos el picnic si llueve.","img":"u:photo-1519692933481-e162a57d6721","v":"m","au":"05b0d48b1d"}],"fill":[{"s":"If it ___ tomorrow, we'll move the barbecue indoors.","a":"rains","o":["will rain","rained"],"h":"if + presente simple","full":"If it rains tomorrow, we'll move the barbecue indoors.","au":"99ee1b0f0a"},{"s":"___ you hurry, you'll miss the last train to Brooklyn.","a":"Unless","o":["If","When"],"h":"a menos que","full":"Unless you hurry, you'll miss the last train to Brooklyn.","au":"e5c18317a4"},{"s":"I'll send you the report as soon as I ___ it.","a":"finish","o":["will finish","finished"],"h":"sin will después de as soon as","full":"I'll send you the report as soon as I finish it.","au":"b0e3dd2c26"},{"s":"If the client calls, ___ him I'm in a meeting.","a":"tell","o":["will tell","told"],"h":"imperativo en el resultado","full":"If the client calls, tell him I'm in a meeting.","au":"c5a2edb493"},{"s":"If you don't back up your files, you ___ lose everything.","a":"could","o":["would","did"],"h":"posibilidad (podrías)","full":"If you don't back up your files, you could lose everything.","au":"bd65a0f5a0"},{"s":"We won't sign the contract unless they ___ the price.","a":"lower","o":["don't lower","will lower"],"h":"unless ya es negativo","full":"We won't sign the contract unless they lower the price.","au":"5ea45929a5"},{"s":"When I ___ to Chicago next month, I'll visit you.","a":"get","o":["will get","got"],"h":"when + presente para el futuro","full":"When I get to Chicago next month, I'll visit you.","au":"97ff816461"}],"goal":{"en":"To talk about real possibilities and their consequences with if, unless and as soon as.","es":"Hablar de posibilidades reales y sus consecuencias con if, unless y as soon as."},"warm":[{"q":"What will you do this weekend if the weather is bad?","au":"57f627ab63","es":"¿Qué harás este fin de semana si hace mal tiempo?","ex":"If the weather is bad, I'll stay home and watch a movie."},{"q":"What usually happens if you miss a deadline at work?","au":"ddfc20911c","es":"¿Qué suele pasar si incumples un plazo en el trabajo?","ex":"If I miss a deadline, my boss gets upset and I have to work late."}],"reading":{"title":"The Monday that almost went wrong","img":"u:photo-1541199249251-f713e6145474","text":"Every project manager in our Chicago office knows the golden rule: if something can go wrong, it will. Last Monday, our biggest client asked for a full presentation by five o'clock. My boss looked at me and said, \"If we miss this deadline, they'll walk away. Unless we split the work, we won't make it.\" So we did. I took the numbers, Kara took the design, and Leo took the script. At noon the system crashed. \"Don't panic,\" Kara said. \"If you backed up your files, we'll be fine.\" Luckily, I had. Then Leo got stuck in traffic on the way back from a meeting. \"As soon as I get to the office, I'll record the voice-over,\" he texted. He arrived at 3:40. By 4:55 everything was ready, and we sent the file with five minutes to spare. The client replied an hour later: \"Great work. If this is what you can do on a Monday, we'll renew the contract for two more years.\" Lesson learned: if in doubt, plan for the worst and follow up early.","au":"997f2c43dc","q":[{"s":"The client wanted the presentation by five o'clock.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The team decided to work alone, without splitting tasks.","a":"no"},{"s":"The writer had backed up the files.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Leo was late because he overslept.","a":"no"},{"s":"The client promised to renew the contract.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"What will you do if you lose your phone?","a":"If I lose my phone, I'll block it and call my bank right away.","es":"¿Qué harás si pierdes tu celular?","qau":"09cb1ded1a","aau":"d3f8866eb9"},{"q":"What won't you do unless you have to?","a":"I won't work on Sundays unless I have to.","es":"¿Qué no harás a menos que tengas que hacerlo?","qau":"e55d3fa2c7","aau":"a5923330c2"},{"q":"What will you do as soon as you get home today?","a":"As soon as I get home, I'll take a shower and cook dinner.","es":"¿Qué harás tan pronto llegues a casa hoy?","qau":"a3e28e11e1","aau":"6585615879"},{"q":"What should a team do if it can't meet a deadline?","a":"If it can't meet the deadline, it should tell the client early.","es":"¿Qué debería hacer un equipo si no puede cumplir un plazo?","qau":"32746ed29a","aau":"4adb468453"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe 5 oraciones con primer condicional sobre tu semana: usa if, unless, as soon as y al menos un imperativo o modal en el resultado.","kw":["if","unless","as soon as"],"n":5,"model":"If I finish work early on Friday, I'll go to the gym. Unless it rains, we'll have a barbecue on Saturday. As soon as I get paid, I'll pay my credit card. If my boss calls, tell him I'm on vacation. If I don't sleep well, I might be tired on Monday."}},{"id":"t1p2","topic":1,"part":2,"title":"Negotiating: as long as, provided that, in case","es":"Negociar: as long as, provided that, in case","acts":["learn","fc2DealNegotiator","dialogue","fill","matchLines","speak"],"tip":"<p>En una negociación usamos conectores más precisos que <b>if</b>:</p>\n<p>🤝 <b>as long as / provided (that) / providing</b> = siempre y cuando (una condición obligatoria):<br><i>We'll give you a 10% discount <b>as long as</b> you order 500 units.</i><br><i><b>Provided that</b> the samples arrive on time, we'll sign next week.</i></p>\n<p>☂️ <b>in case</b> = por si acaso (precaución, NO condición): <i>Take an umbrella <b>in case</b> it rains.</i> (llévala ya, llueva o no)<br>Compara: <i>Take an umbrella <b>if</b> it rains</i> (llévala solo si llueve).</p>\n<p>🎯 <b>Only if</b> enfatiza la única condición: <i>We'll sign <b>only if</b> you include free shipping.</i></p>\n<p>Después de todos ellos: <b>presente simple</b>, nunca <i>will</i>.</p>","tips":["<b>Provided that</b> y <b>providing</b> suenan más formales que <b>as long as</b>: úsalos en correos y contratos.","<b>In case</b> no es lo mismo que <b>if</b>: <i>in case</i> = prevenir algo que puede pasar.","Para sonar amable al negociar: <i>I'm afraid that's a deal-breaker for us</i> o <i>Could we meet halfway?</i>"],"vocab":[{"en":"as long as","es":"siempre y cuando","img":"u:photo-1521791136064-7986c2920216","v":"f","au":"f7a789f0b1"},{"en":"provided that","es":"con tal de que / siempre que","img":"u:photo-1562564055-71e051d33c19","v":"m","au":"2b5d91d998"},{"en":"in case","es":"por si acaso","img":"u:photo-1599921248783-3e0489c161b6","v":"f","au":"c93472b385"},{"en":"a counteroffer","es":"una contraoferta","img":"u:photo-1565728744382-61accd4aa148","v":"m","au":"63f10f625e"},{"en":"meet halfway","es":"llegar a un punto medio","img":"u:photo-1491438590914-bc09fcaaf77a","v":"f","au":"3fcb4375dc"},{"en":"a deal-breaker","es":"un factor decisivo (para no aceptar)","img":"u:photo-1510680865842-cbda31c2ef99","v":"m","au":"b27beaf6b6"},{"en":"on one condition","es":"con una condición","img":"u:photo-1673745783023-aad274c5a1ec","v":"f","au":"3b19d347f7"},{"en":"a bulk discount","es":"un descuento por volumen","img":"u:photo-1684695749267-233af13276d0","v":"m","au":"3c798c56d1"},{"en":"upfront payment","es":"pago por adelantado","img":"u:photo-1654263937079-f63a3ea4d48b","v":"f","au":"2b85d07a47"},{"en":"I can't promise anything.","es":"No puedo prometer nada.","img":"u:photo-1728022037936-67f0617cba73","v":"m","au":"e6ea1c9219"},{"en":"sign off on it","es":"aprobarlo oficialmente","img":"u:photo-1619418602850-35ad20aa1700","v":"f","au":"5ef15f7d87"},{"en":"That works for me.","es":"Me parece bien.","img":"u:photo-1604488912264-dfed70450d76","v":"m","au":"c5d92238fe"}],"sentences":[{"en":"We'll lower the price as long as you pay upfront.","es":"Bajaremos el precio siempre y cuando pague por adelantado.","img":"u:photo-1654263937079-f63a3ea4d48b","v":"m","au":"97e42b1814"},{"en":"Provided that the samples arrive on time, we'll sign.","es":"Siempre que las muestras lleguen a tiempo, firmaremos.","img":"u:photo-1562564055-71e051d33c19","v":"f","au":"0067a92f74"},{"en":"Bring your laptop in case they ask for a demo.","es":"Trae tu portátil por si piden una demostración.","img":"u:photo-1525130413817-d45c1d127c42","v":"m","au":"ceff8aa3b8"},{"en":"We'll accept on one condition: free shipping.","es":"Aceptaremos con una condición: envío gratis.","img":"u:photo-1565728744382-61accd4aa148","v":"f","au":"7d891428dd"},{"en":"If you can't meet halfway, there's no deal.","es":"Si no puede llegar a un punto medio, no hay trato.","img":"u:photo-1510680865842-cbda31c2ef99","v":"m","au":"6dea665b24"},{"en":"I'll sign off on it only if legal approves.","es":"Lo aprobaré solo si el departamento legal lo aprueba.","img":"u:photo-1619418602850-35ad20aa1700","v":"f","au":"2580951da8"}],"fill":[{"s":"We'll offer free delivery ___ you order at least 200 units.","a":"as long as","o":["in case","unless"],"h":"siempre y cuando","full":"We'll offer free delivery as long as you order at least 200 units.","au":"42a617d607"},{"s":"Keep a copy of the invoice ___ there's a problem with the payment.","a":"in case","o":["as long as","provided"],"h":"por si acaso","full":"Keep a copy of the invoice in case there's a problem with the payment.","au":"0a74406ca6"},{"s":"___ that you sign today, the discount is yours.","a":"Provided","o":["In case","Unless"],"h":"con tal de que (formal)","full":"Provided that you sign today, the discount is yours.","au":"ebd5b8297f"},{"s":"We won't renew the contract ___ you improve the service.","a":"unless","o":["as long as","in case"],"h":"a menos que","full":"We won't renew the contract unless you improve the service.","au":"60136ff5b2"},{"s":"I'll accept the offer as long as the salary ___ competitive.","a":"is","o":["will be","would be"],"h":"presente después de as long as","full":"I'll accept the offer as long as the salary is competitive.","au":"99637aec18"},{"s":"Save the file to the cloud in case your laptop ___.","a":"crashes","o":["will crash","crashed"],"h":"presente después de in case","full":"Save the file to the cloud in case your laptop crashes.","au":"6774f1032a"}],"dialogue":{"title":"Closing the deal","es":"Cerrando el trato","img":"u:photo-1565728744382-61accd4aa148","lines":[{"who":"Rachel","v":"f","t":"Thanks for coming to Denver, Marcus. Let's talk numbers.","au":"17d568f58b"},{"who":"Marcus","v":"m","t":"Sure. We'd like 2,000 units, but your price is a bit high for us.","au":"1193ff72e5"},{"who":"Rachel","v":"f","t":"I understand. We can offer an eight percent discount as long as you pay thirty percent upfront.","au":"f2e8580ad7"},{"who":"Marcus","v":"m","t":"Upfront payment is a deal-breaker for us, I'm afraid. Could we meet halfway?","au":"a6fc081be2"},{"who":"Rachel","v":"f","t":"All right. Provided that you sign a two-year contract, we'll drop the upfront payment.","au":"3b8d322810"},{"who":"Marcus","v":"m","t":"That works for me. I'll ask our CFO to sign off on it tomorrow.","au":"7a642a47ae"},{"who":"Rachel","v":"f","t":"Great. I'll send you the draft tonight in case she has questions.","au":"6ad29217b0"},{"who":"Marcus","v":"m","t":"Perfect. If everything goes well, we'll place the first order next week.","au":"cff6d441ed"}],"q":[{"q":"Why isn't Marcus happy at first?","a":"The price is a bit high.","o":["The product is late.","Rachel is rude."]},{"q":"What does Rachel offer if they sign a two-year contract?","a":"No upfront payment.","o":["A free trip to Denver.","A bigger discount."]},{"q":"Why will Rachel send the draft tonight?","a":"In case the CFO has questions.","o":["Because the deal is canceled.","Because Marcus asked for a refund."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To negotiate and set conditions using as long as, provided that, only if and in case.","es":"Negociar y poner condiciones usando as long as, provided that, only if e in case."},"warm":[{"q":"Are you good at negotiating prices? Why or why not?","au":"631fa70094","es":"¿Eres bueno negociando precios? ¿Por qué sí o por qué no?","ex":"Not really. I usually accept the first price because I feel uncomfortable."},{"q":"What do you always carry with you just in case?","au":"8c0489528c","es":"¿Qué llevas siempre contigo por si acaso?","ex":"I always carry a charger in case my phone dies."}],"reading":{"title":"How to win a negotiation without making enemies","img":"u:photo-1565728744382-61accd4aa148","text":"Many people think negotiation is a battle with a winner and a loser. Experienced negotiators in New York and San Francisco see it differently: the best deals are the ones where both sides walk away happy. The first rule is to prepare a list of conditions before you sit down. Decide what is a deal-breaker for you and what is flexible. Then use conditional language to keep the conversation open. Instead of saying \"No,\" try \"We could accept that price as long as you cover shipping.\" Phrases such as \"provided that\" and \"only if\" show that you are willing to move, but not for free. The second rule is to always bring a plan B in case the other side says no. If you have alternatives, you'll feel more confident and less desperate. Finally, never accept the first offer. Make a counteroffer, even a small one, and be ready to meet halfway. If you listen more than you talk, you'll discover what the other person really needs. Remember: a good deal today is great, but a good relationship will bring you many deals tomorrow.","au":"b0ce5bd735","q":[{"s":"Experienced negotiators believe one side must always lose.","a":"no"},{"s":"You should decide on your deal-breakers before the meeting.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The text suggests saying a direct \"No\" to keep things simple.","a":"no"},{"s":"Having a plan B helps you feel more confident.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The text recommends accepting the first offer quickly.","a":"no"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Under what conditions would you accept a job in another city?","a":"I'd accept it as long as the company paid for the move.","es":"¿Bajo qué condiciones aceptarías un trabajo en otra ciudad?","qau":"ebbc330f57","aau":"72e81b9b4b"},{"q":"What do you pack in case your flight is delayed?","a":"I pack a charger and a snack in case my flight is delayed.","es":"¿Qué empacas por si se retrasa tu vuelo?","qau":"fd78418f5e","aau":"79fdb77be4"},{"q":"What is a deal-breaker for you when you rent an apartment?","a":"A deal-breaker for me is not having a parking space.","es":"¿Qué es algo inaceptable para ti cuando alquilas un apartamento?","qau":"8056d9722f","aau":"ff8312efda"},{"q":"How would you ask a supplier for a discount?","a":"We'll order 1,000 units provided that you give us a ten percent discount.","es":"¿Cómo le pedirías un descuento a un proveedor?","qau":"960094a332","aau":"6be1c59f34"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe un correo corto (5–6 oraciones) a un proveedor proponiendo condiciones para un trato. Usa as long as, provided that, in case y only if.","kw":["as long as","provided","in case","only if"],"n":5,"model":"Dear Mr. Lee, thank you for your offer. We will order 800 units as long as the price stays at $12 per unit. Provided that you deliver by May 10, we can sign the contract this week. We will pay 20 percent upfront only if you include free shipping. I'm attaching our previous invoice in case you need it. Best regards, Ana."}}]},{"n":2,"title":"Second Conditionals","es":"Segundo condicional","cover":"u:photo-1658279366796-e0c28623cd27","parts":[{"id":"t2p1","topic":2,"part":1,"title":"Hypothetical worlds","es":"Mundos hipotéticos","acts":["learn","sc1ParallelPortal","listenChoose","fill","typeSentence","speak"],"tip":"<p>El <b>segundo condicional</b> habla de situaciones <b>imaginarias, improbables o contrarias a la realidad</b> en el presente o el futuro.</p>\n<p>📐 <b>If + pasado simple, would / could / might + verbo</b><br><i>If I <b>won</b> the lottery, I<b>'d travel</b> the world.</i> (no espero ganarla)</p>\n<p>⚠️ El pasado aquí <b>NO</b> habla del pasado: es \"distancia de la realidad\". <i>If I <b>had</b> a car</i> = no tengo carro ahora.</p>\n<p>🎩 Con <b>be</b>, el inglés cuidado usa <b>were</b> para todas las personas: <i>If she <b>were</b> here…</i> (<i>was</i> es aceptable en conversación).</p>\n<p>🎲 <b>would</b> = resultado seguro · <b>could</b> = habilidad/posibilidad · <b>might</b> = quizás.</p>\n<p>Compara: <i>If I <b>get</b> the job, I'll move</i> (probable) vs. <i>If I <b>got</b> the job, I'd move</i> (lo veo difícil).</p>","tips":["<b>I'd</b> puede ser <i>I would</i> o <i>I had</i>: en el resultado del 2.º condicional siempre es <i>I would</i>.","Nunca pongas <b>would</b> en la parte del <i>if</i>: ❌ <i>If I would have time</i> → ✅ <i>If I had time</i>.","<b>I'd rather</b> + verbo base: <i>I'd rather work from home</i> (preferiría trabajar desde casa)."],"vocab":[{"en":"win the lottery","es":"ganarse la lotería","img":"u:photo-1713610480144-b7fbc9d9069a","v":"m","au":"25f70a7b75"},{"en":"quit my job","es":"renunciar a mi trabajo","img":"u:photo-1758691737424-b0cdcfce9f66","v":"f","au":"a8ce39bcb5"},{"en":"be my own boss","es":"ser mi propio jefe","img":"u:photo-1762652847007-c01a72f401ad","v":"m","au":"674ece5aeb"},{"en":"move abroad","es":"mudarse al extranjero","img":"u:photo-1758523670991-ee93bc48d81d","v":"f","au":"6da34c045a"},{"en":"travel the world","es":"viajar por el mundo","img":"u:photo-1516738901171-8eb4fc13bd20","v":"f","au":"36042c3423"},{"en":"take a gap year","es":"tomarse un año sabático","img":"u:photo-1501555088652-021faa106b9b","v":"m","au":"3d399d421f"},{"en":"afford","es":"permitirse (económicamente)","img":"u:photo-1518458028785-8fbcd101ebb9","v":"f","au":"3acd0fe01f"},{"en":"a dream come true","es":"un sueño hecho realidad","img":"u:photo-1680538220086-bd896a55ff64","v":"m","au":"bd41ed7792"},{"en":"in an ideal world","es":"en un mundo ideal","img":"u:photo-1533757879476-8f4a3cb1ae4b","v":"f","au":"8c62420858"},{"en":"I'd rather","es":"preferiría","img":"u:photo-1654440059496-133b3c97c823","v":"m","au":"91bdc8eda8"},{"en":"What would you do if…?","es":"¿Qué harías si…?","img":"#What would you do if…?","v":"f","au":"432fdea000"},{"en":"It would make a huge difference.","es":"Haría una gran diferencia.","img":"u:photo-1758691737138-7b9b1884b1db","v":"m","au":"f014ee8008"}],"sentences":[{"en":"If I won the lottery, I'd quit my job.","es":"Si me ganara la lotería, renunciaría a mi trabajo.","img":"u:photo-1713610480144-b7fbc9d9069a","v":"m","au":"28359f42f3"},{"en":"If I had more time, I'd learn to play the piano.","es":"Si tuviera más tiempo, aprendería a tocar el piano.","img":"u:photo-1470019693664-1d202d2c0907","v":"f","au":"89e1502349"},{"en":"If she were my boss, she'd let us work from home.","es":"Si ella fuera mi jefa, nos dejaría trabajar desde casa.","img":"u:photo-1604933762021-54a5858c9832","v":"f","au":"c22dd60265"},{"en":"We could travel the world if we didn't have a mortgage.","es":"Podríamos viajar por el mundo si no tuviéramos una hipoteca.","img":"u:photo-1516738901171-8eb4fc13bd20","v":"m","au":"974227cd89"},{"en":"If I lived in Seattle, I might buy a kayak.","es":"Si viviera en Seattle, quizás compraría un kayak.","img":"u:photo-1592770109272-8489716bbb52","v":"m","au":"c2f3c8eb4d"},{"en":"What would you do if you could be your own boss?","es":"¿Qué harías si pudieras ser tu propio jefe?","img":"u:photo-1762652847007-c01a72f401ad","v":"f","au":"3f4496bc96"}],"fill":[{"s":"If I ___ a million dollars, I'd buy a cabin in Montana.","a":"had","o":["have","would have"],"h":"if + pasado simple","full":"If I had a million dollars, I'd buy a cabin in Montana.","au":"758172b0e9"},{"s":"If he ___ more organized, he'd get promoted.","a":"were","o":["is","would be"],"h":"were para todas las personas","full":"If he were more organized, he'd get promoted.","au":"0494c13730"},{"s":"I ___ move to Miami if my family lived there.","a":"would","o":["will","did"],"h":"resultado imaginario","full":"I would move to Miami if my family lived there.","au":"9ec7aafe4a"},{"s":"If we didn't have kids, we ___ take a gap year.","a":"could","o":["can","will"],"h":"posibilidad (podríamos)","full":"If we didn't have kids, we could take a gap year.","au":"6bd69035bf"},{"s":"If you ___ live anywhere, where would you live?","a":"could","o":["can","would"],"h":"pudieras","full":"If you could live anywhere, where would you live?","au":"dc9ead12c9"},{"s":"She'd be a great manager if she ___ to people more.","a":"listened","o":["listens","would listen"],"h":"pasado en la condición","full":"She'd be a great manager if she listened to people more.","au":"e61bce2bba"}],"goal":{"en":"To imagine hypothetical situations in the present and future with the second conditional.","es":"Imaginar situaciones hipotéticas en el presente y el futuro con el segundo condicional."},"warm":[{"q":"If you could live in any city in the world, where would you live?","au":"0f2c322ab4","es":"Si pudieras vivir en cualquier ciudad del mundo, ¿dónde vivirías?","ex":"If I could live anywhere, I'd live in Vancouver."},{"q":"What would you buy first if you won the lottery?","au":"71617b46ca","es":"¿Qué comprarías primero si te ganaras la lotería?","ex":"I'd buy a house for my parents."}],"reading":{"title":"If money weren't a problem","img":"u:photo-1658279366796-e0c28623cd27","text":"A popular podcast in Los Angeles recently asked its listeners one simple question: \"What would you do if money weren't a problem?\" Thousands of people answered, and the results were surprising. Very few said they would buy a mansion or a sports car. Most people said they would spend more time with their families or travel the world. A nurse from Phoenix wrote, \"If I didn't need the salary, I would still work at the hospital, but only three days a week. I'd use the rest of the time to learn to paint.\" A software engineer from Atlanta said he would take a gap year and volunteer in national parks. \"If I were my own boss, I'd give everyone Fridays off,\" another listener joked. Psychologists say this question is useful because it reveals our real priorities. If your answer is very different from your current life, it might be a sign that you need to make some changes. Of course, in an ideal world, we could all quit our jobs tomorrow. But even small steps, like taking one weekend a month for a hobby, could make a huge difference.","au":"5e5ec26a1f","q":[{"s":"Most listeners said they would buy a mansion.","a":"no"},{"s":"The nurse would stop working completely.","a":"no"},{"s":"The software engineer would volunteer in national parks.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Psychologists think the question shows our real priorities.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The text says small changes can't help.","a":"no"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"What would you do if you didn't have to work?","a":"If I didn't have to work, I'd travel and learn to cook.","es":"¿Qué harías si no tuvieras que trabajar?","qau":"1dff5a40e7","aau":"0140f15950"},{"q":"If you could change one thing about your city, what would it be?","a":"If I could change one thing, I'd improve public transportation.","es":"Si pudieras cambiar una cosa de tu ciudad, ¿qué sería?","qau":"ccf0d36845","aau":"34cd1e14f2"},{"q":"Where would you live if you moved abroad?","a":"If I moved abroad, I'd live in Vancouver.","es":"¿Dónde vivirías si te mudaras al extranjero?","qau":"148a070db4","aau":"34bb773b9d"},{"q":"What would you do if you were the president of your company?","a":"If I were the president, I'd give everyone more vacation days.","es":"¿Qué harías si fueras el presidente de tu empresa?","qau":"fc39d8fde3","aau":"a038b96ce6"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe un párrafo (5 oraciones) sobre tu vida ideal: ¿qué harías si no tuvieras límites de dinero ni de tiempo? Usa would, could y might.","kw":["would","could","might","if"],"n":5,"model":"If money weren't a problem, I would live near the beach in San Diego. I would work only four days a week. If I had more free time, I could learn to surf. I might open a small coffee shop if I found a good place. In an ideal world, I'd travel twice a year with my family."}},{"id":"t2p2","topic":2,"part":2,"title":"If I were you: advice & dilemmas","es":"Si yo fuera tú: consejos y dilemas","acts":["learn","sc2AdviceColumn","dialogue","spinWheel","unscramble","speak"],"tip":"<p>🗣️ Para dar consejos con el segundo condicional:<br><b>If I were you, I'd …</b> / <b>If I were in your shoes, I wouldn't …</b><br><i>If I were you, I'd <b>turn down</b> the offer.</i></p>\n<p>🤔 Para plantear dilemas: <b>What would you do if …?</b><br><i>What would you do if you found a wallet with $500 in it?</i> → <i>I'd return it, of course.</i></p>\n<p>🔁 <b>unless</b> también funciona aquí: <i>I wouldn't take the job <b>unless</b> they paid for the move.</i></p>\n<p>💬 Respuestas cortas: <i>Would you accept? — Yes, I <b>would</b>. / No, I <b>wouldn't</b>.</i></p>\n<p>Siempre <b>If I were you</b> (no <i>If I was you</i>) en contextos formales: es la expresión fija.</p>","tips":["<b>If I were you</b> suena casi como una sola palabra: <i>ifaiuéryu</i>.","Puedes omitir la parte del <i>if</i> cuando es obvia: <i>I'd talk to HR</i> = (If I were you,) I'd talk to HR.","<b>wouldn't</b> se pronuncia <i>wúdent</i>; la <b>l</b> no suena."],"vocab":[{"en":"If I were in your shoes","es":"si yo estuviera en tu lugar","img":"u:photo-1483721310020-03333e577078","v":"m","au":"850cd9bb9b"},{"en":"I'd think twice.","es":"Lo pensaría dos veces.","img":"u:photo-1604780403125-e1cefdc0089a","v":"f","au":"127e488331"},{"en":"weigh the pros and cons","es":"sopesar los pros y los contras","img":"u:photo-1488190211105-8b0e65b80b4e","v":"f","au":"27e28cf1dc"},{"en":"turn down an offer","es":"rechazar una oferta","img":"u:photo-1510680865842-cbda31c2ef99","v":"m","au":"eb2bc4f195"},{"en":"speak up","es":"hablar claro / dar tu opinión","img":"u:photo-1551836022-d5d88e9218df","v":"f","au":"3ca3e303b5"},{"en":"a tough call","es":"una decisión difícil","img":"u:photo-1659355889750-8b0708f4ac8d","v":"m","au":"14717cd70a"},{"en":"I wouldn't dream of it.","es":"Ni se me ocurriría.","img":"u:photo-1639986169769-feb3c3a92346","v":"f","au":"1aaf3f655b"},{"en":"return the wallet","es":"devolver la billetera","img":"u:photo-1789927485132-f710ce7fe3ba","v":"m","au":"c757aeb43a"},{"en":"give it a shot","es":"intentarlo","img":"u:photo-1728637690621-ad046564a657","v":"f","au":"953df0db93"},{"en":"cross the line","es":"pasarse de la raya","img":"u:photo-1727109795068-9c3eeed3c98f","v":"m","au":"c843e12297"},{"en":"take the plunge","es":"lanzarse (decidirse)","img":"u:photo-1664735094204-70b90f93dc33","v":"f","au":"3ce10bb568"},{"en":"otherwise","es":"de lo contrario","img":"#otherwise = si no","v":"m","au":"1b6e5f7f0d"}],"sentences":[{"en":"If I were you, I'd talk to HR first.","es":"Si yo fuera tú, hablaría primero con Recursos Humanos.","img":"u:photo-1573495804664-b1c0849525af","v":"f","au":"ea893be705"},{"en":"I wouldn't take the job unless they paid more.","es":"No aceptaría el trabajo a menos que pagaran más.","img":"u:photo-1510680865842-cbda31c2ef99","v":"m","au":"e144404c2a"},{"en":"What would you do if you found a wallet?","es":"¿Qué harías si encontraras una billetera?","img":"u:photo-1789927485132-f710ce7fe3ba","v":"f","au":"e733ff1c4a"},{"en":"If I were in your shoes, I'd speak up.","es":"Si estuviera en tu lugar, daría mi opinión.","img":"u:photo-1551836022-d5d88e9218df","v":"m","au":"eaf2f1c17a"},{"en":"I'd give it a shot if I were younger.","es":"Lo intentaría si fuera más joven.","img":"u:photo-1728637690621-ad046564a657","v":"f","au":"bc9cc5394e"},{"en":"Would you move to Austin for a better salary?","es":"¿Te mudarías a Austin por un mejor salario?","img":"u:photo-1588993608283-7f0eda4438be","v":"m","au":"10e6db5704"}],"fill":[{"s":"If I ___ you, I'd ask for a raise.","a":"were","o":["am","would be"],"h":"expresión fija para aconsejar","full":"If I were you, I'd ask for a raise.","au":"c6fa87cf43"},{"s":"I ___ accept that offer. The salary is too low.","a":"wouldn't","o":["won't","didn't"],"h":"consejo negativo","full":"I wouldn't accept that offer. The salary is too low.","au":"269ff568ac"},{"s":"What would you do if your boss ___ you to lie?","a":"asked","o":["asks","would ask"],"h":"pasado en la condición","full":"What would you do if your boss asked you to lie?","au":"239cb1f096"},{"s":"If I were in your shoes, I ___ weigh the pros and cons.","a":"would","o":["will","did"],"h":"would + verbo","full":"If I were in your shoes, I would weigh the pros and cons.","au":"45f68e124f"},{"s":"I wouldn't sign it ___ a lawyer read it first.","a":"unless","o":["if","as long as"],"h":"a menos que","full":"I wouldn't sign it unless a lawyer read it first.","au":"1aee695b9e"}],"dialogue":{"title":"A tough call","es":"Una decisión difícil","img":"u:photo-1653762381632-2945469edb7b","lines":[{"who":"Sofia","v":"f","t":"I need some advice. A startup in Seattle offered me a job.","au":"53cacfddf5"},{"who":"Daniel","v":"m","t":"That's great news! So what's the problem?","au":"bff8103b4c"},{"who":"Sofia","v":"f","t":"The salary is amazing, but I'd have to move across the country.","au":"9eace10be8"},{"who":"Daniel","v":"m","t":"If I were you, I'd weigh the pros and cons carefully.","au":"85c0221bea"},{"who":"Sofia","v":"f","t":"I know. If my parents didn't live here, I'd say yes right away.","au":"32d436d15d"},{"who":"Daniel","v":"m","t":"Would they pay for the move? I wouldn't go unless they covered it.","au":"f3bc1aa08c"},{"who":"Sofia","v":"f","t":"They would. And I could work remotely two days a week.","au":"4e3e27a039"},{"who":"Daniel","v":"m","t":"Then if I were in your shoes, I'd take the plunge. You can always come back.","au":"e12a39ecf2"}],"q":[{"q":"Where is the job?","a":"In Seattle.","o":["In Austin.","In Miami."]},{"q":"Why is Sofia hesitating?","a":"Her parents live near her now.","o":["The salary is low.","She hates startups."]},{"q":"What would Daniel do?","a":"He'd take the job.","o":["He'd turn it down.","He'd ask for a raise."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To give advice and discuss moral dilemmas with if I were you and what would you do if.","es":"Dar consejos y discutir dilemas morales con if I were you y what would you do if."},"warm":[{"q":"Who do you usually ask for advice? Why?","au":"4df50e6b51","es":"¿A quién le pides consejo normalmente? ¿Por qué?","ex":"I usually ask my sister because she's very honest."},{"q":"What would you do if you found $100 on the street?","au":"0c7340c58d","es":"¿Qué harías si encontraras 100 dólares en la calle?","ex":"I'd try to find the owner. If I couldn't, I'd donate it."}],"reading":{"title":"Dear Dana: should I take the job?","img":"u:photo-1676906242973-739577556387","text":"Dear Dana, I'm 34 and I've worked at the same insurance company in Dallas for nine years. Last week a startup in Denver offered me a job with a 30% higher salary. The problem is that my wife has a great job here, and our kids love their school. What would you do if you were me? — Torn in Texas. Dear Torn, this is a tough call, and there's no perfect answer. If I were in your shoes, I wouldn't make the decision alone. Sit down with your wife and weigh the pros and cons together. Ask yourselves: would you still want to move if the salary were the same? If the answer is yes, the job is probably about growth, not money, and that's a good sign. If the answer is no, I'd think twice. Startups can be exciting, but they can also close suddenly. Before you turn down the offer, though, ask if they would let you work remotely for a few months. Many companies would agree. Otherwise, you might regret not trying. Whatever you decide, don't burn bridges with your current employer. Good luck! — Dana","au":"0fcb510193","q":[{"s":"Torn has worked at his company for nine years.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The startup is in Dallas.","a":"no"},{"s":"Dana says he should decide alone.","a":"no"},{"s":"Dana suggests asking about working remotely.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Dana thinks startups are always a safe option.","a":"no"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"What would you do if a coworker took credit for your work?","a":"If a coworker took credit for my work, I'd speak up politely.","es":"¿Qué harías si un compañero se atribuyera el mérito de tu trabajo?","qau":"b07aac1ba0","aau":"10e062c914"},{"q":"If your best friend asked you to lie for him, would you do it?","a":"No, I wouldn't. I'd tell him to tell the truth.","es":"Si tu mejor amigo te pidiera mentir por él, ¿lo harías?","qau":"5bed0a05d7","aau":"57b603f746"},{"q":"What advice would you give to someone who hates their job?","a":"If I were them, I'd start looking for a new job.","es":"¿Qué consejo le darías a alguien que odia su trabajo?","qau":"65dca410b9","aau":"6a6e5f4bc0"},{"q":"Would you ever move to another country for love?","a":"Yes, I would, as long as I could work there.","es":"¿Alguna vez te mudarías a otro país por amor?","qau":"1cb277dc25","aau":"b5dce975e5"}],"hw":{"es":"Responde la carta de un lector con un problema (inventa el problema). Escribe 5–6 oraciones de consejo usando If I were you, I'd…, I wouldn't… unless… y What would you do if…?","kw":["If I were you","would","wouldn't","unless"],"n":5,"model":"Dear Carlos, if I were you, I'd talk to your manager this week. I wouldn't quit unless you had another offer. If I were in your shoes, I'd update my résumé too. What would you do if they offered you a raise? I think I'd stay for one more year. Good luck!"}}]},{"n":3,"title":"Third Conditionals","es":"Tercer condicional","cover":"u:photo-1582114803437-a8fef1de0f74","parts":[{"id":"t3p1","topic":3,"part":1,"title":"Past regrets & what could have been","es":"Lamentos del pasado y lo que pudo haber sido","acts":["learn","tc1TimeRewind","fill","memory","typeSentence","speak"],"tip":"<p>El <b>tercer condicional</b> imagina un <b>pasado diferente</b>: algo que NO pasó y su resultado imaginario.</p>\n<p>📐 <b>If + had + participio, would have + participio</b><br><i>If I <b>hadn't overslept</b>, I <b>would have caught</b> the flight.</i><br>(Realidad: me quedé dormido y perdí el vuelo.)</p>\n<p>🎲 Cambia el modal según la certeza: <b>would have</b> (seguro) · <b>could have</b> (habría podido) · <b>might have</b> (quizás habría).</p>\n<p>💭 <b>If only + had + participio</b> expresa un lamento fuerte: <i>If only I <b>had listened</b> to you!</i></p>\n<p>🗣️ En el habla rápida: <i>would have</i> → <b>would've</b> (<i>wúdov</i>), <i>hadn't</i> → <i>jádent</i>.</p>","tips":["Nunca escribas <i>would of</i>: suena igual que <b>would've</b>, pero es un error.","<b>I'd</b> en la parte del if = <b>I had</b>: <i>If <b>I'd</b> known</i> = If I had known.","Muchos nativos dicen <i>If I would have known</i>, pero en inglés correcto es <b>If I had known</b>."],"vocab":[{"en":"miss the flight","es":"perder el vuelo","img":"u:photo-1769745280792-c9c16b553af0","v":"m","au":"48b1dd1aae"},{"en":"oversleep","es":"quedarse dormido","img":"u:photo-1721815714586-73849a2a163b","v":"f","au":"b78567be9b"},{"en":"a close call","es":"algo que casi pasa","img":"u:photo-1687867451910-28941a460f35","v":"m","au":"6f1fc6ed7c"},{"en":"if only","es":"ojalá / si tan solo","img":"u:photo-1642511241125-f0f8f4914907","v":"f","au":"1f25866bf9"},{"en":"in hindsight","es":"en retrospectiva","img":"u:photo-1638486071992-536e48c8fa3e","v":"m","au":"cfb3c9fe46"},{"en":"take the wrong exit","es":"tomar la salida equivocada","img":"u:photo-1667999608784-297b3e813082","v":"f","au":"9d02108c26"},{"en":"pass up a chance","es":"dejar pasar una oportunidad","img":"u:photo-1639494093509-4b09e2279d1a","v":"m","au":"407050ac7c"},{"en":"it would have been","es":"habría sido","img":"#it would have been","v":"f","au":"ddfdedde38"},{"en":"turn out","es":"resultar","img":"u:photo-1512911325838-de9e0bc5d464","v":"f","au":"3962701cce"},{"en":"end up","es":"terminar (en / haciendo)","img":"u:photo-1504697570352-47c3bbc09af9","v":"m","au":"d61a1b0e40"},{"en":"What if…?","es":"¿Y si…?","img":"u:photo-1606595898127-a06c52b4e2b3","v":"f","au":"f367888c6a"},{"en":"make it on time","es":"llegar a tiempo","img":"u:photo-1495704907664-81f74a7efd9b","v":"m","au":"a1fd950b06"}],"sentences":[{"en":"If I hadn't overslept, I would have caught the flight.","es":"Si no me hubiera quedado dormido, habría alcanzado el vuelo.","img":"u:photo-1721815714586-73849a2a163b","v":"m","au":"3b2f0c1bba"},{"en":"If we had taken the right exit, we'd have arrived on time.","es":"Si hubiéramos tomado la salida correcta, habríamos llegado a tiempo.","img":"u:photo-1667999608784-297b3e813082","v":"f","au":"449a6e0280"},{"en":"She might have gotten the job if she'd applied earlier.","es":"Quizás habría conseguido el trabajo si se hubiera postulado antes.","img":"u:photo-1672380135241-c024f7fbfa13","v":"f","au":"9fb2e6ae8b"},{"en":"If only I had listened to my mom!","es":"¡Si tan solo hubiera escuchado a mi mamá!","img":"u:photo-1642511241125-f0f8f4914907","v":"m","au":"add0252ebe"},{"en":"It would have been a disaster if you hadn't called.","es":"Habría sido un desastre si no hubieras llamado.","img":"u:photo-1713256452479-5a20056c0340","v":"f","au":"8027fcec45"},{"en":"In hindsight, we could have saved a lot of money.","es":"En retrospectiva, habríamos podido ahorrar mucho dinero.","img":"u:photo-1638486071992-536e48c8fa3e","v":"m","au":"d9c306d52e"}],"fill":[{"s":"If I ___ the alarm, I wouldn't have overslept.","a":"had set","o":["set","would set"],"h":"had + participio","full":"If I had set the alarm, I wouldn't have overslept.","au":"8a4229736e"},{"s":"If they had left earlier, they ___ the traffic.","a":"would have avoided","o":["would avoid","had avoided"],"h":"would have + participio","full":"If they had left earlier, they would have avoided the traffic.","au":"529fc5146d"},{"s":"She ___ the job if she had prepared better.","a":"might have gotten","o":["might get","had gotten"],"h":"quizás habría","full":"She might have gotten the job if she had prepared better.","au":"56103c9fce"},{"s":"If only I ___ to you!","a":"had listened","o":["listened","would listen"],"h":"lamento del pasado","full":"If only I had listened to you!","au":"e6e6995680"},{"s":"We could have won if our goalkeeper ___ injured.","a":"hadn't been","o":["wasn't","wouldn't be"],"h":"negativo en pasado perfecto","full":"We could have won if our goalkeeper hadn't been injured.","au":"92b3133874"},{"s":"If you'd told me earlier, I ___ helped you.","a":"could have","o":["can have","could"],"h":"habría podido","full":"If you'd told me earlier, I could have helped you.","au":"b53a7dd732"}],"goal":{"en":"To talk about past regrets and imaginary past results with the third conditional.","es":"Hablar de lamentos y resultados imaginarios del pasado con el tercer condicional."},"warm":[{"q":"Have you ever missed a flight, a bus or an important event?","au":"896821af86","es":"¿Alguna vez has perdido un vuelo, un bus o un evento importante?","ex":"Yes, I once missed a flight to Miami because of traffic."},{"q":"Is there a decision in your past you would change?","au":"0e4885db6d","es":"¿Hay alguna decisión de tu pasado que cambiarías?","ex":"Yes, I would have studied English much earlier."}],"reading":{"title":"The wedding we almost missed","img":"u:photo-1769745280792-c9c16b553af0","text":"Two years ago my best friend Jason got married in Savannah, Georgia, and I was the best man. The night before my flight from New York, I stayed up late finishing a project, and I forgot to set my alarm. If I hadn't worked so late, I wouldn't have overslept. I woke up at 7:15, and my flight was at 8:00. I took a taxi, but the driver took the wrong exit and we got stuck in traffic. By the time I got to the gate, the doors were closed. I was devastated. If only I had left the night before, like Jason had suggested! Fortunately, the airline agent was incredibly kind. She found me a seat on a flight to Atlanta, and from there I rented a car and drove four hours. I arrived at the church ten minutes before the ceremony, still wearing jeans. Jason laughed and gave me his spare suit. In hindsight, it turned out to be a great story. If I had arrived on time, nobody would have remembered my speech. Instead, everyone still talks about the best man who almost missed the wedding.","au":"5c5cf936ed","q":[{"s":"The writer forgot to set his alarm.","a":"yes"},{"s":"His flight was from Savannah to New York.","a":"no"},{"s":"The taxi driver took the wrong exit.","a":"yes"},{"s":"He flew directly to Savannah on the next flight.","a":"no"},{"s":"He arrived at the church wearing jeans.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"What would have happened if you hadn't studied English?","a":"If I hadn't studied English, I wouldn't have gotten my current job.","es":"¿Qué habría pasado si no hubieras estudiado inglés?","qau":"c7fa4dcc9b","aau":"d69c7e0fa8"},{"q":"What is something you should have done differently last year?","a":"I should have saved more money last year.","es":"¿Qué es algo que debiste haber hecho diferente el año pasado?","qau":"9ec33b9453","aau":"2bd1207aca"},{"q":"If you had been born in another country, where would you have grown up?","a":"If I had been born in Canada, I would have grown up in Toronto.","es":"Si hubieras nacido en otro país, ¿dónde habrías crecido?","qau":"911ca434e2","aau":"ce7ee31784"},{"q":"What would you have studied if you hadn't chosen your career?","a":"If I hadn't chosen engineering, I would have studied music.","es":"¿Qué habrías estudiado si no hubieras elegido tu carrera?","qau":"c087c4d6e0","aau":"c372c53760"}],"hw":{"es":"Cuenta una pequeña historia (5–6 oraciones) de algo que salió mal en tu vida y escribe al menos 3 oraciones en tercer condicional sobre lo que habría pasado.","kw":["If I had","would have","If only"],"n":5,"model":"Last year I lost an important client. If I had answered his email sooner, he wouldn't have looked for another company. If only I had checked my inbox that weekend! If my assistant hadn't been on vacation, she could have helped me. In hindsight, it was a good lesson. Now I always reply within 24 hours."}},{"id":"t3p2","topic":3,"part":2,"title":"Should have & mixed conditionals","es":"Should have y condicionales mixtos","acts":["learn","tc2StartupPostmortem","dialogue","sort","raceGame","speak"],"tip":"<p>😬 <b>should have / shouldn't have + participio</b> = crítica o arrepentimiento sobre el pasado:<br><i>I <b>should have backed up</b> my files.</i> (no lo hice 😩) · <i>You <b>shouldn't have said</b> that.</i> (lo dijiste)</p>\n<p>🔀 <b>Condicionales mixtos</b> combinan tiempos:</p>\n<p>1️⃣ <b>Pasado → presente</b>: <b>If + had + participio, would + verbo</b><br><i>If I <b>had taken</b> that job in Boston, I <b>would be</b> rich now.</i></p>\n<p>2️⃣ <b>Presente → pasado</b>: <b>If + pasado simple, would have + participio</b><br><i>If I <b>spoke</b> Japanese, I <b>would have understood</b> the meeting yesterday.</i></p>\n<p>🔎 Pista: busca palabras como <b>now, today, still</b> (resultado presente) o <b>yesterday, last year</b> (resultado pasado).</p>","tips":["<b>should have</b> en la conversación suena <i>shúdov</i>: <i>I should've known!</i>","<b>must have</b> = deducción (seguramente), <b>should have</b> = lo correcto que no se hizo. No los confundas.","En los mixtos, el resultado presente casi siempre lleva <b>now</b>: <i>…I would be in Paris <b>now</b>.</i>"],"vocab":[{"en":"should have known","es":"debí haberlo sabido","img":"u:photo-1618498390344-445c804f2ac5","v":"m","au":"7ba69232f3"},{"en":"shouldn't have said that","es":"no debí haber dicho eso","img":"u:photo-1758600588830-1bbcc78d3500","v":"f","au":"d1a71a1967"},{"en":"learn the hard way","es":"aprender a las malas","img":"u:photo-1768401658109-a4dc907f2734","v":"m","au":"c2f4bfec6d"},{"en":"jump to conclusions","es":"sacar conclusiones apresuradas","img":"u:photo-1581182830442-e8bc7babbf15","v":"f","au":"9a7dc2037c"},{"en":"blow it","es":"echarlo a perder","img":"u:photo-1726649339367-c2577a28881b","v":"m","au":"3aa75405b8"},{"en":"burn bridges","es":"quemar los puentes","img":"u:photo-1685630549021-1f8922260c91","v":"f","au":"eb67b2d908"},{"en":"second-guess","es":"dudar de (una decisión)","img":"u:photo-1604364721460-0cbc5866219d","v":"f","au":"a53beee894"},{"en":"a wake-up call","es":"una llamada de atención","img":"u:photo-1541480601022-2308c0f02487","v":"m","au":"1f7400538e"},{"en":"lesson learned","es":"lección aprendida","img":"u:photo-1647559709189-a257be60e147","v":"f","au":"6b781f6d34"},{"en":"hire","es":"contratar","img":"u:photo-1672380135241-c024f7fbfa13","v":"m","au":"8901a4f030"},{"en":"cut corners","es":"hacer las cosas a la ligera","img":"u:photo-1583521214690-73421a1829a9","v":"f","au":"4cd34f2b1a"},{"en":"No use crying over spilled milk.","es":"No sirve de nada llorar sobre la leche derramada.","img":"u:photo-1567011345445-fd175f248019","v":"m","au":"fe8ba5aec4"}],"sentences":[{"en":"I should have backed up my files.","es":"Debí haber hecho una copia de mis archivos.","img":"u:photo-1726649339367-c2577a28881b","v":"m","au":"9440024c59"},{"en":"You shouldn't have jumped to conclusions.","es":"No debiste sacar conclusiones apresuradas.","img":"u:photo-1581182830442-e8bc7babbf15","v":"f","au":"258985bb97"},{"en":"If I had taken that job, I would be in Boston now.","es":"Si hubiera aceptado ese trabajo, ahora estaría en Boston.","img":"u:photo-1565127803082-69dd82351360","v":"m","au":"7d738ef135"},{"en":"If she weren't so shy, she would have spoken up.","es":"Si no fuera tan tímida, habría dado su opinión.","img":"u:photo-1506863530036-1efeddceb993","v":"f","au":"ecb70e4453"},{"en":"We shouldn't have cut corners on the launch.","es":"No debimos hacer el lanzamiento a la ligera.","img":"u:photo-1521737604893-d14cc237f11d","v":"m","au":"243f76fab3"},{"en":"If we had hired a designer, our app would look better today.","es":"Si hubiéramos contratado un diseñador, nuestra app se vería mejor hoy.","img":"u:photo-1572044162444-ad60f128bdea","v":"f","au":"9ae9adc10d"}],"sort":{"cats":["Third conditional","Mixed conditional","Should have"],"items":[{"w":"If I had studied, I would have passed.","c":"Third conditional","au":"6294c72e8f"},{"w":"If we'd left earlier, we wouldn't have missed it.","c":"Third conditional","au":"c6ccf7273b"},{"w":"She'd have called if she had known.","c":"Third conditional","au":"4e4214cd3f"},{"w":"If I had saved money, I would be rich now.","c":"Mixed conditional","au":"5b237963d0"},{"w":"If he weren't so lazy, he would have finished.","c":"Mixed conditional","au":"33e1b35ee3"},{"w":"If I'd moved to LA, I'd be an actor today.","c":"Mixed conditional","au":"1d56150087"},{"w":"I should have listened to you.","c":"Should have","au":"f07038eec2"},{"w":"You shouldn't have lied.","c":"Should have","au":"3c9fcb5f38"},{"w":"We should've hired more people.","c":"Should have","au":"cc8f5ac2c7"}]},"dialogue":{"title":"The launch that failed","es":"El lanzamiento que fracasó","img":"u:photo-1521737604893-d14cc237f11d","lines":[{"who":"Kevin","v":"m","t":"Well, the numbers are in. Only three hundred downloads in the first month.","au":"6dbec8caa2"},{"who":"Laura","v":"f","t":"I know. In hindsight, we shouldn't have launched before the holidays.","au":"c38662f6f1"},{"who":"Kevin","v":"m","t":"Agreed. And we should have tested the app with real users first.","au":"3596f80965"},{"who":"Laura","v":"f","t":"If we had listened to the beta testers, we would have fixed the login bug.","au":"893db6f05e"},{"who":"Kevin","v":"m","t":"True. And if we had hired a marketing person, people would know about us now.","au":"54968eccec"},{"who":"Laura","v":"f","t":"Let's not second-guess everything. It was a wake-up call, not the end.","au":"e09229213d"},{"who":"Kevin","v":"m","t":"You're right. Lesson learned. We won't cut corners next time.","au":"dd274cba61"},{"who":"Laura","v":"f","t":"Exactly. No use crying over spilled milk. Let's fix it and relaunch in March.","au":"5af5b967b9"}],"q":[{"q":"How many downloads did they get?","a":"Only three hundred.","o":["Three thousand.","Thirty thousand."]},{"q":"What should they have done first?","a":"Test the app with real users.","o":["Hire a lawyer.","Launch before the holidays."]},{"q":"When do they plan to relaunch?","a":"In March.","o":["Next week.","Before the holidays."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To criticize past actions with should have and connect past and present with mixed conditionals.","es":"Criticar acciones pasadas con should have y conectar pasado y presente con condicionales mixtos."},"warm":[{"q":"What is the best lesson you have learned the hard way?","au":"e8ff16421a","es":"¿Cuál es la mejor lección que has aprendido a las malas?","ex":"I learned the hard way that I should always back up my files."},{"q":"Do you usually second-guess your decisions?","au":"205c681d6c","es":"¿Sueles dudar de tus decisiones?","ex":"Sometimes. I second-guess big decisions, like changing jobs."}],"reading":{"title":"What failed startups can teach us","img":"u:photo-1521737604893-d14cc237f11d","text":"In Silicon Valley, there's a saying: \"Fail fast, learn faster.\" Every year thousands of startups close, and many founders write a \"post-mortem,\" an honest report about what went wrong. Researchers who analyzed hundreds of these reports found the same mistakes again and again. The most common one? Building a product nobody needed. \"We should have talked to customers before we wrote a single line of code,\" one founder admitted. Another big mistake is running out of money. Many teams spent too much on fancy offices instead of marketing. \"If we had spent less on furniture, we would still be in business today,\" wrote a founder from Austin. Some founders also regret hiring friends instead of experts. \"If my co-founder had been more experienced, we wouldn't have made so many basic errors,\" said another. But the reports aren't only negative. Most founders say failure was a wake-up call that made them better leaders. In fact, many of them started a second company later, and this time they didn't cut corners. As one entrepreneur put it, \"If I hadn't failed the first time, I wouldn't be successful now.\"","au":"8f80e1358d","q":[{"s":"A post-mortem is an honest report about what went wrong.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The most common mistake is hiring too many experts.","a":"no"},{"s":"One founder regrets spending too much on furniture.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Most founders say failure made them worse leaders.","a":"no"},{"s":"Many founders started a second company later.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"What is something you should have done when you were younger?","a":"I should have learned English earlier.","es":"¿Qué es algo que debiste haber hecho cuando eras más joven?","qau":"a995fc4063","aau":"ef9d101a79"},{"q":"What shouldn't you have said or done recently?","a":"I shouldn't have eaten so much pizza last night.","es":"¿Qué no debiste haber dicho o hecho recientemente?","qau":"28bfbcfb68","aau":"9e7fc3e098"},{"q":"If you had chosen a different career, what would you be doing now?","a":"If I had studied medicine, I would be a doctor now.","es":"Si hubieras elegido otra carrera, ¿qué estarías haciendo ahora?","qau":"e6fc968eaa","aau":"88e2647939"},{"q":"If you weren't so busy, what would you have done last weekend?","a":"If I weren't so busy, I would have gone to the beach.","es":"Si no estuvieras tan ocupado, ¿qué habrías hecho el fin de semana pasado?","qau":"f4fca43c6c","aau":"401927fd80"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe un mini 'post-mortem' (5–6 oraciones) de un proyecto o plan personal que no salió bien. Usa should have, shouldn't have y al menos un condicional mixto.","kw":["should have","shouldn't have","would be","If I had"],"n":5,"model":"Last year I tried to open an online store. I should have researched the market first. I shouldn't have spent so much money on the website. If I had asked for help, I would have found better suppliers. If I had planned better, I would have my own business now. Lesson learned: next time I won't cut corners."}}]},{"n":4,"title":"Verbs + Infinitive or Gerund","es":"Verbos + infinitivo o gerundio","cover":"u:photo-1666533533771-331fd9f755ea","parts":[{"id":"t4p1","topic":4,"part":1,"title":"Verb patterns: -ing or to?","es":"Patrones verbales: ¿-ing o to?","acts":["learn","vg1VerbSwipe","sort","fill","catchWord","speak"],"tip":"<p>Algunos verbos van seguidos de <b>-ing</b> (gerundio) y otros de <b>to + verbo</b> (infinitivo). ¡Hay que memorizarlos!</p>\n<p>🟦 <b>+ -ing</b>: enjoy, avoid, consider, keep, mind, finish, suggest, recommend, deny, miss, practice, can't stand, can't help, give up, put off<br><i>I <b>avoid driving</b> at rush hour.</i> · <i>Would you <b>mind closing</b> the window?</i></p>\n<p>🟥 <b>+ to</b>: decide, agree, refuse, afford, manage, plan, hope, expect, offer, promise, seem, pretend, tend, learn, want, would like<br><i>She <b>refused to pay</b> the bill.</i> · <i>We <b>can't afford to buy</b> a house in San Francisco.</i></p>\n<p>⚠️ Después de una <b>preposición</b> siempre <b>-ing</b>: <i>I'm looking forward <b>to meeting</b> you</i> (aquí <i>to</i> es preposición) · <i>I'm used <b>to living</b> alone.</i></p>\n<p>🟪 <b>like, love, hate, prefer, start, begin, continue</b> aceptan ambos sin cambiar mucho el sentido.</p>","tips":["Truco: los verbos de <b>planes y decisiones</b> (decide, plan, hope, promise) miran al futuro → <b>to</b>.","<b>look forward to</b>, <b>be used to</b>, <b>object to</b>: aquí <b>to</b> es preposición → <b>-ing</b>.","<b>suggest</b> nunca va con <i>to</i>: ❌ <i>I suggest to go</i> → ✅ <i>I suggest going</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"enjoy working remotely","es":"disfrutar trabajar a distancia","img":"u:photo-1604933762021-54a5858c9832","v":"f","au":"169ea63698"},{"en":"avoid driving at rush hour","es":"evitar manejar en hora pico","img":"u:photo-1611147533125-9ca445f32036","v":"m","au":"a0fb03949f"},{"en":"consider moving","es":"considerar mudarse","img":"u:photo-1758524942376-d22885af0324","v":"f","au":"e4671a3d82"},{"en":"keep trying","es":"seguir intentando","img":"u:photo-1741175076377-8248180bd1f4","v":"m","au":"b9b0e2d9f4"},{"en":"can't stand waiting","es":"no soportar esperar","img":"u:photo-1643288298077-f1d624de82ed","v":"f","au":"f6ccee6b1a"},{"en":"decide to quit","es":"decidir renunciar","img":"u:photo-1758691737424-b0cdcfce9f66","v":"m","au":"ae8e043116"},{"en":"agree to help","es":"aceptar ayudar","img":"u:photo-1672380135241-c024f7fbfa13","v":"f","au":"ccb14a47ff"},{"en":"refuse to pay","es":"negarse a pagar","img":"u:photo-1777679569537-8f481b36bd43","v":"m","au":"ab1ddf4be8"},{"en":"can't afford to buy","es":"no poder permitirse comprar","img":"u:photo-1623890541471-c8d3607ae7a5","v":"f","au":"9ed2bbf9ae"},{"en":"manage to finish","es":"lograr terminar","img":"u:photo-1758691737138-7b9b1884b1db","v":"m","au":"7413d7fc42"},{"en":"look forward to meeting","es":"esperar con ansias conocer","img":"u:photo-1759430710977-a557a49897ff","v":"f","au":"bae95f445f"},{"en":"be used to living","es":"estar acostumbrado a vivir","img":"u:photo-1672082546749-f8b3e92f21d7","v":"m","au":"6d16848cf1"}],"sentences":[{"en":"I really enjoy working remotely.","es":"Disfruto mucho trabajar a distancia.","img":"u:photo-1604933762021-54a5858c9832","v":"f","au":"23107f2472"},{"en":"We're considering moving to Phoenix.","es":"Estamos considerando mudarnos a Phoenix.","img":"u:photo-1758524942376-d22885af0324","v":"m","au":"2a945548ec"},{"en":"He refused to pay for the broken glass.","es":"Se negó a pagar el vidrio roto.","img":"u:photo-1777679569537-8f481b36bd43","v":"m","au":"0c3c1ee79a"},{"en":"They can't afford to buy a house in San Francisco.","es":"No pueden permitirse comprar una casa en San Francisco.","img":"u:photo-1554107136-57b138ea99df","v":"f","au":"ddc5c6a68b"},{"en":"I'm looking forward to meeting your team.","es":"Tengo muchas ganas de conocer a tu equipo.","img":"u:photo-1759430710977-a557a49897ff","v":"f","au":"c7fa852b23"},{"en":"She finally managed to finish her degree.","es":"Por fin logró terminar su carrera.","img":"u:photo-1658235081483-8f06aa0882cf","v":"m","au":"f04e2845e6"}],"fill":[{"s":"Would you mind ___ the window? It's freezing.","a":"closing","o":["to close","close"],"h":"mind + -ing","full":"Would you mind closing the window? It's freezing.","au":"e154809f0f"},{"s":"We can't afford ___ a new car this year.","a":"to buy","o":["buying","buy"],"h":"afford + to","full":"We can't afford to buy a new car this year.","au":"3b0cb9f7ad"},{"s":"I'm really looking forward to ___ you in Boston.","a":"seeing","o":["see","saw"],"h":"preposición to + -ing","full":"I'm really looking forward to seeing you in Boston.","au":"65c8b87f7a"},{"s":"She suggested ___ the meeting to Friday.","a":"moving","o":["to move","move"],"h":"suggest + -ing","full":"She suggested moving the meeting to Friday.","au":"35b123db24"},{"s":"He promised ___ the report by noon.","a":"to send","o":["sending","send"],"h":"promise + to","full":"He promised to send the report by noon.","au":"e1066044de"},{"s":"I've given up ___ to change his mind.","a":"trying","o":["to try","try"],"h":"give up + -ing","full":"I've given up trying to change his mind.","au":"17768b1607"},{"s":"They're not used to ___ in such cold weather.","a":"living","o":["live","lived"],"h":"be used to + -ing","full":"They're not used to living in such cold weather.","au":"8dc125a9e3"}],"sort":{"cats":["+ -ing","+ to"],"items":[{"w":"enjoy","c":"+ -ing","au":"b6469240c7"},{"w":"avoid","c":"+ -ing","au":"92765a2982"},{"w":"consider","c":"+ -ing","au":"7fedf77fdf"},{"w":"suggest","c":"+ -ing","au":"36b20e7eb8"},{"w":"can't stand","c":"+ -ing","au":"f714c889bc"},{"w":"give up","c":"+ -ing","au":"7b3c18579e"},{"w":"decide","c":"+ to","au":"8d7a4a51a8"},{"w":"refuse","c":"+ to","au":"0224ed74c0"},{"w":"afford","c":"+ to","au":"3acd0fe01f"},{"w":"manage","c":"+ to","au":"ca388a08fd"},{"w":"promise","c":"+ to","au":"7c5e77b393"},{"w":"pretend","c":"+ to","au":"1b60859895"}]},"goal":{"en":"To use verbs followed by -ing or to + infinitive correctly.","es":"Usar correctamente los verbos seguidos de -ing o de to + infinitivo."},"warm":[{"q":"What do you enjoy doing on a Sunday afternoon?","au":"ae02762200","es":"¿Qué disfrutas hacer un domingo por la tarde?","ex":"I enjoy having lunch with my family and taking a nap."},{"q":"What have you decided to change this year?","au":"3a3bddaf9d","es":"¿Qué has decidido cambiar este año?","ex":"I've decided to stop eating junk food and to exercise more."}],"reading":{"title":"Why I decided to work from home","img":"u:photo-1604933762021-54a5858c9832","text":"Three years ago, I was spending almost two hours a day stuck in traffic in Atlanta. I couldn't stand driving at rush hour, and I was always tired. One day I decided to talk to my manager. I suggested working from home two days a week as an experiment. At first she refused to consider it, but after a month she agreed to try. The results were amazing. I managed to finish my reports faster, and I stopped feeling stressed all the time. Now I work remotely four days a week. I really enjoy having lunch with my kids, and I've started running in the mornings instead of sitting in my car. Of course, it isn't perfect. I miss chatting with my coworkers, and I have to avoid checking emails late at night. Some friends keep asking me how I can concentrate at home. The truth is that it took me a while to get used to working alone. My advice? If you're thinking about asking for remote work, prepare a clear plan and offer to measure your results. Most managers can't afford to lose good employees, and many are willing to listen.","au":"26fdff2561","q":[{"s":"The writer used to spend two hours a day in traffic.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The manager agreed immediately.","a":"no"},{"s":"The writer has started running in the mornings.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The writer doesn't miss chatting with coworkers.","a":"no"},{"s":"It took the writer some time to get used to working alone.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"What do you enjoy doing after work?","a":"I enjoy cooking and listening to podcasts.","es":"¿Qué disfrutas hacer después del trabajo?","qau":"cf3e5c3264","aau":"77fc44c11c"},{"q":"What do you avoid doing when you're stressed?","a":"I avoid drinking too much coffee.","es":"¿Qué evitas hacer cuando estás estresado?","qau":"a101611d16","aau":"b024f1a190"},{"q":"What are you planning to do next year?","a":"I'm planning to take a trip to Canada.","es":"¿Qué planeas hacer el próximo año?","qau":"15c608749d","aau":"830525dc9a"},{"q":"What are you looking forward to doing this month?","a":"I'm looking forward to seeing my family.","es":"¿Qué esperas con ansias hacer este mes?","qau":"202ae110f0","aau":"68d7d3e057"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe 6 oraciones sobre tus hábitos y planes usando al menos 3 verbos + -ing (enjoy, avoid, keep…) y 3 verbos + to (decide, plan, hope…).","kw":["enjoy","avoid","decide","plan"],"n":6,"model":"I enjoy reading on the train. I avoid eating fast food during the week. I keep forgetting my umbrella. This year I decided to learn to swim. I'm planning to visit New York in December. I hope to get a promotion soon."}},{"id":"t4p2","topic":4,"part":2,"title":"Same verb, different meaning","es":"Mismo verbo, distinto significado","acts":["learn","vg2MeaningTwins","fill","dialogue","unscramble","speak"],"tip":"<p>Estos verbos aceptan <b>-ing</b> y <b>to</b>, pero <b>cambia el significado</b>:</p>\n<p>🧠 <b>remember / forget + to</b> = acordarse/olvidar <b>hacer</b> algo (tarea pendiente) · <b>+ -ing</b> = recordar algo que <b>ya hiciste</b>.<br><i>Remember <b>to lock</b> the door.</i> vs. <i>I remember <b>locking</b> the door.</i></p>\n<p>🛑 <b>stop + -ing</b> = dejar de hacer · <b>stop + to</b> = parar <b>para</b> hacer otra cosa.<br><i>He stopped <b>smoking</b>.</i> (ya no fuma) vs. <i>He stopped <b>to smoke</b>.</i> (paró para fumar)</p>\n<p>🔧 <b>try + to</b> = esforzarse (es difícil) · <b>try + -ing</b> = probar algo como experimento.<br><i>Try <b>to stay</b> calm.</i> vs. <i>Try <b>restarting</b> the router.</i></p>\n<p>😔 <b>regret + to</b> = lamentar informar (formal) · <b>regret + -ing</b> = arrepentirse de algo hecho.</p>\n<p>📌 Después de preposición (<b>in, of, about, at, without, instead of, before, after</b>) → siempre <b>-ing</b>: <i>She's good <b>at negotiating</b>.</i></p>","tips":["Piensa en el orden: <b>to</b> = la acción viene <b>después</b>; <b>-ing</b> = la acción ya pasó o está en curso.","<b>We regret to inform you…</b> es la frase típica de cartas de rechazo de empleo.","<b>without + -ing</b>: <i>He left <b>without saying</b> goodbye</i> (se fue sin despedirse)."],"vocab":[{"en":"remember to lock the door","es":"acordarse de cerrar con llave","img":"u:photo-1733244766159-f58f4184fd38","v":"f","au":"dfcd223974"},{"en":"remember locking the door","es":"recordar haber cerrado con llave","img":"u:photo-1604364721460-0cbc5866219d","v":"m","au":"3fcf5c26e6"},{"en":"forget to call","es":"olvidar llamar","img":"u:photo-1698891667770-c611cf57d82c","v":"f","au":"cc4992b2f3"},{"en":"never forget seeing","es":"nunca olvidar haber visto","img":"u:photo-1575527048208-6475b441e0a0","v":"m","au":"48aaa20943"},{"en":"stop to buy coffee","es":"parar para comprar café","img":"u:photo-1789652121318-7ad481c346fc","v":"f","au":"a5bfa08f9a"},{"en":"stop smoking","es":"dejar de fumar","img":"u:photo-1527099908998-5b73a5fe2a0d","v":"m","au":"08e177f0f5"},{"en":"try restarting it","es":"probar reiniciándolo","img":"u:photo-1534665482403-a909d0d97c67","v":"m","au":"e0234b8985"},{"en":"try to stay calm","es":"tratar de mantener la calma","img":"u:photo-1758874384683-0accd9fb26ee","v":"f","au":"2e80afcc6b"},{"en":"regret to inform you","es":"lamentar informarle","img":"u:photo-1649019489428-70f505daacd6","v":"m","au":"3ac4b252e9"},{"en":"regret quitting","es":"arrepentirse de renunciar","img":"u:photo-1534330207526-8e81f10ec6fc","v":"f","au":"32cc8b8d99"},{"en":"be interested in learning","es":"estar interesado en aprender","img":"u:photo-1758685848208-e108b6af94cc","v":"f","au":"c9083b7e42"},{"en":"instead of driving","es":"en lugar de manejar","img":"u:photo-1528629297340-d1d466945dc5","v":"m","au":"9ec3ff03e6"}],"sentences":[{"en":"Remember to lock the door when you leave.","es":"Acuérdate de cerrar con llave cuando salgas.","img":"u:photo-1733244766159-f58f4184fd38","v":"f","au":"54ed90e629"},{"en":"I don't remember locking the car.","es":"No recuerdo haber cerrado el carro.","img":"u:photo-1643792801605-1f8081811439","v":"m","au":"fe509183bc"},{"en":"He stopped smoking three years ago.","es":"Dejó de fumar hace tres años.","img":"u:photo-1527099908998-5b73a5fe2a0d","v":"m","au":"62d302130d"},{"en":"We stopped to buy coffee on the way.","es":"Paramos para comprar café en el camino.","img":"u:photo-1789652121318-7ad481c346fc","v":"f","au":"656a9b80be"},{"en":"Have you tried restarting the router?","es":"¿Has probado reiniciando el router?","img":"u:photo-1534665482403-a909d0d97c67","v":"m","au":"fac1a7bfeb"},{"en":"I'll never forget seeing the Grand Canyon.","es":"Nunca olvidaré haber visto el Gran Cañón.","img":"u:photo-1575527048208-6475b441e0a0","v":"f","au":"416c1c735c"}],"fill":[{"s":"Did you remember ___ the electricity bill? It's due today.","a":"to pay","o":["paying","pay"],"h":"tarea pendiente","full":"Did you remember to pay the electricity bill? It's due today.","au":"93c7d7380c"},{"s":"I clearly remember ___ the keys on the table.","a":"leaving","o":["to leave","leave"],"h":"recuerdo del pasado","full":"I clearly remember leaving the keys on the table.","au":"54ce649972"},{"s":"We stopped ___ gas in Albuquerque.","a":"to get","o":["getting","get"],"h":"paramos PARA…","full":"We stopped to get gas in Albuquerque.","au":"dc746d0488"},{"s":"You should stop ___ so much sugar.","a":"eating","o":["to eat","eat"],"h":"dejar de…","full":"You should stop eating so much sugar.","au":"0d91ba9d4e"},{"s":"If the app freezes, try ___ your phone.","a":"restarting","o":["to restart","restart"],"h":"prueba / experimento","full":"If the app freezes, try restarting your phone.","au":"55fa9b62df"},{"s":"We regret ___ you that the position has been filled.","a":"to inform","o":["informing","inform"],"h":"lamentar informar (formal)","full":"We regret to inform you that the position has been filled.","au":"8d80a28226"},{"s":"She left the party without ___ goodbye.","a":"saying","o":["to say","say"],"h":"preposición + -ing","full":"She left the party without saying goodbye.","au":"056f3287f1"}],"dialogue":{"title":"Did you remember?","es":"¿Te acordaste?","img":"u:photo-1783780933273-392188f83694","lines":[{"who":"Jenna","v":"f","t":"Hey, did you remember to pay the internet bill? It's not working.","au":"454981e580"},{"who":"Luis","v":"m","t":"Yes! I remember paying it on Monday. I have the receipt.","au":"0d378cefe8"},{"who":"Jenna","v":"f","t":"Weird. I've tried restarting the router, but nothing.","au":"9ca0f2839e"},{"who":"Luis","v":"m","t":"Did you try unplugging it for a minute? That usually works.","au":"d9e762c17e"},{"who":"Jenna","v":"f","t":"Not yet. Oh, and I forgot to tell you: your mom called.","au":"c95efe9488"},{"who":"Luis","v":"m","t":"Oh no, I promised to call her back yesterday. I regret not doing it.","au":"95dc423411"},{"who":"Jenna","v":"f","t":"Stop worrying. Call her now instead of feeling guilty.","au":"0c5e5ea5b2"},{"who":"Luis","v":"m","t":"You're right. And I'll stop to buy groceries on my way back.","au":"34aa767851"}],"q":[{"q":"When did Luis pay the bill?","a":"On Monday.","o":["Yesterday.","He forgot."]},{"q":"What does Luis suggest for the router?","a":"Unplugging it for a minute.","o":["Buying a new one.","Calling his mom."]},{"q":"What will Luis do on his way back?","a":"Stop to buy groceries.","o":["Stop smoking.","Pay the bill again."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To understand how remember, forget, stop, try and regret change meaning with -ing or to.","es":"Entender cómo remember, forget, stop, try y regret cambian de significado con -ing o to."},"warm":[{"q":"What is something you always forget to do?","au":"a25001cf45","es":"¿Qué es algo que siempre olvidas hacer?","ex":"I always forget to water my plants."},{"q":"What is one thing you will never forget seeing?","au":"23fa507881","es":"¿Qué es algo que nunca olvidarás haber visto?","ex":"I'll never forget seeing the Statue of Liberty for the first time."}],"reading":{"title":"The road trip that taught me patience","img":"u:photo-1690644932424-63fdff67172d","text":"Last summer my brother and I drove from Los Angeles to the Grand Canyon. Before we left, my mom said, \"Remember to check the tires!\" Of course, we forgot to do it. About three hours into the trip, in the middle of the Mojave Desert, we heard a loud noise. A flat tire. My brother tried to change it, but the spare tire was flat too. We tried calling a tow truck, but there was no signal. So we stopped to think. I remember looking at the empty road and feeling completely lost. Finally, a truck driver named Gus stopped to help us. He drove us to a gas station forty miles away, refusing to accept any money. While we waited for the repair, he told us he had stopped smoking after thirty years and now drove with a jar of candy instead. We arrived at the Grand Canyon a day late, but I'll never forget seeing the sunset from the South Rim. Do I regret not checking the tires? Absolutely. But I don't regret taking that trip. Next time, though, I'll stop worrying less and planning more.","au":"6c20819932","q":[{"s":"Their mom reminded them to check the tires.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The spare tire was in perfect condition.","a":"no"},{"s":"They called a tow truck successfully.","a":"no"},{"s":"Gus refused to accept money.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Gus still smokes every day.","a":"no"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Do you remember meeting your best friend for the first time?","a":"Yes, I remember meeting her at a party in college.","es":"¿Recuerdas haber conocido a tu mejor amigo por primera vez?","qau":"7453116d96","aau":"08dced0e99"},{"q":"Have you ever stopped doing something unhealthy?","a":"Yes, I stopped drinking soda two years ago.","es":"¿Alguna vez has dejado de hacer algo poco saludable?","qau":"42ace5e505","aau":"f20d064f3f"},{"q":"What do you do if your computer freezes?","a":"I try restarting it, and if that doesn't work, I call IT.","es":"¿Qué haces si tu computador se congela?","qau":"ad6c7f6950","aau":"7e2e601d5d"},{"q":"Is there something you regret not doing?","a":"I regret not studying abroad when I was younger.","es":"¿Hay algo de lo que te arrepientas de no haber hecho?","qau":"ed918a7dcf","aau":"7682678efd"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe 6 oraciones: una con cada verbo (remember, forget, stop, try, regret) usando la forma que corresponda, y una con preposición + -ing (instead of, without, before…).","kw":["remember","stop","try","regret","instead of"],"n":6,"model":"I always remember to call my mom on Sundays. I'll never forget meeting my wife in Chicago. I stopped eating sugar last year. When I can't sleep, I try reading a boring book. I regret not learning to play an instrument. I walk to work instead of driving."}}]},{"n":5,"title":"So, Neither, Either","es":"So, neither, either","cover":"u:photo-1530047139082-5435ca3c4614","parts":[{"id":"t5p1","topic":5,"part":1,"title":"So do I! Neither do I!","es":"¡Yo también! ¡Yo tampoco!","acts":["learn","snMatchmaker","dialogue","sayPop","fill","speak"],"tip":"<p>Para decir que estás <b>de acuerdo</b> (yo también / yo tampoco) repites el <b>auxiliar</b> de la oración:</p>\n<p>➕ Oración positiva → <b>So + auxiliar + sujeto</b><br><i>I love jazz. → <b>So do I.</b></i> · <i>I've been to Chicago. → <b>So have I.</b></i> · <i>I'm tired. → <b>So am I.</b></i></p>\n<p>➖ Oración negativa → <b>Neither + auxiliar (positivo) + sujeto</b><br><i>I don't eat meat. → <b>Neither do I.</b></i> · <i>I can't swim. → <b>Neither can I.</b></i></p>\n<p>❌ Para estar <b>en desacuerdo</b>, usa sujeto + auxiliar contrario: <i>I love jazz. → <b>Oh, I don't.</b></i> · <i>I haven't seen it. → <b>Really? I have.</b></i></p>\n<p>🔑 El auxiliar depende del tiempo: presente → <b>do/does</b> · pasado → <b>did</b> · perfecto → <b>have/has</b> · <b>be, can, will, would</b> se repiten.</p>","tips":["Después de <b>neither</b> el verbo va en <b>positivo</b>: ❌ <i>Neither don't I</i> → ✅ <i>Neither do I</i>.","<b>Neither</b> en EE. UU. se dice <i>níder</i>; en el Reino Unido <i>náider</i>. ¡Ambas son correctas!","<b>Me too / Me neither</b> son informales; <b>So do I / Neither do I</b> suenan más cuidados."],"vocab":[{"en":"So do I.","es":"Yo también.","img":"u:photo-1713946598491-4f85decbeaaf","v":"f","au":"87091fc9fe"},{"en":"Neither do I.","es":"Yo tampoco.","img":"u:photo-1758873268444-73528cd3ec93","v":"m","au":"17d61210e8"},{"en":"Me too.","es":"Yo también (informal).","img":"u:photo-1543269865-cbf427effbad","v":"f","au":"972b7f7460"},{"en":"Me neither.","es":"Yo tampoco (informal).","img":"u:photo-1659356576489-856f824d68a2","v":"m","au":"e1690ae73f"},{"en":"I do. / I don't.","es":"Yo sí. / Yo no.","img":"u:photo-1498192467103-290f567eb3a3","v":"f","au":"23a2b204bd"},{"en":"So have I.","es":"Yo también (con have).","img":"u:photo-1567502401034-b947ee46e249","v":"m","au":"08f42438cd"},{"en":"Neither can I.","es":"Yo tampoco puedo.","img":"u:photo-1634906344426-2ba0e7c91b09","v":"f","au":"8dcb4490d7"},{"en":"Same here.","es":"Lo mismo digo.","img":"u:photo-1491438590914-bc09fcaaf77a","v":"m","au":"25b5182782"},{"en":"have a lot in common","es":"tener mucho en común","img":"u:photo-1713519346478-c91dbcbe010f","v":"f","au":"c42db31fa0"},{"en":"find common ground","es":"encontrar puntos en común","img":"u:photo-1672380135241-c024f7fbfa13","v":"m","au":"4a73006d5a"},{"en":"I couldn't agree more.","es":"No podría estar más de acuerdo.","img":"u:photo-1758518731706-be5d5230e5a5","v":"f","au":"3bfef21c87"},{"en":"Oh, really? I don't.","es":"¿En serio? Yo no.","img":"u:photo-1713256449316-1a4067517c3b","v":"m","au":"ce06f0e9c9"}],"sentences":[{"en":"I've never been to Alaska. Neither have I.","es":"Nunca he ido a Alaska. Yo tampoco.","img":"u:photo-1673114819432-1aa36952dd3e","v":"f","au":"105076995a"},{"en":"I'm exhausted after this week. So am I.","es":"Estoy agotado después de esta semana. Yo también.","img":"u:photo-1713946598534-a20fd25a4d1d","v":"m","au":"15975feba1"},{"en":"I can't stand long meetings. Neither can I.","es":"No soporto las reuniones largas. Yo tampoco.","img":"u:photo-1517048676732-d65bc937f952","v":"f","au":"026bd42182"},{"en":"I loved the concert last night. So did I.","es":"Me encantó el concierto de anoche. A mí también.","img":"u:photo-1501386761578-eac5c94b800a","v":"m","au":"6db0cddf94"},{"en":"I don't like spicy food. Oh, really? I do.","es":"No me gusta la comida picante. ¿En serio? A mí sí.","img":"u:photo-1687881063470-a78e6ea2590e","v":"f","au":"70703183f0"},{"en":"We have a lot in common.","es":"Tenemos mucho en común.","img":"u:photo-1713519346478-c91dbcbe010f","v":"m","au":"88970ade40"}],"fill":[{"s":"A: I work from home on Fridays. B: So ___ I.","a":"do","o":["am","have"],"h":"presente → do","full":"A: I work from home on Fridays. B: So do I.","au":"1d0088a53b"},{"s":"A: I haven't finished the report. B: Neither ___ I.","a":"have","o":["do","haven't"],"h":"perfecto → have","full":"A: I haven't finished the report. B: Neither have I.","au":"9c120808cd"},{"s":"A: I was born in Texas. B: So ___ my wife.","a":"was","o":["did","is"],"h":"pasado de be → was","full":"A: I was born in Texas. B: So was my wife.","au":"e70d68bb18"},{"s":"A: I can't speak French. B: Neither ___ I.","a":"can","o":["can't","do"],"h":"neither + positivo","full":"A: I can't speak French. B: Neither can I.","au":"db689dbc87"},{"s":"A: I loved that movie. B: Really? I ___.","a":"didn't","o":["don't","wasn't"],"h":"desacuerdo en pasado","full":"A: I loved that movie. B: Really? I didn't.","au":"28510556e7"},{"s":"A: I'll be at the conference. B: So ___ we.","a":"will","o":["are","do"],"h":"futuro → will","full":"A: I'll be at the conference. B: So will we.","au":"7ee5ce8d2e"}],"dialogue":{"title":"Speed networking","es":"Networking rápido","img":"u:photo-1775163560631-6ff15eb2fa1f","lines":[{"who":"Host","v":"f","t":"OK, everyone, you have three minutes. Find someone you have something in common with!","au":"d833b89c28"},{"who":"Nate","v":"m","t":"Hi, I'm Nate. I work in software sales, and I'm new in Austin.","au":"07a08bfcb6"},{"who":"Priya","v":"f","t":"Nice to meet you! I'm Priya. So am I. I moved here in January.","au":"5a576ce0fd"},{"who":"Nate","v":"m","t":"No way. So did I! I came from Chicago. I can't stand the cold anymore.","au":"756ba36f8c"},{"who":"Priya","v":"f","t":"Neither can I! I'm from Minneapolis. But I don't like the heat here either.","au":"0b51d39753"},{"who":"Nate","v":"m","t":"Oh, really? I do. I love it. And I've never been to a rodeo.","au":"e1c31dfb8b"},{"who":"Priya","v":"f","t":"Neither have I. Should we go to one together this weekend?","au":"f4451383f3"},{"who":"Nate","v":"m","t":"Sounds great. I couldn't agree more: we have a lot in common.","au":"e900532f49"}],"q":[{"q":"When did Priya move to Austin?","a":"In January.","o":["Last weekend.","Ten years ago."]},{"q":"What does Nate say about the heat?","a":"He loves it.","o":["He can't stand it.","He has never felt it."]},{"q":"What have neither of them done?","a":"Been to a rodeo.","o":["Worked in sales.","Lived in Chicago."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To agree and disagree naturally with so, neither and short responses with auxiliaries.","es":"Mostrar acuerdo y desacuerdo con naturalidad usando so, neither y respuestas cortas con auxiliares."},"warm":[{"q":"Do you have a lot in common with your best friend?","au":"dd5205923a","es":"¿Tienes mucho en común con tu mejor amigo?","ex":"Yes, we do. We both love soccer and spicy food."},{"q":"What kind of people do you get along with easily?","au":"e4eb450efa","es":"¿Con qué tipo de personas te llevas bien fácilmente?","ex":"I get along with people who are honest and funny."}],"reading":{"title":"Why we love people who agree with us","img":"u:photo-1530047139082-5435ca3c4614","text":"Have you ever met someone and felt an instant connection? Psychologists call it the \"similarity effect\": we tend to like people who share our opinions, habits and experiences. When a stranger at a party says, \"I can't stand reality shows,\" and we answer, \"Neither can I!\" something happens in our brain. We relax, we smile, and we start to trust that person. Researchers at a university in Michigan found that small agreements, such as \"So do I\" or \"Me too,\" make conversations last longer and feel more pleasant. However, the same researchers warn that agreeing with everything can be a problem. If you always say \"So do I\" just to be polite, people may notice that you're not being honest. Real connection also needs respectful disagreement. Saying \"Oh, really? I don't. Why do you like it?\" shows interest and opens a deeper conversation. In job interviews and networking events, the best approach is to find common ground first, and then share your own perspective. In other words, agree when you really agree, disagree kindly when you don't, and always be curious about the other person.","au":"7118c838c4","q":[{"s":"The \"similarity effect\" means we like people who are similar to us.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Small agreements make conversations shorter.","a":"no"},{"s":"The researchers say agreeing with everything can be a problem.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Respectful disagreement can open a deeper conversation.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The text recommends never sharing your own opinion.","a":"no"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"I love traveling alone. And you?","a":"So do I. / Oh, really? I don't. I prefer traveling with friends.","es":"Me encanta viajar solo. ¿Y a ti?","qau":"fb71dbf8a1","aau":"e6077f2bc1"},{"q":"I've never tried sushi. What about you?","a":"Neither have I. / Really? I have. I love it.","es":"Nunca he probado el sushi. ¿Y tú?","qau":"147062675c","aau":"50c3638d14"},{"q":"I can't work without coffee. And you?","a":"Neither can I! / I can. I drink tea.","es":"No puedo trabajar sin café. ¿Y tú?","qau":"ac2782402a","aau":"ba3e544e39"},{"q":"I didn't watch the game last night. Did you?","a":"Neither did I. / I did. It was amazing.","es":"No vi el partido anoche. ¿Y tú?","qau":"975f8c0c61","aau":"4112719b3a"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe 6 afirmaciones sobre ti (3 positivas y 3 negativas) y debajo de cada una la respuesta de un amigo: 3 de acuerdo (So… / Neither…) y 3 en desacuerdo.","kw":["So","Neither","I don't","I do"],"n":6,"model":"I love jazz. So do I. I've never been to Hawaii. Neither have I. I can play the guitar. Really? I can't. I don't like coffee. Oh, I do. I was born in May. So was I. I won't travel this year. Really? I will."}},{"id":"t5p2","topic":5,"part":2,"title":"Either, neither… nor & short answers","es":"Either, neither… nor y respuestas cortas","acts":["learn","snAuxRadar","fill","sort","bubblePop","speak"],"tip":"<p>🔁 Hay varias formas de decir <b>yo tampoco</b>:<br><i>I don't drink coffee.</i> → <b>Neither do I.</b> = <b>Nor do I.</b> (formal) = <b>I don't either.</b> = <b>Me neither.</b> (informal)</p>\n<p>⚠️ <b>either</b> va al final con verbo <b>negativo</b>; <b>neither</b> va al principio con verbo <b>positivo</b>.<br>❌ <i>I don't neither</i> · ✅ <i>I don't <b>either</b></i> · ✅ <i><b>Neither</b> do I</i></p>\n<p>⚖️ <b>neither A nor B</b> = ni A ni B (verbo positivo): <i><b>Neither</b> the manager <b>nor</b> the CEO answered.</i><br><b>either A or B</b> = o A o B: <i>You can pay <b>either</b> in cash <b>or</b> by card.</i><br><b>both A and B</b> = tanto A como B: <i><b>Both</b> Miami <b>and</b> Orlando are hot.</i></p>\n<p>💬 <b>Reacciones cortas</b> con auxiliar muestran interés: <i>I quit my job. → <b>You did?</b></i> · <i>I'm getting married. → <b>Are you?</b> Congrats!</i></p>","tips":["Con <b>neither…nor</b> el verbo concuerda con el sujeto más cercano: <i>Neither my boss nor my coworkers <b>were</b> there.</i>","<b>Either</b> se dice <i>íder</i> en EE. UU.; suena muy natural al final: <i>I can't <b>either</b>.</i>","Las reacciones <i>You did? / Is she?</i> suben de tono al final, como una pregunta de sorpresa."],"vocab":[{"en":"I don't either.","es":"Yo tampoco (con either).","img":"u:photo-1659356576489-856f824d68a2","v":"m","au":"6c37204cff"},{"en":"not… either","es":"tampoco (con verbo negativo)","img":"u:photo-1639986169769-feb3c3a92346","v":"f","au":"df6c07fc45"},{"en":"neither… nor","es":"ni… ni","img":"u:photo-1610559176044-d2695ca6c63d","v":"f","au":"f06d5861ca"},{"en":"either… or","es":"o… o","img":"u:photo-1429743305873-d4065c15f93e","v":"m","au":"563eb53bc0"},{"en":"both… and","es":"tanto… como","img":"u:photo-1769412340450-528930c62f77","v":"f","au":"e6d8f75879"},{"en":"So did she.","es":"Ella también (pasado).","img":"u:photo-1758520387283-303b0b332e89","v":"f","au":"a9c1036a2c"},{"en":"Neither was I.","es":"Yo tampoco estaba.","img":"u:photo-1692133226337-55e513450a32","v":"m","au":"7d2433a73d"},{"en":"Nor do I.","es":"Ni yo (formal).","img":"u:photo-1431540015161-0bf868a2d407","v":"f","au":"e7ba4b79a6"},{"en":"So would I.","es":"Yo también lo haría.","img":"u:photo-1542353436-312f0e1f67ff","v":"m","au":"a2698b24cd"},{"en":"Neither has he.","es":"Él tampoco (con have).","img":"u:photo-1718461455367-9c6be6e51206","v":"m","au":"a28573ae00"},{"en":"either way","es":"de cualquier forma","img":"u:photo-1583125320604-8245f1e50c1e","v":"f","au":"c7cd94ac85"},{"en":"You did?","es":"¿Ah, sí? (reacción con auxiliar)","img":"u:photo-1758523672207-bc370d350fd9","v":"m","au":"6ba481b799"}],"sentences":[{"en":"I didn't get the email either.","es":"Yo tampoco recibí el correo.","img":"u:photo-1524508762098-fd966ffb6ef9","v":"f","au":"8a01401089"},{"en":"Neither my boss nor my coworkers knew about it.","es":"Ni mi jefe ni mis compañeros lo sabían.","img":"u:photo-1758691737138-7b9b1884b1db","v":"m","au":"c06ad7bdce"},{"en":"You can pay either in cash or by card.","es":"Puede pagar en efectivo o con tarjeta.","img":"u:photo-1654263937079-f63a3ea4d48b","v":"f","au":"710aa8c0e5"},{"en":"Both Miami and San Diego have great beaches.","es":"Tanto Miami como San Diego tienen excelentes playas.","img":"u:photo-1589083130544-0d6a2926e519","v":"m","au":"efb072d571"},{"en":"She wasn't at the meeting, and neither was I.","es":"Ella no estuvo en la reunión, y yo tampoco.","img":"u:photo-1692133226337-55e513450a32","v":"f","au":"6e5ee459c0"},{"en":"I'd love to work abroad. So would I!","es":"Me encantaría trabajar en el extranjero. ¡A mí también!","img":"u:photo-1542353436-312f0e1f67ff","v":"m","au":"a77473196a"}],"fill":[{"s":"A: I don't like horror movies. B: I don't ___.","a":"either","o":["neither","too"],"h":"negativo + either","full":"A: I don't like horror movies. B: I don't either.","au":"fe044677ba"},{"s":"___ the hotel nor the restaurant accepted pets.","a":"Neither","o":["Either","Both"],"h":"ni… ni","full":"Neither the hotel nor the restaurant accepted pets.","au":"7d32fd68c5"},{"s":"You can ___ call me or send me a text.","a":"either","o":["neither","both"],"h":"o… o","full":"You can either call me or send me a text.","au":"33e580191c"},{"s":"A: I didn't sleep well. B: ___ did I.","a":"Neither","o":["Either","So"],"h":"neither + auxiliar positivo","full":"A: I didn't sleep well. B: Neither did I.","au":"6ce3cf511d"},{"s":"She can't drive, and her husband can't ___.","a":"either","o":["neither","too"],"h":"tampoco al final","full":"She can't drive, and her husband can't either.","au":"e9d186f75f"},{"s":"A: I've just bought a house! B: You ___? Congratulations!","a":"have","o":["did","are"],"h":"reacción con el mismo auxiliar","full":"A: I've just bought a house! B: You have? Congratulations!","au":"9c1a4a69f5"}],"sort":{"cats":["Agree (+)","Agree (−)","Disagree"],"items":[{"w":"So do I.","c":"Agree (+)","au":"87091fc9fe"},{"w":"Me too.","c":"Agree (+)","au":"972b7f7460"},{"w":"So have I.","c":"Agree (+)","au":"19b1493386"},{"w":"So would I.","c":"Agree (+)","au":"b833cd29df"},{"w":"Neither do I.","c":"Agree (−)","au":"17173fdaf0"},{"w":"I don't either.","c":"Agree (−)","au":"01c2091c6a"},{"w":"Nor have I.","c":"Agree (−)","au":"3cf2c878d2"},{"w":"Me neither.","c":"Agree (−)","au":"fc7d5376f2"},{"w":"Oh, I do!","c":"Disagree","au":"5391f2f2b3"},{"w":"Really? I haven't.","c":"Disagree","au":"838c9b1fd1"},{"w":"I can't, actually.","c":"Disagree","au":"f4178abf2f"}]},"goal":{"en":"To use either, neither… nor, both… and, and short reactions with auxiliaries.","es":"Usar either, neither… nor, both… and y reacciones cortas con auxiliares."},"warm":[{"q":"Which do you prefer: the beach or the mountains, or both?","au":"c193722462","es":"¿Qué prefieres: la playa, las montañas o ambas?","ex":"I like both, but I prefer the mountains because I don't like the heat."},{"q":"What is something neither you nor your family likes?","au":"edb2e18e8e","es":"¿Qué es algo que ni a ti ni a tu familia les gusta?","ex":"Neither my family nor I like waking up early on weekends."}],"reading":{"title":"Two cities, one decision","img":"u:photo-1589083130544-0d6a2926e519","text":"When my company told me I could transfer either to Miami or to San Diego, I thought the decision would be easy. It wasn't. Both cities have great beaches, and both are expensive. My wife didn't want to live too far from her family in Houston, and I didn't either. On the other hand, neither of us likes humid weather, and Miami is very humid in the summer. So we made a list. Miami was closer to Houston, and the flights were cheaper. San Diego had a milder climate and more hiking trails. Neither city was perfect, and neither of us wanted to make a mistake. My daughter didn't care at all. \"I'll be happy either way,\" she said, \"as long as I can have a dog.\" Finally, we visited both cities for a long weekend. In San Diego, a neighbor told us, \"I moved here from Florida, and I've never regretted it.\" \"You did?\" my wife asked. \"Why?\" \"No hurricanes and no humidity,\" she answered. That night, my wife and I looked at each other and smiled. Neither of us needed to say anything. We moved to San Diego three months later.","au":"c696e04daf","q":[{"s":"The company offered a transfer to either Miami or San Diego.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The writer's wife wanted to live far from her family.","a":"no"},{"s":"Neither the writer nor his wife likes humid weather.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Their daughter had a strong preference for Miami.","a":"no"},{"s":"They finally moved to San Diego.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"I don't speak German. Do you?","a":"No, I don't either. / Actually, I do. A little.","es":"No hablo alemán. ¿Y tú?","qau":"5fa08a8f80","aau":"4f2220a810"},{"q":"Would you prefer to work either from home or at the office?","a":"I'd prefer to work from home, but either option is fine.","es":"¿Preferirías trabajar desde casa o en la oficina?","qau":"fcf6ed847d","aau":"4c47008a80"},{"q":"What are two things both you and your partner enjoy?","a":"Both my partner and I enjoy hiking and cooking.","es":"¿Cuáles son dos cosas que disfrutan tanto tú como tu pareja?","qau":"86bf2eb46a","aau":"3ffb5adfd4"},{"q":"I just got a promotion!","a":"You did? Congratulations! That's great news.","es":"¡Me acaban de ascender!","qau":"f5a4893832","aau":"5dcd542c28"}],"hw":{"es":"Compara dos ciudades, trabajos o productos en 6 oraciones usando either… or, neither… nor, both… and y not… either.","kw":["either","neither","nor","both"],"n":6,"model":"I could buy either a car or a motorcycle. Both options are expensive. Neither the car nor the motorcycle is new. The car doesn't have air conditioning, and the motorcycle doesn't either. Both are red. In the end, I bought neither of them and took the bus."}}]},{"n":6,"title":"Present/Past Perfect Continuous","es":"Presente y pasado perfecto continuo","cover":"u:photo-1501139083538-0139583c060f","parts":[{"id":"t6p1","topic":6,"part":1,"title":"I've been doing: duration & evidence","es":"I've been doing: duración y evidencia","acts":["learn","ppcSherlock","listenChoose","fill","oddOneOut","speak"],"tip":"<p>📐 <b>Presente perfecto continuo</b>: <b>have / has + been + -ing</b></p>\n<p>⏳ <b>Duración</b> de algo que empezó en el pasado y <b>sigue</b>: <i>I<b>'ve been working</b> here <b>since</b> 2020 / <b>for</b> five years.</i><br>Pregunta: <i><b>How long have you been</b> living in Houston?</i></p>\n<p>🔍 <b>Evidencia visible</b> de una actividad reciente: <i>Your eyes are red. <b>Have you been crying?</b></i> · <i>The streets are wet. It<b>'s been raining</b>.</i></p>\n<p>⚖️ <b>been doing</b> (actividad, proceso) vs. <b>have done</b> (resultado, cantidad):<br><i>I<b>'ve been writing</b> emails all morning.</i> (la actividad) · <i>I<b>'ve written</b> twenty emails.</i> (el resultado)</p>\n<p>📌 <b>for</b> + periodo (for two hours) · <b>since</b> + punto de inicio (since Monday, since 2019).</p>","tips":["En el habla, <b>I've been</b> suena <i>aivbin</i>: <i>I've been waiting</i> → <i>aivbinwéitin</i>.","En español decimos <i>llevo dos años trabajando</i>; en inglés: <i>I've been working for two years</i>, ¡nunca <i>I carry</i>!","<b>lately</b> y <b>recently</b> combinan muy bien con este tiempo: <i>I've been sleeping badly lately.</i>"],"vocab":[{"en":"I've been working here since 2020.","es":"Trabajo aquí desde 2020.","img":"u:photo-1713946598691-173f44f13dc9","v":"m","au":"90cd4a93a2"},{"en":"have been waiting for ages","es":"llevar una eternidad esperando","img":"u:photo-1743324754696-c636e1aed0b6","v":"f","au":"f4dcb11940"},{"en":"out of breath","es":"sin aliento","img":"u:photo-1571008887538-b36bb32f4571","v":"m","au":"744e99fb36"},{"en":"covered in paint","es":"cubierto de pintura","img":"u:photo-1688372199140-cade7ae820fe","v":"f","au":"89d98c92a8"},{"en":"puffy eyes","es":"ojos hinchados","img":"u:photo-1610354878912-08f1ab8ae913","v":"f","au":"99868cccee"},{"en":"It's been pouring.","es":"Ha estado lloviendo a cántaros.","img":"u:photo-1576514864427-f0809d2b66eb","v":"m","au":"d5a0eb2b1d"},{"en":"binge-watch","es":"ver series en maratón","img":"u:photo-1758525862392-1b25015f3fe1","v":"f","au":"d9762929af"},{"en":"lately","es":"últimamente","img":"u:photo-1550592704-6c76defa9985","v":"m","au":"38348d6534"},{"en":"all morning","es":"toda la mañana","img":"u:photo-1552650272-b8a34e21bc4b","v":"f","au":"03bc5f8e70"},{"en":"How long have you been…?","es":"¿Cuánto tiempo llevas…?","img":"#How long have you been…?","v":"m","au":"862c019ac7"},{"en":"sweaty","es":"sudado","img":"u:photo-1605296867304-46d5465a13f1","v":"m","au":"087a8a7002"},{"en":"burn out","es":"agotarse (por estrés)","img":"u:photo-1713946598534-a20fd25a4d1d","v":"f","au":"61baa587cc"}],"sentences":[{"en":"I've been working here since 2020.","es":"Trabajo aquí desde 2020.","img":"u:photo-1713946598691-173f44f13dc9","v":"m","au":"54e5029a05"},{"en":"You're out of breath. Have you been running?","es":"Estás sin aliento. ¿Has estado corriendo?","img":"u:photo-1571008887538-b36bb32f4571","v":"f","au":"d4e08180a8"},{"en":"It's been pouring all morning in Portland.","es":"Ha llovido a cántaros toda la mañana en Portland.","img":"u:photo-1576514864427-f0809d2b66eb","v":"m","au":"b922188450"},{"en":"How long have you been learning English?","es":"¿Cuánto tiempo llevas aprendiendo inglés?","img":"u:photo-1758685848208-e108b6af94cc","v":"f","au":"15a7924d22"},{"en":"We've been binge-watching that series all weekend.","es":"Hemos visto esa serie en maratón todo el fin de semana.","img":"u:photo-1758525862392-1b25015f3fe1","v":"m","au":"86b28e78bb"},{"en":"She's been feeling burned out lately.","es":"Se ha sentido agotada últimamente.","img":"u:photo-1713946598534-a20fd25a4d1d","v":"f","au":"4063731231"}],"fill":[{"s":"I've been living in Houston ___ 2018.","a":"since","o":["for","from"],"h":"punto de inicio","full":"I've been living in Houston since 2018.","au":"4f41c18780"},{"s":"They've been arguing ___ two hours.","a":"for","o":["since","during"],"h":"periodo de tiempo","full":"They've been arguing for two hours.","au":"ea17078ad5"},{"s":"Your hands are covered in paint! What have you ___ doing?","a":"been","o":["being","be"],"h":"have + been + -ing","full":"Your hands are covered in paint! What have you been doing?","au":"c76b7b358b"},{"s":"I've ___ this book three times.","a":"read","o":["been reading","reading"],"h":"resultado (cantidad)","full":"I've read this book three times.","au":"666f812f01"},{"s":"How long ___ you been waiting?","a":"have","o":["did","are"],"h":"pregunta de duración","full":"How long have you been waiting?","au":"371993ef3e"},{"s":"She's tired because she's been ___ all night.","a":"studying","o":["studied","study"],"h":"actividad reciente","full":"She's tired because she's been studying all night.","au":"f26924cb2f"}],"goal":{"en":"To talk about duration and recent activities with visible results using the present perfect continuous.","es":"Hablar de duración y de actividades recientes con resultados visibles usando el presente perfecto continuo."},"warm":[{"q":"How long have you been studying English?","au":"2ae6abc81b","es":"¿Cuánto tiempo llevas estudiando inglés?","ex":"I've been studying English for three years."},{"q":"What have you been doing lately to relax?","au":"33bd80a5f3","es":"¿Qué has estado haciendo últimamente para relajarte?","ex":"I've been doing yoga and reading novels."}],"reading":{"title":"Burnout: the silent epidemic","img":"u:photo-1713946598534-a20fd25a4d1d","text":"Are you tired all the time? Have you been sleeping badly lately? Have you been feeling irritated with your coworkers? If the answer is yes, you might be suffering from burnout. Doctors in the United States have been studying this problem for decades, and recent surveys show that more than half of American workers have been experiencing some symptoms. Take Michelle, a marketing manager from Philadelphia. \"I've been working at the same agency for six years,\" she explains. \"For the last eight months, I've been staying at the office until ten almost every night. I've been drinking five cups of coffee a day, and I haven't been exercising at all.\" Her friends noticed it first. \"You've been crying, haven't you?\" her sister asked one evening when she saw her puffy eyes. That conversation was a turning point. Michelle has been seeing a therapist since March, and she's been taking short walks during her lunch break. \"I've read three books about stress, and I've learned to say no,\" she says. Experts recommend regular breaks, physical activity and clear limits on work emails. Burnout is common, but it isn't permanent.","au":"3cf8580028","q":[{"s":"More than half of American workers have experienced symptoms of burnout.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Michelle has been working at the agency for eight months.","a":"no"},{"s":"She hasn't been exercising.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Her sister noticed her puffy eyes.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Michelle has been seeing a therapist since January.","a":"no"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"How long have you been living in your current home?","a":"I've been living here for five years.","es":"¿Cuánto tiempo llevas viviendo en tu casa actual?","qau":"c3ff7c0288","aau":"e48b0e4c92"},{"q":"What have you been doing lately to stay healthy?","a":"I've been walking every morning and eating less sugar.","es":"¿Qué has estado haciendo últimamente para mantenerte saludable?","qau":"b9c7bd7331","aau":"0a3be66814"},{"q":"You look tired. What have you been doing?","a":"I've been working on a big project all week.","es":"Te ves cansado. ¿Qué has estado haciendo?","qau":"729835f2ca","aau":"cf30400c49"},{"q":"How many books have you read this year?","a":"I've read four books this year.","es":"¿Cuántos libros has leído este año?","qau":"de9f60efd6","aau":"430242e0bb"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe 6 oraciones sobre tu vida actual: 3 con How long / for / since (duración) y 3 con evidencias visibles (ej. I'm sweaty because I've been running).","kw":["have been","for","since"],"n":6,"model":"I've been living in Miami since 2019. I've been working at a hotel for four years. I've been studying English for eight months. My hands are dirty because I've been gardening. I'm tired because I've been working nonstop. My eyes are red because I've been reading all night."}},{"id":"t6p2","topic":6,"part":2,"title":"Had been doing & stative verbs","es":"Had been doing y verbos de estado","acts":["learn","ppcMarathonApp","dialogue","fill","typeSentence","speak"],"tip":"<p>📐 <b>Pasado perfecto continuo</b>: <b>had been + -ing</b> = una acción que <b>duró</b> hasta un momento del pasado.</p>\n<p>⏪ <i>We <b>had been waiting</b> for two hours <b>when</b> the flight was finally canceled.</i><br><i>She was exhausted because she <b>had been working</b> nonstop.</i> (causa en el pasado)</p>\n<p>🔁 Compara: <b>has been doing</b> (hasta <u>ahora</u>) · <b>had been doing</b> (hasta un momento del <u>pasado</u>).</p>\n<p>🧊 <b>Verbos de estado</b> NO usan forma continua: <b>know, own, belong, believe, understand, like, love, hate, need, want, seem, prefer, mean</b>.<br>❌ <i>I've been knowing him for years.</i> → ✅ <i>I<b>'ve known</b> him for years.</i><br>❌ <i>She had been owning the house.</i> → ✅ <i>She <b>had owned</b> the house for ten years.</i></p>","tips":["<b>had been</b> en conversación suena <i>(I)d bin</i>: <i>I'd been waiting</i>.","Algunos verbos cambian: <b>think</b> (opinar = estado) vs. <b>I've been thinking about it</b> (pensar = proceso, ✅).","<b>have</b> de posesión es estado (<i>I've had this car for years</i>), pero <b>have</b> = comer/pasarla es acción (<i>We've been having fun</i>)."],"vocab":[{"en":"had been waiting","es":"había estado esperando","img":"u:photo-1582759780227-70da2727d8a5","v":"m","au":"db40a24ee6"},{"en":"had been saving up","es":"había estado ahorrando","img":"u:photo-1768839721719-c5ed97c1fd58","v":"f","au":"927bbcb02a"},{"en":"run out of gas","es":"quedarse sin gasolina","img":"u:photo-1599523170027-ee188424e94d","v":"m","au":"f2931e0649"},{"en":"exhausted","es":"agotado","img":"u:photo-1774050021349-d2024626b531","v":"f","au":"a09fc753f2"},{"en":"get promoted","es":"ser ascendido","img":"u:photo-1758518729466-827cd8293992","v":"f","au":"a9dab1aa0a"},{"en":"own","es":"ser dueño de","img":"u:photo-1741156386380-0236c72eb6f9","v":"m","au":"92d1e2c04c"},{"en":"belong to","es":"pertenecer a","img":"u:photo-1677445166019-4fa91a090e49","v":"m","au":"280affc2c2"},{"en":"believe","es":"creer","img":"u:photo-1676511128590-e4c715831068","v":"f","au":"39191242c0"},{"en":"recently","es":"recientemente","img":"u:photo-1676287566973-7e25f18f12a9","v":"f","au":"9f141496cd"},{"en":"nonstop","es":"sin parar","img":"u:photo-1618340338709-027f57b98a16","v":"m","au":"111010e4a7"},{"en":"train for a marathon","es":"entrenar para un maratón","img":"u:photo-1613936360976-8f35cf0e5461","v":"f","au":"809700e3e1"},{"en":"finally","es":"por fin","img":"u:photo-1766970096331-78c8af007a3b","v":"m","au":"fdd33a7619"}],"sentences":[{"en":"We had been waiting for two hours when the flight was canceled.","es":"Llevábamos dos horas esperando cuando cancelaron el vuelo.","img":"u:photo-1582759780227-70da2727d8a5","v":"m","au":"8e0f8a8039"},{"en":"She was exhausted because she had been working nonstop.","es":"Estaba agotada porque había estado trabajando sin parar.","img":"u:photo-1774050021349-d2024626b531","v":"f","au":"a19f1eaa3c"},{"en":"They had been saving up for years before they bought the house.","es":"Habían estado ahorrando durante años antes de comprar la casa.","img":"u:photo-1768839721719-c5ed97c1fd58","v":"m","au":"90f11053d1"},{"en":"I've known my best friend since high school.","es":"Conozco a mi mejor amigo desde la secundaria.","img":"u:photo-1543269865-cbf427effbad","v":"f","au":"744ffc5656"},{"en":"He had been training for months, so he finally finished the marathon.","es":"Había entrenado durante meses, así que por fin terminó el maratón.","img":"u:photo-1766970096331-78c8af007a3b","v":"m","au":"e5c02b481c"},{"en":"This watch has belonged to my family for a century.","es":"Este reloj ha pertenecido a mi familia durante un siglo.","img":"u:photo-1677445166019-4fa91a090e49","v":"f","au":"bd31f09466"}],"fill":[{"s":"We ___ been driving for hours when we ran out of gas.","a":"had","o":["have","were"],"h":"antes de otro momento pasado","full":"We had been driving for hours when we ran out of gas.","au":"8ec5fc0b68"},{"s":"I've ___ her since we were in college.","a":"known","o":["been knowing","knowing"],"h":"know = verbo de estado","full":"I've known her since we were in college.","au":"2f0c96c641"},{"s":"Her eyes were red. She had been ___.","a":"crying","o":["cried","cry"],"h":"had been + -ing","full":"Her eyes were red. She had been crying.","au":"41ff5fe4de"},{"s":"This house has ___ to my grandparents since 1965.","a":"belonged","o":["been belonging","belong"],"h":"belong = estado","full":"This house has belonged to my grandparents since 1965.","au":"ff34a4d926"},{"s":"How long had you been ___ there before you got promoted?","a":"working","o":["worked","work"],"h":"duración en el pasado","full":"How long had you been working there before you got promoted?","au":"be3c9d000c"},{"s":"I ___ been thinking about your offer for days.","a":"have","o":["had","am"],"h":"hasta ahora (presente)","full":"I have been thinking about your offer for days.","au":"fe5296d34d"}],"dialogue":{"title":"A fresh start in Portland","es":"Un nuevo comienzo en Portland","img":"u:photo-1641243745040-5cbf212d28ee","lines":[{"who":"Megan","v":"f","t":"So, how long have you been living in Portland?","au":"82f5dfc33d"},{"who":"Andrés","v":"m","t":"About eight months. Before that, I'd been living in Miami for almost ten years.","au":"2c3490fd33"},{"who":"Megan","v":"f","t":"Wow, that's a big change. Why did you move?","au":"744cba701c"},{"who":"Andrés","v":"m","t":"I'd been working nonstop at a bank, and I was totally burned out.","au":"7842a80b7c"},{"who":"Megan","v":"f","t":"I can imagine. And what have you been doing since you arrived?","au":"93da2ad60e"},{"who":"Andrés","v":"m","t":"I've been training for the Portland Marathon. I've already run three half marathons.","au":"b2fea2cfc2"},{"who":"Megan","v":"f","t":"Impressive! I've known a lot of runners, but you're the first one who moved for it.","au":"cb9f504883"},{"who":"Andrés","v":"m","t":"Ha! I'd been dreaming about cooler weather for years. Now I finally have it.","au":"9582382eac"}],"q":[{"q":"How long had Andrés been living in Miami?","a":"Almost ten years.","o":["Eight months.","Three years."]},{"q":"Why did he move?","a":"He was burned out from work.","o":["He got promoted.","His family moved."]},{"q":"What has he been doing in Portland?","a":"Training for a marathon.","o":["Working at a bank.","Looking for a house."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To describe actions that had been happening before a past moment and to avoid using stative verbs in continuous forms.","es":"Describir acciones que venían ocurriendo antes de un momento pasado y evitar los verbos de estado en forma continua."},"warm":[{"q":"Have you ever waited a very long time for something? What happened?","au":"ef3dad2dcf","es":"¿Alguna vez has esperado mucho tiempo por algo? ¿Qué pasó?","ex":"Yes, I had been waiting for my visa for a year when it finally arrived."},{"q":"What had you been doing before you started this course?","au":"1891df8d82","es":"¿Qué habías estado haciendo antes de empezar este curso?","ex":"I had been studying with apps, but I wasn't speaking."}],"reading":{"title":"Twenty-six miles of patience","img":"u:photo-1613936360976-8f35cf0e5461","text":"When Carlos Medina crossed the finish line of the Chicago Marathon last October, he burst into tears. He had been training for this moment for almost two years. Before that, he had never run more than five miles. \"I'd been working at a desk for fifteen years, and my doctor told me I needed to change my lifestyle,\" he remembers. So he started running three times a week before work. At first, it was terrible. He had been running for only ten minutes when he had to stop because he was out of breath. But he didn't give up. By the following spring, he had been running regularly for months and had lost twenty pounds. He also changed his diet and stopped eating fast food. The hardest part of the marathon came at mile twenty. \"I had been running for more than three hours, and my legs were exhausted. I believed I couldn't finish,\" he says. Then he saw his wife and daughter holding a sign with his name. \"I've known my wife for twenty years, and I've never seen her cry like that.\" Carlos finished in four hours and forty minutes. Now he's training for Boston.","au":"14a38d1ccf","q":[{"s":"Carlos had been training for almost two years.","a":"yes"},{"s":"He had run several marathons before Chicago.","a":"no"},{"s":"At first he had to stop after ten minutes.","a":"yes"},{"s":"At mile twenty he had been running for more than three hours.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Carlos isn't planning to run another marathon.","a":"no"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"What had you been doing before you started studying English?","a":"I had been working at a bank for ten years.","es":"¿Qué habías estado haciendo antes de empezar a estudiar inglés?","qau":"5f5258ca46","aau":"7ea9a2abd4"},{"q":"How long have you known your best friend?","a":"I've known her since high school.","es":"¿Hace cuánto conoces a tu mejor amigo?","qau":"5ead79f6b7","aau":"cd062389ac"},{"q":"Why were you tired yesterday?","a":"I was tired because I had been working all day.","es":"¿Por qué estabas cansado ayer?","qau":"f1bd62bc30","aau":"a63bb6c1cf"},{"q":"Have you ever run out of gas or battery? What had you been doing?","a":"Yes, I had been driving for hours and I forgot to check the tank.","es":"¿Alguna vez te has quedado sin gasolina o sin batería? ¿Qué habías estado haciendo?","qau":"d3291608ef","aau":"59e551caca"}],"hw":{"es":"Cuenta un logro personal (6 oraciones): qué habías estado haciendo antes, cuánto tiempo, y cómo te sentiste. Usa had been + -ing al menos 3 veces y un verbo de estado correctamente (know, own, believe…).","kw":["had been","for","know"],"n":6,"model":"Last year I finally got my driver's license. I had been taking classes for three months. I had been practicing every Saturday with my father. Before the test, I had been sleeping badly because I was nervous. I didn't believe I could pass. When I passed, I felt incredibly proud."}}]},{"n":7,"title":"Relative Clauses","es":"Cláusulas relativas","cover":"u:photo-1531058020387-3be344556be6","parts":[{"id":"t7p1","topic":7,"part":1,"title":"Who, which, whose, where, when","es":"Who, which, whose, where, when","acts":["learn","rcTabooCards","matchLines","fill","quizShow","speak"],"tip":"<p>Las <b>cláusulas relativas especificativas</b> (defining) dicen <b>exactamente de quién o de qué</b> hablamos. No llevan comas.</p>\n<p>👤 <b>who</b> (o <b>that</b>) → personas: <i>The woman <b>who</b> called you is my landlord.</i><br>📦 <b>which</b> (o <b>that</b>) → cosas: <i>This is the app <b>which/that</b> saved my business.</i><br>🔑 <b>whose</b> → posesión (cuyo): <i>He's the neighbor <b>whose</b> dog barks all night.</i><br>📍 <b>where</b> → lugares: <i>That's the café <b>where</b> we met.</i><br>📅 <b>when</b> → momentos: <i>I remember the day <b>when</b> I arrived in New York.</i><br>❓ <b>why</b> → razones: <i>That's the reason <b>why</b> I quit.</i></p>\n<p>⚠️ No repitas el sujeto: ❌ <i>The man who <b>he</b> lives next door</i> → ✅ <i>The man who lives next door</i>.</p>","tips":["<b>that</b> es el más común en inglés hablado de EE. UU. para personas y cosas en cláusulas sin comas.","<b>whose</b> suena igual que <b>who's</b> (<i>júz</i>), pero <i>who's</i> = who is.","Úsalas para definir palabras en inglés sin traducir: <i>A landlord is a person who rents out property.</i>"],"vocab":[{"en":"who","es":"que / quien (personas)","img":"u:photo-1517457373958-b7bdd4587205","v":"f","au":"2b970fca8d"},{"en":"which","es":"que / el cual (cosas)","img":"u:photo-1703675858673-56aab77ccbec","v":"m","au":"27eb97bc08"},{"en":"whose","es":"cuyo / cuya","img":"u:photo-1672402700956-d7ae87a0cdb2","v":"f","au":"85feab26ff"},{"en":"where","es":"donde (lugares)","img":"u:photo-1477959858617-67f85cf4f1df","v":"m","au":"d51db62523"},{"en":"when","es":"cuando (momentos)","img":"u:photo-1633526543814-9718c8922b7a","v":"f","au":"84bfacfac4"},{"en":"landlord","es":"arrendador / casero","img":"u:photo-1722487631997-cf1e0f92c2c4","v":"m","au":"cb04d07db7"},{"en":"roommate","es":"compañero de apartamento","img":"u:photo-1783780933273-392188f83694","v":"f","au":"454a3a2485"},{"en":"neighborhood","es":"barrio / vecindario","img":"u:photo-1749292177172-66edfd44e7cc","v":"m","au":"1991973d49"},{"en":"the person in charge","es":"la persona a cargo","img":"u:photo-1542744173-8e7e53415bb0","v":"f","au":"cfc6ce68ef"},{"en":"device","es":"dispositivo","img":"u:photo-1703675858673-56aab77ccbec","v":"m","au":"101545c76c"},{"en":"job applicant","es":"candidato (a un empleo)","img":"u:photo-1672380135241-c024f7fbfa13","v":"f","au":"a182364702"},{"en":"the reason why","es":"la razón por la cual","img":"u:photo-1758873269108-7c03a92f7586","v":"m","au":"f4c9930164"}],"sentences":[{"en":"A landlord is a person who rents out an apartment.","es":"Un casero es una persona que alquila un apartamento.","img":"u:photo-1722487631997-cf1e0f92c2c4","v":"m","au":"2c0fdfef09"},{"en":"This is the app that helped me find a roommate.","es":"Esta es la app que me ayudó a encontrar compañero de apartamento.","img":"u:photo-1592890288564-76628a30a657","v":"f","au":"f2ab060995"},{"en":"She's the coworker whose idea won the contest.","es":"Ella es la compañera cuya idea ganó el concurso.","img":"u:photo-1758873269108-7c03a92f7586","v":"f","au":"fee7f5d24b"},{"en":"That's the neighborhood where I grew up.","es":"Ese es el barrio donde crecí.","img":"u:photo-1749292177172-66edfd44e7cc","v":"m","au":"c1bbf5bfc0"},{"en":"I'll never forget the day when I arrived in New York.","es":"Nunca olvidaré el día en que llegué a Nueva York.","img":"u:photo-1628947733273-cdae71c9bfd3","v":"f","au":"afa417e523"},{"en":"The reason why I called is to invite you.","es":"La razón por la que llamé es para invitarte.","img":"u:photo-1758873268528-af4613d099b6","v":"m","au":"102c0c25a6"}],"fill":[{"s":"A plumber is a person ___ fixes pipes and leaks.","a":"who","o":["which","where"],"h":"persona","full":"A plumber is a person who fixes pipes and leaks.","au":"559d9595fb"},{"s":"This is the laptop ___ I bought in Seattle.","a":"that","o":["who","whose"],"h":"cosa","full":"This is the laptop that I bought in Seattle.","au":"84664812f6"},{"s":"That's the guy ___ car was towed last night.","a":"whose","o":["who's","who"],"h":"posesión (cuyo)","full":"That's the guy whose car was towed last night.","au":"ab233ff355"},{"s":"Do you know a restaurant ___ we can eat after 11 p.m.?","a":"where","o":["which","when"],"h":"lugar","full":"Do you know a restaurant where we can eat after 11 p.m.?","au":"b2fa1bf76f"},{"s":"2020 was the year ___ everything changed.","a":"when","o":["where","which"],"h":"momento","full":"2020 was the year when everything changed.","au":"f155d6bde6"},{"s":"The candidate ___ we interviewed yesterday was brilliant.","a":"who","o":["whose","where"],"h":"persona (objeto)","full":"The candidate who we interviewed yesterday was brilliant.","au":"5234d68406"}],"goal":{"en":"To define people, things, places and times precisely with defining relative clauses.","es":"Definir con precisión personas, cosas, lugares y momentos con cláusulas relativas especificativas."},"warm":[{"q":"Who is a person who has inspired you?","au":"a66a99979a","es":"¿Quién es una persona que te ha inspirado?","ex":"My grandmother, who raised six children alone, has inspired me."},{"q":"What is a place where you feel completely relaxed?","au":"c9a3ba285c","es":"¿Cuál es un lugar donde te sientes completamente relajado?","ex":"The beach is the place where I feel completely relaxed."}],"reading":{"title":"Finding the perfect roommate in New York","img":"u:photo-1783780933273-392188f83694","text":"Finding an apartment in New York is hard, but finding a roommate who you can actually live with is even harder. When Isabel moved from Puerto Rico to Brooklyn, she used an app that matches people according to their habits. \"I was looking for someone who was clean, quiet and didn't smoke,\" she says. The app asked questions that most people never think about: What time do you go to bed? How often do you have guests? Is there a neighborhood where you'd prefer to live? After two weeks, Isabel met Hannah, a nurse whose schedule was the opposite of hers. \"She works the night shift, which means we almost never need the bathroom at the same time,\" Isabel laughs. Their landlord, a retired teacher who lives on the first floor, was happy too. \"The tenants I had before were always fighting,\" he says. Of course, there were problems. The day when Hannah's cat ate Isabel's plant, they had a serious conversation. But they set some rules that both of them respect. \"The reason why it works is communication,\" Hannah explains. \"A good roommate is someone who tells you when something bothers them.\"","au":"021966e6b2","q":[{"s":"Isabel moved to Brooklyn from Puerto Rico.","a":"yes"},{"s":"She wanted a roommate who smoked.","a":"no"},{"s":"Hannah works the night shift.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The landlord lives on the top floor.","a":"no"},{"s":"Hannah thinks communication is the key.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"How would you describe a good boss?","a":"A good boss is someone who listens and gives clear feedback.","es":"¿Cómo describirías a un buen jefe?","qau":"b2cd3d9cb1","aau":"6605347891"},{"q":"What is an app that you can't live without?","a":"An app that I can't live without is Google Maps.","es":"¿Cuál es una app sin la que no puedes vivir?","qau":"c004ef84b4","aau":"c15427b34d"},{"q":"Can you describe a place where you'd love to live?","a":"I'd love to live in a neighborhood where I can walk everywhere.","es":"¿Puedes describir un lugar donde te encantaría vivir?","qau":"8e82ce10ca","aau":"1682a3ab5f"},{"q":"Do you remember a day when everything went wrong?","a":"Yes, the day when I lost my passport in Orlando.","es":"¿Recuerdas un día en que todo salió mal?","qau":"d00fc7bebf","aau":"045b4d59f8"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe 6 definiciones de palabras en inglés como en un diccionario, usando who, which/that, whose, where y when (ej. A landlord is a person who…).","kw":["who","which","whose","where","when"],"n":6,"model":"A landlord is a person who rents out a house or an apartment. A charger is a device that gives power to your phone. An orphan is a child whose parents have died. A gym is a place where people exercise. A deadline is the moment when you must finish a task. A roommate is someone who shares an apartment with you."}},{"id":"t7p2","topic":7,"part":2,"title":"Commas, prepositions & which","es":"Comas, preposiciones y which","acts":["learn","rcFusionLab","sort","fill","speed","speak"],"tip":"<p>✂️ <b>Explicativas (non-defining)</b>: dan información <b>extra</b> y van <b>entre comas</b>. Aquí <b>NO</b> se puede usar <i>that</i>.<br><i>My sister<b>, who lives in Boston,</b> is a nurse.</i> (solo tengo una hermana)</p>\n<p>🔄 <b>which</b> puede referirse a <b>toda la oración anterior</b>: <i>The flight was canceled<b>, which</b> ruined our plans.</i> (lo cual)</p>\n<p>🫥 <b>Omitir el pronombre</b>: en las especificativas, si el pronombre es <b>objeto</b> (va seguido de otro sujeto), puedes quitarlo:<br><i>The people (<s>who</s>) I work with are great.</i> · Pero NO si es sujeto: <i>The man <b>who</b> called…</i></p>\n<p>📎 <b>Preposiciones</b>: informal al final → <i>the city I live <b>in</b></i> · formal antes del pronombre → <i>the city <b>in which</b> I live</i> · <i>the people <b>with whom</b> I work</i>.</p>\n<p>🔢 Cuantificadores: <b>most of whom, some of which, all of which, none of whom</b>.</p>","tips":["Las comas cambian el significado: <i>My brother who lives in LA</i> (tengo varios) vs. <i>My brother, who lives in LA,</i> (solo uno).","Al leer en voz alta, las comas son <b>pausas</b>: <i>My boss | who's from Texas | loves barbecue.</i>","<b>whom</b> es formal; en conversación se usa <i>who</i> o se omite: <i>the man (who) I met</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":", which surprised everyone","es":", lo cual sorprendió a todos","img":"u:photo-1501386761578-eac5c94b800a","v":"f","au":"bc6d5ab0d6"},{"en":"the city in which","es":"la ciudad en la que","img":"u:photo-1500111709600-7761aa8216c7","v":"m","au":"eee1b88424"},{"en":"the people I work with","es":"la gente con la que trabajo","img":"u:photo-1603201667230-bd139210db18","v":"f","au":"2010991d99"},{"en":"most of whom","es":"la mayoría de los cuales","img":"u:photo-1587825140708-dfaf72ae4b04","v":"m","au":"02a46c4147"},{"en":"whom","es":"a quien (formal)","img":"u:photo-1649019489428-70f505daacd6","v":"f","au":"d5ce13c969"},{"en":"the house where I grew up","es":"la casa donde crecí","img":"u:photo-1661332626584-2ef99ddd6794","v":"m","au":"96f719fbd7"},{"en":"my sister, who lives in Boston","es":"mi hermana, que vive en Boston","img":"u:photo-1766381854360-e4ab2f8f7291","v":"f","au":"4667b8ebd0"},{"en":"which is why","es":"razón por la cual","img":"u:photo-1758873269108-7c03a92f7586","v":"m","au":"077880479d"},{"en":"all of which","es":"todo lo cual / todos los cuales","img":"u:photo-1583521214690-73421a1829a9","v":"f","au":"3a73709fbb"},{"en":"the moment when","es":"el momento en que","img":"u:photo-1590632396158-a5765ff11bda","v":"m","au":"06db6a01c2"},{"en":"whose name I forget","es":"cuyo nombre olvido","img":"u:photo-1760078083438-c5b32344c2da","v":"f","au":"3573514cd7"},{"en":"by which time","es":"para ese entonces","img":"u:photo-1690664465052-32387a465a92","v":"m","au":"d0f63e5a26"}],"sentences":[{"en":"My sister, who lives in Boston, is a nurse.","es":"Mi hermana, que vive en Boston, es enfermera.","img":"u:photo-1766381854360-e4ab2f8f7291","v":"f","au":"d3f452635f"},{"en":"The flight was canceled, which ruined our plans.","es":"Cancelaron el vuelo, lo cual arruinó nuestros planes.","img":"u:photo-1764251105292-7a495215a398","v":"m","au":"20874f61c3"},{"en":"The people I work with are really supportive.","es":"Las personas con las que trabajo me apoyan mucho.","img":"u:photo-1603201667230-bd139210db18","v":"f","au":"c7cb5487ed"},{"en":"San Francisco is the city in which I started my company.","es":"San Francisco es la ciudad en la que fundé mi empresa.","img":"u:photo-1500111709600-7761aa8216c7","v":"m","au":"9983712b28"},{"en":"We hired ten interns, most of whom were bilingual.","es":"Contratamos diez practicantes, la mayoría de los cuales eran bilingües.","img":"u:photo-1587825140708-dfaf72ae4b04","v":"f","au":"4dbb335832"},{"en":"I missed the bus, which is why I was late.","es":"Perdí el bus, razón por la cual llegué tarde.","img":"u:photo-1623975522495-82ea8c48de56","v":"m","au":"7ed1ab581b"}],"fill":[{"s":"My boss, ___ is from Texas, loves barbecue.","a":"who","o":["that","which"],"h":"non-defining: no se usa that","full":"My boss, who is from Texas, loves barbecue.","au":"80d66d7632"},{"s":"They canceled the concert, ___ disappointed thousands of fans.","a":"which","o":["that","what"],"h":"which = lo cual","full":"They canceled the concert, which disappointed thousands of fans.","au":"b6ec8dcb24"},{"s":"The apartment ___ I'm renting has a great view.","a":"that","o":["what","whose"],"h":"pronombre objeto (también se puede omitir)","full":"The apartment that I'm renting has a great view.","au":"5acc140d85"},{"s":"This is the company for ___ I worked in Chicago.","a":"which","o":["that","where"],"h":"preposición + which","full":"This is the company for which I worked in Chicago.","au":"7a1bf5565c"},{"s":"We met fifty candidates, most of ___ had experience.","a":"whom","o":["who","them"],"h":"most of whom","full":"We met fifty candidates, most of whom had experience.","au":"e10898e4f4"},{"s":"The house ___ I grew up in was sold last year.","a":"that","o":["where","what"],"h":"preposición al final","full":"The house that I grew up in was sold last year.","au":"1e122eb770"}],"sort":{"cats":["Defining","Non-defining"],"items":[{"w":"The man who called you is my landlord.","c":"Defining","au":"25c40b2917"},{"w":"The app that I use is free.","c":"Defining","au":"c82dd43c12"},{"w":"People who exercise sleep better.","c":"Defining","au":"739814cdf9"},{"w":"That's the café where we met.","c":"Defining","au":"762af71dd3"},{"w":"The book I'm reading is great.","c":"Defining","au":"b743046415"},{"w":"My mom, who is 70, still runs.","c":"Non-defining","au":"f216159fcd"},{"w":"Chicago, where I studied, is windy.","c":"Non-defining","au":"93d7d4e10e"},{"w":"He quit, which surprised everyone.","c":"Non-defining","au":"1512589c81"},{"w":"Our CEO, whose name is Lisa, resigned.","c":"Non-defining","au":"e5ff779235"},{"w":"The Grand Canyon, which I visited in May, is huge.","c":"Non-defining","au":"511eaa42fc"}]},"goal":{"en":"To add extra information with non-defining clauses and use prepositions and which to refer to a whole idea.","es":"Añadir información extra con cláusulas explicativas y usar preposiciones y which para referirse a una idea completa."},"warm":[{"q":"Can you describe the city where you grew up?","au":"c13acab09b","es":"¿Puedes describir la ciudad donde creciste?","ex":"The city where I grew up is small, which means everybody knows each other."},{"q":"Who is a person you work or study with that you really admire?","au":"858eace439","es":"¿Quién es una persona con la que trabajas o estudias y que admiras mucho?","ex":"My coworker Ana, who speaks four languages, is the person I admire most."}],"reading":{"title":"San Francisco: a city of reinventions","img":"u:photo-1500111709600-7761aa8216c7","text":"San Francisco, which sits on a small peninsula in Northern California, has reinvented itself many times. In 1848, gold was discovered nearby, which turned a village of about 1,000 people into a city of 25,000 in just two years. Most of the newcomers, many of whom came from China, Chile and Mexico, never found gold. Instead, they opened shops, restaurants and banks. In 1906, a terrible earthquake destroyed most of the city, after which residents rebuilt it in less than ten years. Later, in the 1960s, the city became the center of a cultural movement whose music and ideas spread around the world. Today San Francisco is famous for technology. Many of the companies with which we communicate every day were founded in the area, which is why rents are among the highest in the country. Of course, not everyone is happy about this. Some longtime residents, most of whom can no longer afford to live there, feel that the city has lost its soul. Others argue that change is exactly what has always made San Francisco special. Either way, the city in which so many dreams began continues to surprise the world.","au":"eaa776d86e","q":[{"s":"The discovery of gold made the population grow quickly.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Most newcomers became rich from gold.","a":"no"},{"s":"After the 1906 earthquake, the city was rebuilt in less than ten years.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Rents in San Francisco are among the lowest in the country.","a":"no"},{"s":"All longtime residents are happy about the changes.","a":"no"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Can you describe your hometown with a non-defining clause?","a":"My hometown, which is near the mountains, is very quiet.","es":"¿Puedes describir tu ciudad natal con una cláusula explicativa?","qau":"e5730ee1fd","aau":"de0712acbf"},{"q":"Who is someone you work with that you admire?","a":"My manager, who started as an intern, is the person I admire most.","es":"¿Quién es alguien con quien trabajas y que admiras?","qau":"195ee91f68","aau":"07eee5f738"},{"q":"What is something that happened recently, which surprised you?","a":"My brother got married, which surprised everyone.","es":"¿Qué pasó recientemente que te sorprendió?","qau":"2c30c07eff","aau":"cc2a324cae"},{"q":"What is the city in which you would most like to live?","a":"The city in which I'd most like to live is Vancouver.","es":"¿Cuál es la ciudad en la que más te gustaría vivir?","qau":"d23137eacb","aau":"ec39e75b93"}],"hw":{"es":"Describe tu ciudad o una ciudad que conozcas en 6 oraciones. Usa al menos 2 cláusulas con comas (who/which), una con which = lo cual, y una con preposición + which/whom.","kw":["which","who","in which","whom"],"n":6,"model":"Chicago, which is on Lake Michigan, is my favorite city. My cousin, who lives downtown, works as an architect. The city is very cold in winter, which is why people love summer there. The neighborhood in which she lives has great restaurants. The people with whom she works are from all over the world. Most of the buildings, many of which are very tall, are beautiful."}}]},{"n":8,"title":"Tag Questions","es":"Preguntas coletilla","cover":"u:photo-1758525223149-db03363e43e7","parts":[{"id":"t8p1","topic":8,"part":1,"title":"Checking information with tags","es":"Confirmar información con coletillas","acts":["learn","tagPingPong","fill","sort","unscramble","speak"],"tip":"<p>Una <b>tag question</b> (pregunta coletilla) es la pequeña pregunta al final de una oración: equivale a <i>¿verdad?</i>, <i>¿no?</i>, <i>¿cierto?</i> en español.</p>\n<p>📐 <b>Regla de oro:</b> oración <b>positiva</b> → coletilla <b>negativa</b>; oración <b>negativa</b> → coletilla <b>positiva</b>.<br>\n<i>You <b>are</b> tired, <b>aren't</b> you?</i> · <i>You <b>aren't</b> tired, <b>are</b> you?</i></p>\n<p>🔧 La coletilla repite el <b>auxiliar</b> de la oración (be, have, can, will, should…). Si no hay auxiliar, usa <b>do / does / did</b>:<br>\n<i>She <b>works</b> remotely, <b>doesn't</b> she?</i> · <i>They <b>called</b>, <b>didn't</b> they?</i></p>\n<p>👤 La coletilla siempre usa un <b>pronombre</b>: <i>Your boss</i> → <b>he/she</b>; <i>The meeting</i> → <b>it</b>; <i>There is…</i> → <b>isn't there?</b></p>\n<p>⚠️ Cuidado con <b>'s</b>: puede ser <b>is</b> o <b>has</b>. <i>She's finished, <b>hasn't</b> she?</i> (has finished) · <i>She's tired, <b>isn't</b> she?</i> (is tired)</p>","tips":["Las coletillas se dicen <b>rápido y unidas</b>: <i>isn't it?</i> suena casi <i>ízenit</i>.","<b>won't</b> (will not) suena <i>uóunt</i>, diferente de <b>want</b> (<i>uánt</i>).","En <b>didn't they?</b> la 't' de <i>didn't</i> casi desaparece: <i>dídən dey</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"It's freezing, isn't it?","es":"Hace un frío terrible, ¿verdad?","img":"u:photo-1583170492868-dd617c96fdee","v":"m","au":"1cc2dbc1b5"},{"en":"You've met Laura, haven't you?","es":"Ya conoces a Laura, ¿no?","img":"u:photo-1491438590914-bc09fcaaf77a","v":"f","au":"41dd7c7294"},{"en":"She can't drive, can she?","es":"Ella no sabe manejar, ¿o sí?","img":"u:photo-1578041262130-633307b3bfd6","v":"f","au":"876ab4e3a6"},{"en":"They didn't call back, did they?","es":"No devolvieron la llamada, ¿cierto?","img":"u:photo-1691380302295-b19eda6ae52b","v":"m","au":"2ee753f5e5"},{"en":"He'll be late again, won't he?","es":"Va a llegar tarde otra vez, ¿no?","img":"u:photo-1495704907664-81f74a7efd9b","v":"m","au":"9147622dab"},{"en":"We should leave now, shouldn't we?","es":"Deberíamos irnos ya, ¿no?","img":"u:photo-1713947505221-8a11da8aa744","v":"f","au":"6c0ca90b3d"},{"en":"The flight was delayed, wasn't it?","es":"El vuelo se retrasó, ¿no?","img":"u:photo-1746125047145-d6698eef563a","v":"m","au":"5349c14c44"},{"en":"You don't take sugar, do you?","es":"No tomas azúcar, ¿verdad?","img":"u:photo-1709651808265-977ed7ef78c6","v":"f","au":"4f037bb5a0"},{"en":"She works remotely, doesn't she?","es":"Ella trabaja a distancia, ¿cierto?","img":"u:photo-1524508762098-fd966ffb6ef9","v":"f","au":"6772968cb1"},{"en":"There's a catch, isn't there?","es":"Hay truco, ¿no? (algo escondido)","img":"u:photo-1758523418784-efd368723c42","v":"m","au":"9c9d47307f"},{"en":"to double-check","es":"verificar dos veces","img":"u:photo-1758876201660-103984519266","v":"f","au":"937e3441ca"},{"en":"to break the ice","es":"romper el hielo","img":"u:photo-1604881988758-f76ad2f7aac1","v":"m","au":"fbe723f667"}],"sentences":[{"en":"The report is due on Friday, isn't it?","es":"El informe se entrega el viernes, ¿no?","img":"u:photo-1676287566973-7e25f18f12a9","v":"f","au":"22c6bf99f7"},{"en":"You haven't seen my charger, have you?","es":"No has visto mi cargador, ¿o sí?","img":"u:photo-1592890288564-76628a30a657","v":"m","au":"56efcdfddb"},{"en":"Your brother lives in Seattle, doesn't he?","es":"Tu hermano vive en Seattle, ¿cierto?","img":"u:photo-1502175353174-a7a70e73b362","v":"f","au":"5235fa77a9"},{"en":"We met at the conference, didn't we?","es":"Nos conocimos en la conferencia, ¿no?","img":"u:photo-1531058020387-3be344556be6","v":"m","au":"d98dc9e2d4"},{"en":"The rent has gone up again, hasn't it?","es":"El arriendo subió otra vez, ¿no?","img":"u:photo-1760898002480-a89156856aa0","v":"f","au":"0fabc66349"},{"en":"She can speak three languages, can't she?","es":"Ella habla tres idiomas, ¿no?","img":"u:photo-1713947506048-80f76419b2fe","v":"m","au":"548241d9e6"}],"fill":[{"s":"You're from Chicago, ___ you?","a":"aren't","o":["don't","isn't"],"h":"are → aren't","full":"You're from Chicago, aren't you?","au":"1c14e29fe6"},{"s":"She works in finance, ___ she?","a":"doesn't","o":["isn't","don't"],"h":"presente simple con she → doesn't","full":"She works in finance, doesn't she?","au":"9555d3e388"},{"s":"They've already signed the contract, ___ they?","a":"haven't","o":["didn't","aren't"],"h":"have signed (present perfect) → haven't","full":"They've already signed the contract, haven't they?","au":"6d0fcae1f1"},{"s":"He couldn't find a parking spot, ___ he?","a":"could","o":["couldn't","did"],"h":"oración negativa → coletilla positiva","full":"He couldn't find a parking spot, could he?","au":"844451c671"},{"s":"We'll need a bigger budget, ___ we?","a":"won't","o":["will","don't"],"h":"will → won't","full":"We'll need a bigger budget, won't we?","au":"f4baa792b6"},{"s":"Your manager approved the trip, ___ she?","a":"didn't","o":["wasn't","hasn't"],"h":"pasado simple sin auxiliar → didn't","full":"Your manager approved the trip, didn't she?","au":"548c350470"}],"sort":{"cats":["do / does / did","be","have / has"],"items":[{"w":"You live downtown","c":"do / does / did","au":"63645360ea"},{"w":"She called the client","c":"do / does / did","au":"e538f57ed0"},{"w":"He drinks too much coffee","c":"do / does / did","au":"14a0995e78"},{"w":"It's a great deal","c":"be","au":"4225f7a9e3"},{"w":"They were at the gym","c":"be","au":"37d6a8e0a6"},{"w":"I'm not late","c":"be","au":"5e99b5d9aa"},{"w":"We've met before","c":"have / has","au":"5d6e296ac3"},{"w":"She's finished the slides","c":"have / has","au":"915d0b9e5f"},{"w":"They haven't paid yet","c":"have / has","au":"f28339d45b"}]},"goal":{"en":"To check information and keep a conversation going with tag questions.","es":"Confirmar información y mantener una conversación con preguntas coletilla."},"warm":[{"q":"How do you usually break the ice with a new coworker?","au":"3d09095723","es":"¿Cómo sueles romper el hielo con un compañero de trabajo nuevo?","ex":"I usually ask about their weekend or offer them a coffee."},{"q":"What do you say when you want someone to agree with you?","au":"c10c964481","es":"¿Qué dices cuando quieres que alguien esté de acuerdo contigo?","ex":"I say something like 'It's a great idea, isn't it?'"}],"reading":{"title":"The art of small talk","img":"u:photo-1604881988758-f76ad2f7aac1","text":"When Valeria moved from Lima to Minneapolis for a marketing job, her English was already strong, but something felt off. Her sentences were correct, yet conversations at the office died after a few seconds. Her manager, Greg, gave her some advice that changed everything: \"Use more tag questions.\" At first she was confused. Then she started listening carefully at the coffee machine. People constantly said things like \"It's freezing today, isn't it?\" or \"You've worked with Priya before, haven't you?\" Valeria realized that these little questions are not really about information. They are invitations. They show that you want the other person to join in, agree, or add something. She began practicing them on purpose. In meetings she would say, \"We can still meet the deadline, can't we?\" and suddenly her colleagues were explaining their ideas instead of just nodding. She also learned to be careful with the auxiliary: \"She works remotely, doesn't she?\" not \"isn't she?\" Six months later, Valeria leads her own small team. She says that tag questions made her sound less like a textbook and more like a person who wants to connect.","au":"cc0da0edc4","q":[{"s":"Valeria's English was weak when she arrived in Minneapolis.","a":"no"},{"s":"Greg suggested using more tag questions.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Valeria noticed tag questions near the coffee machine.","a":"yes"},{"s":"According to the text, tag questions are mainly about getting new information.","a":"no"},{"s":"Valeria now leads a small team.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"It's a beautiful day, isn't it?","a":"Yes, it is. It's perfect for a walk.","es":"Es un día hermoso, ¿verdad?","qau":"bb397d6b70","aau":"dd833b188c"},{"q":"You've been to New York, haven't you?","a":"Yes, I have. I went there two years ago.","es":"Has estado en Nueva York, ¿no?","qau":"7547339a7c","aau":"c568312eea"},{"q":"You don't work on Saturdays, do you?","a":"No, I don't. I only work Monday to Friday.","es":"No trabajas los sábados, ¿cierto?","qau":"d746886102","aau":"14a7900517"},{"q":"Your boss speaks Spanish, doesn't she?","a":"Yes, she does. She lived in Mexico for years.","es":"Tu jefa habla español, ¿no?","qau":"f788b3a514","aau":"6a6891af01"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe un pequeño diálogo de 'small talk' en la oficina (6 líneas) usando al menos 5 tag questions con auxiliares diferentes (is, have, do, did, will, can).","kw":["isn't","haven't","doesn't","didn't"],"n":6,"model":"A: Busy morning, isn't it? B: Very! You've seen the new schedule, haven't you? A: Yes. Our boss doesn't like Mondays, does she? B: No, she doesn't. The client called yesterday, didn't he? A: He did. We'll finish on time, won't we? B: Of course we can do it."}},{"id":"t8p2","topic":8,"part":2,"title":"Tricky tags and intonation","es":"Coletillas especiales y entonación","acts":["learn","tagPitchDetective","dialogue","listenChoose","typeSentence","speak"],"tip":"<p>Hay coletillas <b>especiales</b> que no siguen la regla normal:</p>\n<p>🙋 <b>I am</b> → <b>aren't I?</b> <i>(nunca \"amn't I\")</i>: <i>I'm invited, <b>aren't I</b>?</i><br>\n🤝 <b>Let's</b> → <b>shall we?</b>: <i>Let's start, <b>shall we</b>?</i><br>\n👉 <b>Imperativo</b> → <b>will you? / would you? / can you?</b>: <i>Close the door, <b>will you</b>?</i> · <i>Don't tell anyone, <b>will you</b>?</i></p>\n<p>🚫 Palabras <b>negativas</b> (<b>never, nobody, nothing, hardly, rarely, no one</b>) hacen la oración negativa → coletilla <b>positiva</b>: <i>You <b>never</b> complain, <b>do</b> you?</i><br>\n👥 <b>nobody / somebody / everyone</b> → <b>they</b>; <b>nothing / everything</b> → <b>it</b>.</p>\n<p>🎵 <b>Entonación:</b> ↘ <b>descendente</b> = estás seguro y solo buscas que te den la razón. ↗ <b>ascendente</b> = de verdad no sabes y preguntas.</p>","tips":["Para confirmar algo que ya sabes, baja la voz al final: <i>Nice day, ↘isn't it?</i>","Si de verdad dudas, sube la voz: <i>You've paid, ↗haven't you?</i>","<b>shall we</b> se dice suave y unido: <i>shəl uí</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"I'm right, aren't I?","es":"Tengo razón, ¿no?","img":"u:photo-1590650213165-c1fef80648c4","v":"f","au":"55d7c0b17e"},{"en":"Let's grab lunch, shall we?","es":"Vamos a almorzar, ¿sí?","img":"u:photo-1568992688065-536aad8a12f6","v":"m","au":"8f124066b5"},{"en":"Pass me the file, will you?","es":"Pásame el archivo, ¿sí?","img":"u:photo-1758518729912-bf3a84c400e0","v":"f","au":"18ce784a6d"},{"en":"Don't be late, will you?","es":"No llegues tarde, ¿vale?","img":"u:photo-1495704907664-81f74a7efd9b","v":"m","au":"16efd1dafe"},{"en":"Nobody noticed, did they?","es":"Nadie se dio cuenta, ¿verdad?","img":"u:photo-1758876019043-cedb0b6f56ea","v":"m","au":"0e18a68db6"},{"en":"Nothing happened, did it?","es":"No pasó nada, ¿cierto?","img":"u:photo-1659356576489-856f824d68a2","v":"f","au":"f6dc105e01"},{"en":"You've never been to Alaska, have you?","es":"Nunca has ido a Alaska, ¿o sí?","img":"u:photo-1673114819432-1aa36952dd3e","v":"f","au":"23f7980b88"},{"en":"Everyone's here, aren't they?","es":"Ya están todos, ¿no?","img":"u:photo-1431540015161-0bf868a2d407","v":"m","au":"116f687d4d"},{"en":"rising intonation","es":"entonación ascendente (pregunta real)","img":"#↗ real question","v":"f","au":"50fb23c646"},{"en":"falling intonation","es":"entonación descendente (solo confirmas)","img":"#↘ just confirming","v":"m","au":"a4b9638688"},{"en":"to seek confirmation","es":"buscar confirmación","img":"u:photo-1631203928521-bde1e727e8b7","v":"f","au":"ec2ba912c4"},{"en":"That's a fair point.","es":"Ese es un punto válido.","img":"u:photo-1531537571171-a707bf2683da","v":"m","au":"389a788724"}],"sentences":[{"en":"I'm invited to the launch, aren't I?","es":"Estoy invitado al lanzamiento, ¿no?","img":"u:photo-1730134322176-862f1cf9bc9f","v":"m","au":"31e5b9d809"},{"en":"Let's not argue about it, shall we?","es":"No discutamos por eso, ¿sí?","img":"u:photo-1551801679-787f2accc402","v":"f","au":"89394fe212"},{"en":"Close the door on your way out, will you?","es":"Cierra la puerta al salir, ¿sí?","img":"u:photo-1632858265907-961f1454ccf6","v":"m","au":"36dfbd17ab"},{"en":"Nobody has complained yet, have they?","es":"Nadie se ha quejado todavía, ¿verdad?","img":"u:photo-1771979788419-84487b12e3a0","v":"f","au":"63b7a4aaec"},{"en":"Somebody left the lights on, didn't they?","es":"Alguien dejó las luces encendidas, ¿no?","img":"u:photo-1542081403278-ba5973c25c7a","v":"m","au":"2ca0ff3284"},{"en":"You hardly ever take a day off, do you?","es":"Casi nunca te tomas un día libre, ¿verdad?","img":"u:photo-1544717302-de2939b7ef71","v":"f","au":"2713215ebc"}],"fill":[{"s":"I'm on the guest list, ___ I?","a":"aren't","o":["am not","amn't"],"h":"I am → aren't I","full":"I'm on the guest list, aren't I?","au":"6f7c08a761"},{"s":"Let's take a short break, ___ we?","a":"shall","o":["will","don't"],"h":"Let's → shall we","full":"Let's take a short break, shall we?","au":"2d40176542"},{"s":"Don't forget the slides, ___ you?","a":"will","o":["do","don't"],"h":"imperativo → will you","full":"Don't forget the slides, will you?","au":"3c7babdbd7"},{"s":"Nobody called the client, ___ they?","a":"did","o":["didn't","does"],"h":"nobody es negativo → coletilla positiva","full":"Nobody called the client, did they?","au":"ac1acc426f"},{"s":"She hardly ever complains, ___ she?","a":"does","o":["doesn't","is"],"h":"hardly ever = negativo → coletilla positiva","full":"She hardly ever complains, does she?","au":"4bded2e834"},{"s":"Everything is ready, ___ it?","a":"isn't","o":["aren't","is"],"h":"everything → it","full":"Everything is ready, isn't it?","au":"ea130e6205"},{"s":"Somebody took my stapler, ___ they?","a":"didn't","o":["did","wasn't"],"h":"somebody → they","full":"Somebody took my stapler, didn't they?","au":"5f34fc8095"}],"dialogue":{"title":"Small talk before the meeting","es":"Charla antes de la reunión","img":"u:photo-1431540015161-0bf868a2d407","lines":[{"who":"Rachel","v":"f","t":"Morning, Diego! Crazy traffic on the freeway today, wasn't it?","au":"0898e41594"},{"who":"Diego","v":"m","t":"Terrible. I'm not the last one here, am I?","au":"afe7755bb9"},{"who":"Rachel","v":"f","t":"No, relax. Nobody has seen Mark yet, have they?","au":"14bf65b170"},{"who":"Diego","v":"m","t":"He's flying back from Phoenix, isn't he? He'll be late, won't he?","au":"87e1f6f020"},{"who":"Rachel","v":"f","t":"Probably. Let's start without him, shall we?","au":"eb394810e9"},{"who":"Diego","v":"m","t":"Good idea. Pass me the agenda, will you?","au":"cedd2ec115"},{"who":"Rachel","v":"f","t":"Here you go. You've read the new proposal, haven't you?","au":"034e8c5208"},{"who":"Diego","v":"m","t":"Not yet. I'm in trouble, aren't I?","au":"b3682d2b09"}],"q":[{"q":"How was the traffic?","a":"Terrible.","o":["Light.","Normal."]},{"q":"Why will Mark be late?","a":"He's flying back from Phoenix.","o":["He's sick.","He missed the bus."]},{"q":"What hasn't Diego done?","a":"Read the new proposal.","o":["Printed the agenda.","Called Mark."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To use special tag questions and the right intonation to sound natural.","es":"Usar coletillas especiales y la entonación correcta para sonar natural."},"warm":[{"q":"Is there a word in Spanish you use at the end of questions, like ¿no? or ¿verdad?","au":"b0836eb1af","es":"¿Hay alguna palabra en español que uses al final de las preguntas, como ¿no? o ¿verdad?","ex":"Yes, I always say '¿cierto?' at the end."},{"q":"When do you ask a question that you already know the answer to?","au":"e073d9e5c9","es":"¿Cuándo haces una pregunta cuya respuesta ya sabes?","ex":"When I want to start a conversation or check something."}],"reading":{"title":"It's all in the melody","img":"u:photo-1431540015161-0bf868a2d407","text":"Linguists say that English speakers often understand a tag question by its melody before they process its words. Imagine two colleagues in a Chicago office. One says, \"The client signed the contract, didn't she?\" If her voice goes down at the end, she is almost certain and simply wants agreement. If her voice goes up, she genuinely doesn't know and needs an answer. Same words, different meaning. Learners also struggle with the special cases. \"I'm right, aren't I?\" sounds strange at first, because the logical form, \"amn't I,\" is not used in standard English. Suggestions with \"let's\" take \"shall we?\", as in \"Let's call it a day, shall we?\" Commands become softer with \"will you?\": \"Send me the slides, will you?\" Negative words such as never, nobody, nothing and hardly are another trap. Because they already make the sentence negative, the tag must be positive: \"Nobody called, did they?\" Experts recommend practicing with short dialogues and recording yourself. Listen for the melody: falling for confirmation, rising for real doubt. Once you control it, you will sound more confident and much less robotic in meetings, interviews and casual chats.","au":"d3cb9e1eaf","q":[{"s":"English speakers often understand a tag by its melody.","a":"yes"},{"s":"A falling voice means the speaker really doesn't know.","a":"no"},{"s":"\"Amn't I\" is the normal tag in standard English.","a":"no"},{"s":"After \"let's\", we use \"shall we?\".","a":"yes"},{"s":"After \"nobody\", the tag must be positive.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"I'm next, aren't I?","a":"Yes, you are. You can go in now.","es":"Sigo yo, ¿no?","qau":"19139459e6","aau":"e7043ece7e"},{"q":"Let's take a break, shall we?","a":"Good idea. I need a coffee.","es":"Tomemos un descanso, ¿sí?","qau":"7d3041572c","aau":"1102391d41"},{"q":"Nobody called while I was out, did they?","a":"Actually, your sister called twice.","es":"Nadie llamó mientras estaba fuera, ¿verdad?","qau":"ff64241370","aau":"91207f886b"},{"q":"You never eat meat, do you?","a":"No, I don't. I've been a vegetarian for years.","es":"Nunca comes carne, ¿cierto?","qau":"e05b5402d5","aau":"eec88095f6"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe 6 oraciones con coletillas especiales: una con I am, una con let's, una con imperativo, y tres con never / nobody / nothing. Marca con ↗ o ↘ la entonación.","kw":["aren't I","shall we","will you","did they"],"n":6,"model":"I'm invited, aren't I? ↘ Let's order pizza, shall we? ↘ Call me later, will you? ↘ Nobody saw the email, did they? ↗ You never drink coffee, do you? ↘ Nothing went wrong, did it? ↗"}}]},{"n":9,"title":"Reported Speech","es":"Estilo indirecto","cover":"u:photo-1629904869392-ae2a682d4d01","parts":[{"id":"t9p1","topic":9,"part":1,"title":"Reporting statements: backshift","es":"Reportar lo que alguien dijo","acts":["learn","reportedGossipChain","sort","fill","matchLines","speak"],"tip":"<p>El <b>estilo indirecto</b> (reported speech) sirve para contar lo que otra persona dijo.</p>\n<p>⏪ <b>Backshift:</b> cuando el verbo que introduce está en pasado (<i>said, told</i>), el tiempo verbal \"retrocede\":<br>\n<b>am/is → was</b> · <b>are → were</b> · <b>do → did</b> · <b>did / have done → had done</b> · <b>will → would</b> · <b>can → could</b> · <b>may → might</b>.<br>\n<i>\"I'm exhausted.\"</i> → <i>She said she <b>was</b> exhausted.</i></p>\n<p>🗣️ <b>say vs tell:</b> <b>say</b> (something) <i>— He said that…</i> · <b>tell</b> + <b>persona</b> <i>— He told <b>me</b> that…</i> (nunca <i>said me</i>).</p>\n<p>📅 Cambian también tiempo y lugar: <b>today → that day</b> · <b>tomorrow → the next day</b> · <b>yesterday → the day before</b> · <b>now → then</b> · <b>here → there</b> · <b>this → that</b>.</p>\n<p>💡 Si lo dicho <b>sigue siendo cierto</b>, el backshift es opcional: <i>She said she <b>lives</b> in Denver.</i></p>","tips":["<b>said</b> se pronuncia <i>sed</i>, no <i>seid</i>.","<b>told</b> suena <i>tould</i>, con la 'l' suave.","En el habla rápida <b>he would</b> → <b>he'd</b> (<i>jid</i>) y <b>she had</b> → <b>she'd</b> (<i>shid</i>)."],"vocab":[{"en":"He said (that)…","es":"Él dijo que…","img":"u:photo-1611095790444-1dfa35e37b52","v":"m","au":"26e247791c"},{"en":"She told me (that)…","es":"Ella me dijo que…","img":"u:photo-1653762381632-2945469edb7b","v":"f","au":"9291b7d7c8"},{"en":"backshift","es":"retroceso del tiempo verbal","img":"#is → was · will → would","v":"f","au":"d886306a1e"},{"en":"the day before","es":"el día anterior","img":"u:photo-1676287566973-7e25f18f12a9","v":"m","au":"dbad0b9ae1"},{"en":"the next day","es":"al día siguiente","img":"u:photo-1650570725926-cd88ef8784bd","v":"f","au":"fca68cdc5b"},{"en":"that night","es":"esa noche","img":"u:photo-1599939571322-792a326991f2","v":"m","au":"6e2ca145d9"},{"en":"then","es":"en ese momento / entonces","img":"u:photo-1563861826100-9cb868fdbe1c","v":"f","au":"b38dfb64a1"},{"en":"to pass on a message","es":"transmitir un mensaje","img":"u:photo-1758598306765-10156411ffc4","v":"f","au":"5d379d28a8"},{"en":"word for word","es":"palabra por palabra","img":"u:photo-1759659334772-c3a05b8178e9","v":"m","au":"e00a228d9e"},{"en":"according to","es":"según","img":"u:photo-1524508762098-fd966ffb6ef9","v":"f","au":"3dab0ae338"},{"en":"to quote someone","es":"citar a alguien","img":"u:photo-1519304520401-239e2a56a1aa","v":"m","au":"ac5b4b0a1d"},{"en":"to gossip","es":"chismosear","img":"u:photo-1629904869392-ae2a682d4d01","v":"f","au":"3598a0823c"}],"sentences":[{"en":"She said she was working from home.","es":"Ella dijo que estaba trabajando desde casa.","img":"u:photo-1524508762098-fd966ffb6ef9","v":"f","au":"fca6be4d0c"},{"en":"He told me he had lost his keys.","es":"Él me dijo que había perdido sus llaves.","img":"u:photo-1643792801605-1f8081811439","v":"m","au":"765641fa6e"},{"en":"They said they would call the next day.","es":"Dijeron que llamarían al día siguiente.","img":"u:photo-1691380302295-b19eda6ae52b","v":"f","au":"f975d39a27"},{"en":"My boss told us the deadline had changed.","es":"Mi jefe nos dijo que la fecha límite había cambiado.","img":"u:photo-1758518731706-be5d5230e5a5","v":"m","au":"41f4bf9995"},{"en":"You said you could fix it!","es":"¡Dijiste que podías arreglarlo!","img":"u:photo-1625047509248-ec889cbff17f","v":"f","au":"92ea51473f"},{"en":"She said she'd been to Boston the week before.","es":"Dijo que había estado en Boston la semana anterior.","img":"u:photo-1565127803082-69dd82351360","v":"m","au":"9be62ba90d"}],"fill":[{"s":"Mark ___ me he was quitting.","a":"told","o":["said","talked"],"h":"tell + persona","full":"Mark told me he was quitting.","au":"a1235afa06"},{"s":"She ___ that the store was closed.","a":"said","o":["told","spoke"],"h":"say + that (sin persona)","full":"She said that the store was closed.","au":"9007867628"},{"s":"He said he ___ tired. (\"I'm tired.\")","a":"was","o":["is","were"],"h":"am → was","full":"He said he was tired. (\"I'm tired.\")","au":"1dd3e28ef2"},{"s":"They said they ___ help us. (\"We will help you.\")","a":"would","o":["will","can"],"h":"will → would","full":"They said they would help us. (\"We will help you.\")","au":"d4127d7320"},{"s":"She said she ___ the ad. (\"I saw the ad.\")","a":"had seen","o":["has seen","sees"],"h":"pasado → had + participio","full":"She said she had seen the ad. (\"I saw the ad.\")","au":"d4fefb9733"},{"s":"He said he'd do it ___. (\"I'll do it tomorrow.\")","a":"the next day","o":["tomorrow","yesterday"],"h":"tomorrow → the next day","full":"He said he'd do it the next day. (\"I'll do it tomorrow.\")","au":"863611461a"},{"s":"They said they ___ come. (\"We can't come.\")","a":"couldn't","o":["can't","won't"],"h":"can't → couldn't","full":"They said they couldn't come. (\"We can't come.\")","au":"42126282d4"}],"sort":{"cats":["say","tell"],"items":[{"w":"the truth","c":"tell","au":"7c38f4ff42"},{"w":"a lie","c":"tell","au":"ba21a3251a"},{"w":"goodbye","c":"say","au":"479deca251"},{"w":"a story","c":"tell","au":"7bd470ddc2"},{"w":"something nice","c":"say","au":"c4d844a42a"},{"w":"sorry","c":"say","au":"61d7e8edf4"},{"w":"someone a secret","c":"tell","au":"299cbb231f"},{"w":"a joke","c":"tell","au":"7faa86005c"},{"w":"no to an offer","c":"say","au":"b0c1499763"},{"w":"the difference","c":"tell","au":"14160fc447"}]},"goal":{"en":"To report what other people said using backshift and say vs. tell.","es":"Contar lo que otras personas dijeron usando backshift y say vs. tell."},"warm":[{"q":"What was the last piece of news a friend told you?","au":"13c52636dc","es":"¿Cuál fue la última noticia que te contó un amigo?","ex":"My friend told me she was getting married."},{"q":"Do you remember something important your parents said to you as a child?","au":"d5906dfd99","es":"¿Recuerdas algo importante que te dijeron tus padres de niño?","ex":"My father said that education was the best investment."}],"reading":{"title":"The message that got lost","img":"u:photo-1758598306765-10156411ffc4","text":"Last spring, a small design agency in San Diego almost lost its biggest client because of a message that was passed on badly. On Monday, the client called and spoke to Tyler, the new receptionist. She said, \"We're changing the launch date. We'll need the final files by Thursday.\" Tyler wrote a quick note and gave it to Megan, the project manager. Megan told the designers that the client had changed the date, but she said the files were due \"next Thursday,\" not that week. The designers relaxed and focused on other projects. On Thursday morning, the client called again, very upset. She said she had been waiting for the files since eight o'clock and that she couldn't understand the delay. The agency director apologized and promised that the team would send everything that night. They worked until two in the morning and saved the account. Afterwards, the director told everyone that messages had to be reported word for word, with exact days and times. Now the agency uses a simple form: who called, what they said, and when they need it. Tyler jokes that he has never written \"tomorrow\" on a note again.","au":"3aae9fd0ba","q":[{"s":"The agency is in San Diego.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The client spoke to Megan first.","a":"no"},{"s":"Megan said the files were due the following week.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The team worked until two in the morning.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The director said messages could be reported in a general way.","a":"no"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"What did your boss say yesterday?","a":"She said that the meeting had been moved to Friday.","es":"¿Qué dijo tu jefe ayer?","qau":"fed72c60dd","aau":"bb162226b5"},{"q":"What did your friend tell you?","a":"He told me he was moving to Texas.","es":"¿Qué te dijo tu amigo?","qau":"3d6f802a88","aau":"dae039b87a"},{"q":"What did the doctor say?","a":"She said I needed to rest for a week.","es":"¿Qué dijo el médico?","qau":"e638916199","aau":"c36a36ae3f"}],"hw":{"es":"Piensa en una conversación reciente (con tu jefe, un amigo o tu familia) y repórtala en 6 oraciones usando said y told, con backshift y cambios de tiempo (the next day, the day before...).","kw":["said","told"],"n":6,"model":"Yesterday my boss told me she was very happy with my work. She said the client had loved the presentation. She told me I would lead the next project. She said we would meet the next day to discuss it. My colleague said he had heard the news the day before. He told me he was proud of me."}},{"id":"t9p2","topic":9,"part":2,"title":"Reporting verbs","es":"Verbos para reportar","acts":["learn","reportingVerbCourtroom","dialogue","fill","quizShow","speak"],"tip":"<p>En vez de repetir siempre <i>said</i>, el inglés avanzado usa <b>verbos que resumen la intención</b>. Cada uno tiene su <b>patrón</b>:</p>\n<p>➡️ <b>verbo + -ing:</b> <b>suggest, admit, deny</b> — <i>He <b>denied taking</b> the money.</i><br>\n➡️ <b>verbo + to + verbo:</b> <b>promise, refuse, offer, agree</b> — <i>She <b>offered to drive</b> me.</i><br>\n➡️ <b>verbo + persona + to:</b> <b>advise, warn, remind, ask, tell</b> — <i>They <b>warned us not to</b> go.</i><br>\n➡️ <b>verbo + preposición + -ing:</b> <b>apologize for, insist on, accuse someone of</b> — <i>He <b>apologized for being</b> late.</i></p>\n<p>⚠️ <b>suggest</b> nunca lleva <i>to</i>: ❌ <i>suggested to go</i> ✅ <i>suggested going</i> / <i>suggested (that) we go</i>.</p>","tips":["<b>suggest</b> en EE. UU. suena <i>səgyést</i>.","<b>advise</b> (verbo) termina en sonido <i>z</i>: <i>advaiz</i>; <b>advice</b> (sustantivo) termina en <i>s</i>.","<b>denied</b> se dice <i>dináid</i>, con acento al final."],"vocab":[{"en":"suggest doing","es":"sugerir hacer","img":"u:photo-1531537571171-a707bf2683da","v":"f","au":"dd8e01d100"},{"en":"admit doing","es":"admitir haber hecho","img":"u:photo-1790596684701-912aa2e686ef","v":"m","au":"8eb18b4a03"},{"en":"deny doing","es":"negar haber hecho","img":"u:photo-1622566359362-539a508d6af5","v":"m","au":"f4a47af6b6"},{"en":"promise to do","es":"prometer hacer","img":"u:photo-1672380135241-c024f7fbfa13","v":"f","au":"936e15aa40"},{"en":"warn someone not to","es":"advertir a alguien que no","img":"u:photo-1578986568309-707ef1017f69","v":"m","au":"9ffee81807"},{"en":"advise someone to","es":"aconsejar a alguien que","img":"u:photo-1551836022-d5d88e9218df","v":"f","au":"ff60743624"},{"en":"refuse to do","es":"negarse a hacer","img":"u:photo-1762328020748-4912b568d313","v":"f","au":"1c6f1fa034"},{"en":"offer to do","es":"ofrecerse a hacer","img":"u:photo-1608342381036-15657da6bf58","v":"m","au":"63c30c1669"},{"en":"remind someone to","es":"recordarle a alguien que","img":"u:photo-1580934174026-8142803ebb5b","v":"f","au":"19dab84775"},{"en":"apologize for doing","es":"disculparse por hacer","img":"u:photo-1739303987849-ceddfda25c7e","v":"f","au":"8528dd458a"},{"en":"accuse someone of","es":"acusar a alguien de","img":"u:photo-1768839721041-437940836abb","v":"m","au":"0a2bc457b5"},{"en":"insist on doing","es":"insistir en hacer","img":"u:photo-1551836022-d5d88e9218df","v":"f","au":"c131705896"}],"sentences":[{"en":"She suggested taking the earlier flight.","es":"Sugirió tomar el vuelo más temprano.","img":"u:photo-1553619948-505cc1cdc320","v":"f","au":"05f584bf2e"},{"en":"He admitted making a mistake.","es":"Admitió haber cometido un error.","img":"u:photo-1790596684701-912aa2e686ef","v":"m","au":"e4b8c72c89"},{"en":"The CEO denied leaking the report.","es":"El CEO negó haber filtrado el informe.","img":"u:photo-1444653614773-995cb1ef9efa","v":"m","au":"ee5f926bce"},{"en":"My doctor advised me to cut down on sugar.","es":"Mi médico me aconsejó reducir el azúcar.","img":"u:photo-1631217868264-e5b90bb7e133","v":"f","au":"89cc667945"},{"en":"They warned us not to drive at night.","es":"Nos advirtieron que no manejáramos de noche.","img":"u:photo-1564668836804-05a2de350bb6","v":"m","au":"bf434ef4c5"},{"en":"She promised to send the invoice today.","es":"Prometió enviar la factura hoy.","img":"u:photo-1544717302-de2939b7ef71","v":"f","au":"c8781a5b47"}],"fill":[{"s":"He denied ___ the money.","a":"taking","o":["to take","take"],"h":"deny + -ing","full":"He denied taking the money.","au":"4fade0442d"},{"s":"She offered ___ me to the airport.","a":"to drive","o":["driving","drive"],"h":"offer + to + verbo","full":"She offered to drive me to the airport.","au":"fa48dde8c1"},{"s":"The lawyer advised us ___ anything.","a":"not to sign","o":["to not signing","don't sign"],"h":"advise + persona + (not) to","full":"The lawyer advised us not to sign anything.","au":"03f2cb914d"},{"s":"They accused him ___ lying.","a":"of","o":["for","about"],"h":"accuse someone of + -ing","full":"They accused him of lying.","au":"90204da07f"},{"s":"I suggested ___ a meeting.","a":"having","o":["to have","have"],"h":"suggest + -ing","full":"I suggested having a meeting.","au":"35677caef6"},{"s":"She apologized ___ being late.","a":"for","o":["of","about"],"h":"apologize for + -ing","full":"She apologized for being late.","au":"ab601b980e"},{"s":"He refused ___ the contract.","a":"to sign","o":["signing","sign"],"h":"refuse + to","full":"He refused to sign the contract.","au":"776c94a7b0"}],"dialogue":{"title":"What did the manager say?","es":"¿Qué dijo la gerente?","img":"u:photo-1758518731706-be5d5230e5a5","lines":[{"who":"Kevin","v":"m","t":"You missed the meeting! Did Sandra say anything about the merger?","au":"7196d8a467"},{"who":"Lucía","v":"f","t":"Not much. She refused to give any details, but she promised to update us next week.","au":"77476a3881"},{"who":"Kevin","v":"m","t":"Did anyone ask about layoffs?","au":"bc94d6ec6e"},{"who":"Lucía","v":"f","t":"Tom did. Sandra denied planning any layoffs this year.","au":"b2de49d4d0"},{"who":"Kevin","v":"m","t":"That's a relief. Anything else?","au":"4af0526c38"},{"who":"Lucía","v":"f","t":"She reminded everyone to submit their expense reports by Friday.","au":"e1deabd5e1"},{"who":"Kevin","v":"m","t":"Oops. I'd better do mine today.","au":"801c04fe45"},{"who":"Lucía","v":"f","t":"Yes! And she advised us not to talk to the press.","au":"4b118d6eec"}],"q":[{"q":"What did Sandra promise?","a":"To update the team next week.","o":["To give details today.","To hire more people."]},{"q":"What did she deny?","a":"Planning layoffs this year.","o":["Talking to the press.","Missing the meeting."]},{"q":"What did she remind everyone to do?","a":"Submit their expense reports.","o":["Call the press.","Read the merger contract."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To summarize what people said with reporting verbs like suggest, deny and warn.","es":"Resumir lo que dijo la gente con verbos como suggest, deny y warn."},"warm":[{"q":"Have you ever promised to do something and then forgotten?","au":"034e2d651b","es":"¿Alguna vez prometiste hacer algo y luego se te olvidó?","ex":"Yes, I promised to call my aunt and I forgot."},{"q":"What is the best advice anyone has ever given you?","au":"53a7cb8e6f","es":"¿Cuál es el mejor consejo que alguien te ha dado?","ex":"My mother advised me to save ten percent of my salary."}],"reading":{"title":"Inside a press conference","img":"u:photo-1444653614773-995cb1ef9efa","text":"Journalists rarely write \"he said\" five times in a row. Instead, they choose reporting verbs that capture the intention behind the words. Consider yesterday's press conference at a tech company in Austin, where customer data had been exposed. The CEO admitted making serious mistakes and apologized for not informing users sooner. However, she denied hiding the problem on purpose. When a reporter asked about compensation, she refused to give exact numbers but promised to offer free credit monitoring to every affected customer. A cybersecurity expert who attended the event warned users not to click on suspicious emails over the next few weeks. He advised everyone to change their passwords immediately and suggested turning on two-step verification. Later, an angry investor accused the board of ignoring earlier warnings, and a board member insisted on defending the company's security team. Notice how much information these verbs carry. \"She said she was sorry\" is simple; \"she apologized for not informing users\" is precise and professional. Each verb also has its own grammar pattern: deny and suggest take -ing, promise and refuse take to, warn and advise take a person plus to. Mastering them will make your reports and emails sound truly advanced.","au":"e704fba805","q":[{"s":"The press conference was in Austin.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The CEO denied making any mistakes.","a":"no"},{"s":"The CEO promised free credit monitoring.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The expert suggested turning on two-step verification.","a":"yes"},{"s":"An investor apologized to the board.","a":"no"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"What did your doctor advise you to do?","a":"She advised me to exercise more and sleep eight hours.","es":"¿Qué te aconsejó hacer tu médico?","qau":"c02866c237","aau":"8bdb787abf"},{"q":"Has anyone ever accused you of something you didn't do?","a":"Yes, my brother once accused me of breaking his phone.","es":"¿Alguien te ha acusado alguna vez de algo que no hiciste?","qau":"829a199674","aau":"cee740c852"},{"q":"What did your manager suggest at the last meeting?","a":"He suggested hiring two more people.","es":"¿Qué sugirió tu gerente en la última reunión?","qau":"69438f6c44","aau":"67c697b732"},{"q":"What did you promise to do this year?","a":"I promised to practice English every day.","es":"¿Qué prometiste hacer este año?","qau":"74353e060a","aau":"abc6a364fe"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe un pequeño reporte de noticias (6 oraciones) sobre una reunión o evento inventado usando 6 verbos diferentes: suggest, admit, deny, promise, warn, advise.","kw":["suggested","denied","promised","warned"],"n":6,"model":"At yesterday's meeting, the director admitted making a mistake with the budget. She denied wasting money on travel. Then she promised to present a new plan in May. The finance manager warned us not to spend more than ten percent. He advised everyone to keep all receipts. Finally, Ana suggested using a new app to track expenses."}}]},{"n":10,"title":"Direct and Indirect Questions","es":"Preguntas directas e indirectas","cover":"u:photo-1787724779319-3ebd1c848bee","parts":[{"id":"t10p1","topic":10,"part":1,"title":"Polite indirect questions","es":"Preguntas indirectas corteses","acts":["learn","politeConciergeDesk","sort","unscramble","catchWord","speak"],"tip":"<p>Las <b>preguntas indirectas</b> suenan más <b>educadas y profesionales</b>. Empiezan con una frase introductoria: <b>Could you tell me…? · Do you know…? · I was wondering…</b></p>\n<p>🔄 <b>Lo más importante:</b> después de la introducción, el orden es de <b>afirmación</b> (sujeto + verbo), <b>sin do/does/did</b>:<br>\n❓ <i>Where <b>is</b> the station?</i> → ✅ <i>Could you tell me where <b>the station is</b>?</i><br>\n❓ <i>What time <b>does</b> it open?</i> → ✅ <i>Do you know what time <b>it opens</b>?</i></p>\n<p>❔ Si la pregunta es de <b>sí/no</b>, usa <b>if</b> o <b>whether</b>: <i>Is breakfast included?</i> → <i>Do you know <b>if</b> breakfast is included?</i></p>\n<p>✏️ El signo de interrogación depende de la frase inicial: <i>Do you know…<b>?</b></i> pero <i>I was wondering if you could help me<b>.</b></i></p>","tips":["<b>Could you</b> se une: <i>kúdʒu</i>.","<b>Would you mind</b> suena <i>wúdʒu máind</i>.","<b>wondering</b> se dice <i>uánderin</i> (no confundir con <b>wandering</b>, <i>uónderin</i>)."],"vocab":[{"en":"Could you tell me…?","es":"¿Podría decirme…?","img":"u:photo-1787724779319-3ebd1c848bee","v":"f","au":"ae170e67cf"},{"en":"Do you know…?","es":"¿Sabe usted…?","img":"u:photo-1760282341931-0c1b595a1cb0","v":"m","au":"f8ee18a368"},{"en":"I was wondering if…","es":"Me preguntaba si…","img":"u:photo-1702047129200-89734f555f38","v":"f","au":"304101fb64"},{"en":"Would you mind telling me…?","es":"¿Le importaría decirme…?","img":"u:photo-1771979788419-84487b12e3a0","v":"m","au":"491e3028f0"},{"en":"Do you happen to know…?","es":"¿Por casualidad sabe…?","img":"u:photo-1615155052169-6c7f27a2fe89","v":"m","au":"9d417bc053"},{"en":"Can you remind me…?","es":"¿Me puedes recordar…?","img":"u:photo-1580934174026-8142803ebb5b","v":"f","au":"77b4e25815"},{"en":"Any idea…?","es":"¿Tienes idea de…? (informal)","img":"u:photo-1604881988758-f76ad2f7aac1","v":"m","au":"197912471b"},{"en":"word order","es":"orden de las palabras","img":"#subject + verb","v":"f","au":"e8aec8bffe"},{"en":"the front desk","es":"la recepción","img":"u:photo-1759038085950-1234ca8f5fed","v":"f","au":"c609e4ff79"},{"en":"the restroom","es":"el baño (en un lugar público)","img":"u:photo-1622768761182-ed301028a2e0","v":"m","au":"3b77b12695"},{"en":"checkout time","es":"hora de salida (hotel)","img":"u:photo-1673687779028-cff003cdab93","v":"f","au":"69e3d69664"},{"en":"to come across as rude","es":"parecer grosero","img":"u:photo-1532348904171-919f8b2b7e62","v":"m","au":"c90c39c6b6"}],"sentences":[{"en":"Could you tell me where the restroom is?","es":"¿Podría decirme dónde está el baño?","img":"u:photo-1622768761182-ed301028a2e0","v":"m","au":"c039767ae1"},{"en":"Do you know what time the museum opens?","es":"¿Sabe a qué hora abre el museo?","img":"u:photo-1753363754464-58a41b3b954b","v":"f","au":"534fded070"},{"en":"I was wondering if you could help me.","es":"Me preguntaba si podría ayudarme.","img":"u:photo-1760282341931-0c1b595a1cb0","v":"m","au":"c45c977384"},{"en":"Can you tell me how much this costs?","es":"¿Me puede decir cuánto cuesta esto?","img":"u:photo-1483181957632-8bda974cbc91","v":"f","au":"0fd5a570c1"},{"en":"Do you happen to know where Main Street is?","es":"¿Por casualidad sabe dónde queda Main Street?","img":"u:photo-1615155052169-6c7f27a2fe89","v":"m","au":"a3df8e048c"},{"en":"Would you mind telling me your name again?","es":"¿Le importaría decirme su nombre otra vez?","img":"u:photo-1491438590914-bc09fcaaf77a","v":"f","au":"b5f96c0805"}],"fill":[{"s":"Could you tell me where ___?","a":"the station is","o":["is the station","does the station be"],"h":"sujeto + verbo","full":"Could you tell me where the station is?","au":"e4a8f227ef"},{"s":"Do you know what time ___?","a":"the bank opens","o":["does the bank open","opens the bank"],"h":"sin do/does","full":"Do you know what time the bank opens?","au":"b79b26c391"},{"s":"I was wondering ___ you could help me.","a":"if","o":["that","what"],"h":"pregunta de sí/no → if","full":"I was wondering if you could help me.","au":"89af376912"},{"s":"Can you tell me how much ___?","a":"it costs","o":["does it cost","costs it"],"h":"sin does","full":"Can you tell me how much it costs?","au":"fae85abef7"},{"s":"Do you know who ___ this report?","a":"wrote","o":["did write","has wrote"],"h":"who es el sujeto → verbo directo","full":"Do you know who wrote this report?","au":"2cd00a47b1"},{"s":"Would you mind ___ me the password?","a":"telling","o":["to tell","tell"],"h":"would you mind + -ing","full":"Would you mind telling me the password?","au":"f7a60fb149"}],"sort":{"cats":["Direct question","Indirect question"],"items":[{"w":"Where is the gym?","c":"Direct question","au":"dc606c36bc"},{"w":"Could you tell me where the gym is?","c":"Indirect question","au":"d1b609d5c3"},{"w":"What time does it close?","c":"Direct question","au":"dd91422ccc"},{"w":"Do you know what time it closes?","c":"Indirect question","au":"da24fa5f7f"},{"w":"Is breakfast included?","c":"Direct question","au":"ecec32b62d"},{"w":"I was wondering if breakfast is included.","c":"Indirect question","au":"24f6d88551"},{"w":"How much is the room?","c":"Direct question","au":"1d21479173"},{"w":"Can you tell me how much the room is?","c":"Indirect question","au":"91f9e67e46"},{"w":"Did they call?","c":"Direct question","au":"129fbf77ef"},{"w":"Do you know if they called?","c":"Indirect question","au":"e9e4677aac"}]},"goal":{"en":"To ask polite indirect questions in hotels, stores and at work.","es":"Hacer preguntas indirectas y corteses en hoteles, tiendas y en el trabajo."},"warm":[{"q":"How do you ask a stranger for help politely in Spanish?","au":"7a268a040a","es":"¿Cómo le pides ayuda a un desconocido de forma cortés en español?","ex":"I say 'Disculpe, ¿me podría ayudar?'"},{"q":"Have you ever felt that someone was rude to you in customer service?","au":"560f9176f9","es":"¿Alguna vez sentiste que alguien fue grosero contigo en servicio al cliente?","ex":"Yes, once at a bank the cashier didn't even look at me."}],"reading":{"title":"Why 'Where is the bathroom?' can sound rude","img":"u:photo-1759038085950-1234ca8f5fed","text":"In many languages, a direct question is perfectly polite if you add \"please.\" In American English, however, especially in customer service, direct questions can sound surprisingly abrupt. Imagine a tired guest arriving at a hotel in Orlando and saying, \"Where is the elevator? What time is breakfast?\" Nothing is grammatically wrong, but the receptionist may feel the guest is giving orders. Compare: \"Could you tell me where the elevator is? And do you happen to know what time breakfast starts?\" The second version sounds warm and respectful, and it often gets better service. These are called indirect questions. They begin with an introductory phrase and then use the word order of a normal statement. Learners frequently make the mistake of keeping the question order: \"Can you tell me where is the station?\" The correct form is \"where the station is.\" Similarly, the auxiliary do disappears: \"Do you know what time the store opens?\" not \"what time does the store open.\" For yes/no questions, use if or whether: \"I was wondering if you had a room available.\" Hotel trainers say that guests who speak this way are remembered positively. Politeness, it seems, is not only about what you ask but how you ask it.","au":"2443aae631","q":[{"s":"Direct questions are always polite in American English if you smile.","a":"no"},{"s":"The guest in the example arrives at a hotel in Orlando.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Indirect questions use the word order of a normal statement.","a":"yes"},{"s":"\"Can you tell me where is the station?\" is correct.","a":"no"},{"s":"For yes/no questions, we use if or whether.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Could you tell me where the nearest pharmacy is?","a":"Sure, it's two blocks down on the left.","es":"¿Podría decirme dónde está la farmacia más cercana?","qau":"088d0e519f","aau":"a92577f852"},{"q":"Do you know what time the bank closes?","a":"I think it closes at five.","es":"¿Sabe a qué hora cierra el banco?","qau":"b373b91c9a","aau":"3219d08b15"},{"q":"I was wondering if you could help me with my suitcase.","a":"Of course! Let me take it for you.","es":"Me preguntaba si podría ayudarme con mi maleta.","qau":"7e219e9ec3","aau":"bb69251da4"},{"q":"Do you happen to know how much a taxi to the airport costs?","a":"It's about forty dollars.","es":"¿Por casualidad sabe cuánto cuesta un taxi al aeropuerto?","qau":"274e67a5ca","aau":"3da8a4da81"}],"hw":{"es":"Imagina que llegas a un hotel en EE. UU. Escribe 6 preguntas indirectas para la recepción (wifi, desayuno, checkout, gimnasio, restaurantes, transporte).","kw":["could you tell me","do you know","if"],"n":6,"model":"Could you tell me what the wifi password is? Do you know what time breakfast starts? I was wondering if I could check out late. Can you tell me where the gym is? Do you happen to know if there's a good restaurant nearby? Could you tell me how I can get to the airport?"}},{"id":"t10p2","topic":10,"part":2,"title":"Reported questions at work","es":"Preguntas reportadas en el trabajo","acts":["learn","whetherEscapeLock","dialogue","fill","raceGame","speak"],"tip":"<p>Para <b>reportar una pregunta</b> usa <b>asked / wanted to know / wondered</b> + orden de <b>afirmación</b> + <b>backshift</b>:</p>\n<p>❓ <i>\"Where <b>do you live</b>?\"</i> → <i>She asked me where <b>I lived</b>.</i><br>\n❓ <i>\"<b>Can you</b> start on Monday?\"</i> → <i>He asked <b>if/whether I could</b> start on Monday.</i></p>\n<p>🔀 <b>if</b> y <b>whether</b> significan <i>si</i> (condicional de duda). Pero solo <b>whether</b> se usa:<br>\n• antes de <b>to + verbo</b>: <i>I don't know <b>whether to</b> accept.</i><br>\n• después de <b>preposición</b>: <i>It depends <b>on whether</b> they pay.</i><br>\n• con <b>or not</b> justo después: <i><b>whether or not</b> you agree</i>.</p>\n<p>🚫 Las preguntas reportadas <b>no llevan signo de interrogación</b> ni <i>do/does/did</i>.</p>","tips":["<b>whether</b> y <b>weather</b> se pronuncian igual: <i>uéder</i>.","<b>asked</b> suena <i>askt</i>, una sola sílaba.","<b>wanted to know</b> en habla rápida: <i>uánirə nóu</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"She asked me if…","es":"Me preguntó si…","img":"u:photo-1698047682091-782b1e5c6536","v":"f","au":"20a6111a37"},{"en":"He wanted to know…","es":"Quería saber…","img":"u:photo-1517245386807-bb43f82c33c4","v":"m","au":"1685bd2862"},{"en":"whether or not","es":"si… o no","img":"u:photo-1659355889750-8b0708f4ac8d","v":"f","au":"3bc2228e4b"},{"en":"whether to accept","es":"si aceptar o no","img":"u:photo-1758523419048-eeb546daac05","v":"m","au":"7e3d0349ba"},{"en":"a job interview","es":"una entrevista de trabajo","img":"u:photo-1672380135241-c024f7fbfa13","v":"f","au":"347d3bd6b7"},{"en":"salary expectations","es":"expectativas salariales","img":"u:photo-1600880292203-757bb62b4baf","v":"m","au":"8e9bb784ab"},{"en":"to inquire about","es":"informarse sobre","img":"u:photo-1766066014237-00645c74e9c6","v":"f","au":"4dffa978cf"},{"en":"a follow-up email","es":"un correo de seguimiento","img":"u:photo-1544717302-de2939b7ef71","v":"f","au":"520cbadc5f"},{"en":"the hiring manager","es":"el gerente de contratación","img":"u:photo-1573497620053-ea5300f94f21","v":"m","au":"001192f84f"},{"en":"to be shortlisted","es":"quedar preseleccionado","img":"u:photo-1758520144555-af04bf9ad3e2","v":"f","au":"181b7c2b95"},{"en":"notice period","es":"periodo de preaviso","img":"u:photo-1634562876572-5abe57afcceb","v":"m","au":"d2ac4e7dc9"},{"en":"to reach out","es":"contactar","img":"u:photo-1758876020967-e5a80e49463a","v":"m","au":"50d9b20552"}],"sentences":[{"en":"She asked me if I could start on Monday.","es":"Me preguntó si podía empezar el lunes.","img":"u:photo-1698047682091-782b1e5c6536","v":"f","au":"f260a72ec5"},{"en":"They wanted to know why I had left.","es":"Querían saber por qué me había ido.","img":"u:photo-1573497620053-ea5300f94f21","v":"m","au":"5589739e37"},{"en":"He asked whether I was willing to relocate.","es":"Preguntó si estaba dispuesto a mudarme.","img":"u:photo-1758523671165-967ec4af0d76","v":"m","au":"20333a1213"},{"en":"I'm not sure whether to accept the offer.","es":"No estoy seguro de si aceptar la oferta.","img":"u:photo-1758523419048-eeb546daac05","v":"f","au":"93bc541b0b"},{"en":"The recruiter asked what my salary expectations were.","es":"La reclutadora preguntó cuáles eran mis expectativas salariales.","img":"u:photo-1600880292203-757bb62b4baf","v":"f","au":"15906faf78"}],"fill":[{"s":"She asked me where I ___.","a":"lived","o":["did live","do I live"],"h":"sin did + backshift","full":"She asked me where I lived.","au":"d139505b1a"},{"s":"He asked ___ I had any experience.","a":"if","o":["that","what"],"h":"pregunta de sí/no → if","full":"He asked if I had any experience.","au":"bf06469813"},{"s":"They wanted to know when I ___ start.","a":"could","o":["can I","could I"],"h":"sujeto + verbo","full":"They wanted to know when I could start.","au":"39ec29dc7e"},{"s":"I can't decide ___ to apply or not.","a":"whether","o":["if","that"],"h":"whether + to + verbo","full":"I can't decide whether to apply or not.","au":"904278cca8"},{"s":"The manager asked us what we ___ about the plan.","a":"thought","o":["did think","think did"],"h":"pasado sin did","full":"The manager asked us what we thought about the plan.","au":"2a76cd08a4"},{"s":"She asked me how long I ___ there.","a":"had worked","o":["have I worked","did I work"],"h":"backshift: had + participio","full":"She asked me how long I had worked there.","au":"cd105d210c"}],"dialogue":{"title":"After the interview","es":"Después de la entrevista","img":"u:photo-1672380135241-c024f7fbfa13","lines":[{"who":"Andrea","v":"f","t":"So, how did the interview go? What did they ask you?","au":"bcacfda7b9"},{"who":"Luis","v":"m","t":"First, the hiring manager asked me why I wanted to leave my current job.","au":"5b544e8520"},{"who":"Andrea","v":"f","t":"Classic. Did they ask about money?","au":"59cf32793c"},{"who":"Luis","v":"m","t":"Yes. She wanted to know what my salary expectations were.","au":"acd94c6816"},{"who":"Andrea","v":"f","t":"And what did you say?","au":"9a3d877878"},{"who":"Luis","v":"m","t":"I said I was flexible. Then she asked whether I was willing to relocate to Atlanta.","au":"b157519080"},{"who":"Andrea","v":"f","t":"Wow! Are you?","au":"47a1eafb30"},{"who":"Luis","v":"m","t":"I'm still wondering whether to say yes. They'll let me know if I've been shortlisted.","au":"638cf81a6f"}],"q":[{"q":"What did the manager ask first?","a":"Why he wanted to leave his job.","o":["How old he was.","Where he lived."]},{"q":"Where might Luis have to move?","a":"To Atlanta.","o":["To Boston.","To Miami."]},{"q":"What is Luis still wondering?","a":"Whether to say yes.","o":["Whether to call Andrea.","Whether to buy a car."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To report questions from interviews and meetings, using if and whether correctly.","es":"Reportar preguntas de entrevistas y reuniones usando if y whether correctamente."},"warm":[{"q":"What is the most difficult question you have ever been asked in a job interview?","au":"a80c67727a","es":"¿Cuál es la pregunta más difícil que te han hecho en una entrevista de trabajo?","ex":"They asked me what my biggest weakness was."},{"q":"Do you prefer to ask questions or to answer them?","au":"38e026c682","es":"¿Prefieres hacer preguntas o responderlas?","ex":"I prefer to ask questions. I'm very curious."}],"reading":{"title":"Debriefing after an interview","img":"u:photo-1672380135241-c024f7fbfa13","text":"Career coaches in the United States often recommend a simple habit: write a debrief right after every job interview. Sebastián, a software engineer who recently moved to Raleigh, tried it after interviewing with a healthcare startup. In his notes, he wrote that the hiring manager had asked him why he wanted to leave his current company and what he knew about their product. She also wanted to know whether he had ever led a team and how he dealt with tight deadlines. Then she asked if he would be willing to work on weekends during product launches, which surprised him. Finally, she asked what his salary expectations were. Writing these reported questions helped Sebastián notice patterns. He realized that he had answered the leadership question too vaguely and that he wasn't sure whether to accept weekend work. Before his second interview, he prepared stronger stories and decided to ask whether weekend shifts were paid as overtime. He got the job, and the company agreed to give him extra days off instead. His advice for other candidates: keep a record of every question, because the same ones come back again and again. Note that in reported questions, the word order is like a statement and there is no question mark.","au":"dae8058334","q":[{"s":"Sebastián moved to Raleigh.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The hiring manager asked if he had ever led a team.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Sebastián was happy with his answer about leadership.","a":"no"},{"s":"He decided to ask whether weekend shifts were paid as overtime.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Reported questions always end with a question mark.","a":"no"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"What did they ask you in your last job interview?","a":"They asked me why I wanted the job and whether I could travel.","es":"¿Qué te preguntaron en tu última entrevista de trabajo?","qau":"5b68a83626","aau":"6188f34d5f"},{"q":"What did your boss want to know?","a":"She wanted to know if I had finished the report.","es":"¿Qué quería saber tu jefe?","qau":"fc0141318a","aau":"6e76485c07"},{"q":"Are you sure whether to change jobs?","a":"I'm still deciding whether to accept the offer or not.","es":"¿Estás seguro de si cambiar de trabajo?","qau":"f35deb1dbc","aau":"ba53a283e3"}],"hw":{"es":"Recuerda una entrevista (de trabajo, de visa o de la universidad) y escribe 6 preguntas que te hicieron en estilo indirecto. Usa asked, wanted to know, if y whether.","kw":["asked","wanted to know","if","whether"],"n":6,"model":"The interviewer asked me what my name was. She wanted to know where I had studied. She asked if I had worked abroad. Then she asked whether I could start in June. She wanted to know how much I expected to earn. Finally, she asked if I had any questions for her."}}]},{"n":11,"title":"Passive and Active Voice","es":"Voz pasiva y activa","cover":"u:photo-1504711434969-e33886168f5c","parts":[{"id":"t11p1","topic":11,"part":1,"title":"The passive in all tenses","es":"La voz pasiva en todos los tiempos","acts":["learn","passiveNewsroomTicker","fill","sort","sayPop","speak"],"tip":"<p>La <b>voz pasiva</b> pone el foco en la <b>acción o el resultado</b>, no en quién la hace. Fórmula: <b>be</b> (en el tiempo que necesites) + <b>participio pasado</b>.</p>\n<p>🕐 <b>Presente:</b> is/are <b>made</b> · <b>Pres. continuo:</b> is/are <b>being</b> made · <b>Pasado:</b> was/were made · <b>Pas. continuo:</b> was/were being made<br>\n✅ <b>Present perfect:</b> has/have <b>been</b> made · <b>Past perfect:</b> had been made · <b>Futuro:</b> will <b>be</b> made · <b>Modales:</b> can/must/should <b>be</b> made</p>\n<p>👤 Usa <b>by + agente</b> solo si es <b>importante o nuevo</b>: <i>The bridge was designed <b>by Joseph Strauss</b>.</i> Omite el agente si es obvio o desconocido: <i>My bike was stolen</i> (❌ <i>by someone</i>).</p>\n<p>💡 En español a menudo usamos <b>\"se\"</b>: <i>Se habla inglés</i> → <i>English <b>is spoken</b></i>.</p>","tips":["La terminación <b>-ed</b> suena <i>-id</i> solo después de 't' o 'd': <i>painted</i> (<i>péintid</i>), pero <i>delivered</i> (<i>delívərd</i>).","<b>been</b> en inglés americano suena <i>bin</i>.","<b>being</b> se pronuncia <i>bí-in</i>, dos sílabas cortas."],"vocab":[{"en":"is made","es":"es fabricado / se fabrica","img":"u:photo-1716191299980-a6e8827ba10b","v":"f","au":"0e2aa1aeb7"},{"en":"was built","es":"fue construido","img":"u:photo-1501594907352-04cda38ebc29","v":"m","au":"c70c5329a6"},{"en":"is being repaired","es":"está siendo reparado","img":"u:photo-1529792083865-d23889753466","v":"f","au":"7044e252f8"},{"en":"has been canceled","es":"ha sido cancelado","img":"u:photo-1746125047145-d6698eef563a","v":"m","au":"d5985c0eeb"},{"en":"had been sold","es":"había sido vendido","img":"u:photo-1782024743263-bb153ea077e1","v":"f","au":"81ad2244ec"},{"en":"will be announced","es":"será anunciado","img":"u:photo-1785807047596-3f3abd23df6a","v":"m","au":"2bd2fcffd3"},{"en":"can be downloaded","es":"se puede descargar","img":"u:photo-1480694313141-fce5e697ee25","v":"f","au":"48acf756d0"},{"en":"must be signed","es":"debe ser firmado","img":"u:photo-1562564055-71e051d33c19","v":"m","au":"4084ec90f8"},{"en":"by + agent","es":"por + quien hace la acción","img":"#by + agent","v":"f","au":"8a37da8162"},{"en":"to be launched","es":"ser lanzado","img":"u:photo-1457364887197-9150188c107b","v":"m","au":"0e299821f9"},{"en":"to be laid off","es":"ser despedido (recorte)","img":"u:photo-1758691737357-12839a28de6d","v":"m","au":"0f3fb9de0f"},{"en":"to be promoted","es":"ser ascendido","img":"u:photo-1758520144658-c87be518b87e","v":"f","au":"3d23327c4d"}],"sentences":[{"en":"The bridge was built in 1937.","es":"El puente fue construido en 1937.","img":"u:photo-1501594907352-04cda38ebc29","v":"m","au":"00797e7a82"},{"en":"The main road is being repaired.","es":"La vía principal está siendo reparada.","img":"u:photo-1529792083865-d23889753466","v":"f","au":"3cb84b1fe2"},{"en":"Your package has been delivered.","es":"Su paquete ha sido entregado.","img":"u:photo-1758523670564-d1d6a734dc0b","v":"m","au":"57973b6175"},{"en":"The winners will be announced tomorrow.","es":"Los ganadores serán anunciados mañana.","img":"u:photo-1785807047596-3f3abd23df6a","v":"f","au":"d8dc795fdb"},{"en":"This form must be signed by a manager.","es":"Este formulario debe ser firmado por un gerente.","img":"u:photo-1562564055-71e051d33c19","v":"m","au":"6da73efa17"},{"en":"The house had been sold before we called.","es":"La casa ya había sido vendida cuando llamamos.","img":"u:photo-1782024743263-bb153ea077e1","v":"f","au":"fe960e7405"}],"fill":[{"s":"English ___ all over the world.","a":"is spoken","o":["speaks","is speaking"],"h":"presente pasivo","full":"English is spoken all over the world.","au":"1d2a9cde4d"},{"s":"The museum ___ in 2010.","a":"was opened","o":["opened was","has opened"],"h":"pasado pasivo: was + participio","full":"The museum was opened in 2010.","au":"3f1addb8a8"},{"s":"The report ___ right now.","a":"is being written","o":["is writing","was written"],"h":"presente continuo pasivo","full":"The report is being written right now.","au":"6cf1beac05"},{"s":"All flights ___ due to the storm.","a":"have been canceled","o":["have canceled","are canceling"],"h":"present perfect pasivo","full":"All flights have been canceled due to the storm.","au":"c6f6f1834e"},{"s":"The results ___ next week.","a":"will be published","o":["will publish","are publishing"],"h":"futuro pasivo","full":"The results will be published next week.","au":"41d2530907"},{"s":"The documents must ___ by Friday.","a":"be signed","o":["sign","signed"],"h":"modal + be + participio","full":"The documents must be signed by Friday.","au":"8d0c25c2d0"},{"s":"The car ___ before the police arrived.","a":"had been stolen","o":["had stolen","was stealing"],"h":"past perfect pasivo","full":"The car had been stolen before the police arrived.","au":"6c387ebe47"}],"sort":{"cats":["Present","Past","Perfect","Future / Modal"],"items":[{"w":"is made","c":"Present","au":"0e2aa1aeb7"},{"w":"are being tested","c":"Present","au":"acfe8ad29a"},{"w":"was built","c":"Past","au":"52e3d83563"},{"w":"were being painted","c":"Past","au":"a331a91aec"},{"w":"has been sold","c":"Perfect","au":"2bb21dd6ed"},{"w":"had been canceled","c":"Perfect","au":"5248fb0706"},{"w":"will be sent","c":"Future / Modal","au":"226bc1215d"},{"w":"can be fixed","c":"Future / Modal","au":"199c6a139b"},{"w":"must be paid","c":"Future / Modal","au":"91c06dedc6"},{"w":"were found","c":"Past","au":"1488c62c47"},{"w":"have been hired","c":"Perfect","au":"7e78896307"},{"w":"is cleaned daily","c":"Present","au":"df0d9e0727"}]},"goal":{"en":"To use the passive voice in all tenses and decide when to include the agent.","es":"Usar la voz pasiva en todos los tiempos y decidir cuándo incluir al agente."},"warm":[{"q":"Do you know when your city was founded?","au":"ab9366817d","es":"¿Sabes cuándo fue fundada tu ciudad?","ex":"I think it was founded in the sixteenth century."},{"q":"What is something that has been built or renovated near your home recently?","au":"215d14bd8d","es":"¿Qué se ha construido o renovado cerca de tu casa recientemente?","ex":"A new shopping mall has been built near my house."}],"reading":{"title":"A bridge that was never supposed to exist","img":"u:photo-1501594907352-04cda38ebc29","text":"Today, the Golden Gate Bridge is photographed by millions of tourists every year, but for decades it was considered impossible to build. Engineers argued that the strait was too deep, the winds too strong and the fog too thick. The project was finally approved in 1930, and construction was started in 1933 under the direction of chief engineer Joseph Strauss. Much of the elegant design, however, was created by Charles Ellis and Leon Moisseiff, whose names were left out of the official celebrations for years. During construction, a safety net was installed under the bridge, and nineteen workers were saved by it. The bridge was opened to pedestrians in May 1937, and the next day it was opened to cars. Since then, it has been painted continuously in its famous color, \"International Orange.\" Today, the cables are being inspected regularly, and the structure has been reinforced to resist earthquakes. Plans have also been made for the future: new barriers will be added and the deck will be maintained for generations. Notice how this text uses the passive voice: the focus is on the bridge and what happened to it, not on the people who did each action. When the agent matters, it is introduced with by.","au":"316a6977c5","q":[{"s":"The bridge was approved in 1930.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The whole design was created by Joseph Strauss alone.","a":"no"},{"s":"A safety net saved nineteen workers.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The bridge was opened to cars before pedestrians.","a":"no"},{"s":"The structure has been reinforced against earthquakes.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"When was your house or building built?","a":"It was built in the nineties.","es":"¿Cuándo fue construida tu casa o edificio?","qau":"943843f877","aau":"ed76568c8f"},{"q":"What language is spoken in Brazil?","a":"Portuguese is spoken in Brazil.","es":"¿Qué idioma se habla en Brasil?","qau":"082577d31c","aau":"dfb6f2f4ce"},{"q":"Has your street ever been repaired?","a":"Yes, it was repaired last year.","es":"¿Han reparado alguna vez tu calle?","qau":"1da6293c58","aau":"eee2ab982b"},{"q":"What will be done in your city next year?","a":"A new metro line will be opened.","es":"¿Qué se hará en tu ciudad el próximo año?","qau":"28ca956f40","aau":"66c0115be1"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe 6 oraciones en voz pasiva sobre tu ciudad o tu empresa usando tiempos diferentes (presente, pasado, present perfect, continuo, futuro y modal).","kw":["was","has been","will be","is being"],"n":6,"model":"My city was founded in 1616. Coffee is grown in the region. A new hospital is being built downtown. The main park has been renovated. A new airport will be opened in 2028. More trees should be planted in the streets."}},{"id":"t11p2","topic":11,"part":2,"title":"News, rumors and processes","es":"Noticias, rumores y procesos","acts":["learn","passiveFactoryConveyor","dialogue","typeSentence","bubblePop","speak"],"tip":"<p>📰 La <b>pasiva impersonal</b> es típica de noticias y textos formales. Hay dos estructuras:</p>\n<p>1️⃣ <b>It + is said / believed / thought / reported / expected + that…</b><br>\n<i><b>It is believed that</b> the thief is in Miami.</i></p>\n<p>2️⃣ <b>Sujeto + is said / believed… + to + infinitivo</b><br>\n• Presente: <i>The thief <b>is believed to be</b> in Miami.</i><br>\n• En progreso: <i>He <b>is thought to be hiding</b>.</i><br>\n• Pasado: <i>He <b>is said to have left</b> the country.</i> (<b>to have + participio</b>)</p>\n<p>🏭 Para <b>describir procesos</b> se usa el presente pasivo con conectores: <b>First, … Then, … After that, … Finally, …</b> — <i>First, the beans <b>are roasted</b>.</i></p>\n<p>🗞️ Los <b>titulares</b> omiten el verbo <i>be</i>: <i>\"Bank <b>Robbed</b> in Dallas\"</i> = <i>A bank was robbed in Dallas.</i></p>","tips":["<b>allegedly</b> suena <i>əlédʒidli</i>.","<b>believed</b> termina con un sonido <i>d</i> suave: <i>bilívd</i>.","<b>thought</b> en EE. UU. suena <i>zot</i>, la 'gh' no se pronuncia."],"vocab":[{"en":"It is said that…","es":"Se dice que…","img":"u:photo-1482356432770-3a99f07aba35","v":"f","au":"424c3fe0f0"},{"en":"He is believed to be…","es":"Se cree que él está…","img":"u:photo-1544502062-f82887f03d1c","v":"m","au":"5d90c2fc7a"},{"en":"She is thought to have…","es":"Se piensa que ella ha…","img":"u:photo-1702047129200-89734f555f38","v":"f","au":"11980dbff3"},{"en":"It is reported that…","es":"Se informa que…","img":"u:photo-1578593139775-971441c3c518","v":"m","au":"015689923a"},{"en":"is expected to","es":"se espera que","img":"u:photo-1573358695783-005699a7fc94","v":"f","au":"1927227d5d"},{"en":"a headline","es":"un titular","img":"u:photo-1504711434969-e33886168f5c","v":"m","au":"6bbf4d9ef5"},{"en":"the beans are roasted","es":"los granos se tuestan","img":"u:photo-1447933601403-0c6688de566e","v":"f","au":"2804ebf9a6"},{"en":"the grapes are harvested","es":"las uvas se cosechan","img":"u:photo-1759742269093-de3d9fed6714","v":"m","au":"7d0c4e95d8"},{"en":"the parts are assembled","es":"las piezas se ensamblan","img":"u:photo-1716191299980-a6e8827ba10b","v":"f","au":"29d9059d13"},{"en":"it is then packaged","es":"luego se empaca","img":"u:photo-1684695749267-233af13276d0","v":"m","au":"f307f5553f"},{"en":"allegedly","es":"supuestamente","img":"u:photo-1768839721041-437940836abb","v":"f","au":"0bceeae3b2"},{"en":"to be estimated","es":"calcularse / estimarse","img":"u:photo-1707157284454-553ef0a4ed0d","v":"m","au":"8bd76974e4"}],"sentences":[{"en":"It is said that the hotel is haunted.","es":"Se dice que el hotel está embrujado.","img":"u:photo-1544209912-78c662d72f73","v":"f","au":"d91d80b028"},{"en":"The suspect is believed to have left the country.","es":"Se cree que el sospechoso salió del país.","img":"u:photo-1553619948-505cc1cdc320","v":"m","au":"fa26e3fcaf"},{"en":"The coffee beans are roasted at high temperatures.","es":"Los granos de café se tuestan a altas temperaturas.","img":"u:photo-1447933601403-0c6688de566e","v":"f","au":"9413d82982"},{"en":"Thousands of cars are produced here every day.","es":"Aquí se producen miles de carros cada día.","img":"u:photo-1716191299980-a6e8827ba10b","v":"m","au":"f1b8e164d8"},{"en":"The new stadium is expected to open in May.","es":"Se espera que el nuevo estadio abra en mayo.","img":"u:photo-1761941336817-1c258e7ef78c","v":"f","au":"340db679d1"}],"fill":[{"s":"It ___ that prices will rise again.","a":"is said","o":["says","is saying"],"h":"It + is said + that","full":"It is said that prices will rise again.","au":"ec87a0fc75"},{"s":"He is believed ___ in Miami now.","a":"to be living","o":["living","to living"],"h":"is believed + to + infinitivo","full":"He is believed to be living in Miami now.","au":"b2cd9a8fe8"},{"s":"The singer is thought ___ the band last year.","a":"to have left","o":["to leave","leaving"],"h":"pasado → to have + participio","full":"The singer is thought to have left the band last year.","au":"4510868a96"},{"s":"First, the grapes ___ by hand.","a":"are picked","o":["pick","are picking"],"h":"proceso → presente pasivo","full":"First, the grapes are picked by hand.","au":"8feb34e59d"},{"s":"The fire is reported ___ at 3 a.m.","a":"to have started","o":["to start","starting"],"h":"hecho pasado → to have + participio","full":"The fire is reported to have started at 3 a.m.","au":"2905eed910"},{"s":"It ___ that the CEO will resign.","a":"is rumored","o":["rumors","is rumoring"],"h":"rumor → it is rumored","full":"It is rumored that the CEO will resign.","au":"901302b089"}],"dialogue":{"title":"The evening news","es":"El noticiero de la noche","img":"u:photo-1578593139775-971441c3c518","lines":[{"who":"Anchor","v":"f","t":"Good evening. Our top story: a rare painting has been stolen from a museum in Philadelphia.","au":"ea897f47dc"},{"who":"Reporter","v":"m","t":"That's right, Karen. The painting is believed to be worth twelve million dollars.","au":"1e6748914b"},{"who":"Anchor","v":"f","t":"Do the police have any suspects?","au":"a0c233ec87"},{"who":"Reporter","v":"m","t":"Two men are thought to have entered the building through the roof.","au":"ffe9e1ef05"},{"who":"Anchor","v":"f","t":"Incredible. Was anyone hurt?","au":"c65d44f706"},{"who":"Reporter","v":"m","t":"No. A security guard was tied up, but he wasn't injured.","au":"0d17742026"},{"who":"Anchor","v":"f","t":"And what happens next?","au":"cf4eb961b6"},{"who":"Reporter","v":"m","t":"A reward is expected to be offered tomorrow. Back to you, Karen.","au":"aa0c0a42a3"}],"q":[{"q":"What was stolen?","a":"A rare painting.","o":["A car.","Twelve million dollars in cash."]},{"q":"How did the thieves get in?","a":"Through the roof.","o":["Through the front door.","Through a window."]},{"q":"What is expected tomorrow?","a":"A reward will be offered.","o":["The painting will be found.","The museum will close."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To understand news language and describe processes with the impersonal passive.","es":"Entender el lenguaje de las noticias y describir procesos con la pasiva impersonal."},"warm":[{"q":"Where do you usually get your news?","au":"4b91f026eb","es":"¿Dónde sueles informarte de las noticias?","ex":"I usually read the news on my phone."},{"q":"Do you believe everything you read in headlines?","au":"14bc398fd7","es":"¿Crees todo lo que lees en los titulares?","ex":"No, I always check other sources."}],"reading":{"title":"From the farm to your cup","img":"u:photo-1447933601403-0c6688de566e","text":"Coffee is said to be the second most traded commodity in the world, and the journey of a single cup is surprisingly long. First, the coffee cherries are picked by hand, often on steep mountain farms. The cherries are then washed and the beans are separated from the fruit. After that, the beans are dried in the sun for up to two weeks and are carefully turned several times a day. Once they are dry, they are sorted by size and quality, packed in large bags and shipped to roasters around the world. In a roastery in Seattle or Portland, the green beans are roasted at temperatures of around 400 degrees Fahrenheit, which is when their famous aroma is created. Finally, the coffee is ground, packaged and sold. It is estimated that more than two billion cups are consumed every day. However, the industry faces problems. Many small farmers are believed to earn less than they did twenty years ago, and climate change is expected to reduce suitable farmland. It is reported that some companies have begun to pay fairer prices. The next time you order a latte, remember how many hands it has passed through.","au":"552ebd3b48","q":[{"s":"Coffee cherries are often picked by hand.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The beans are dried in the sun for up to two months.","a":"no"},{"s":"The beans are roasted at around 400 degrees Fahrenheit.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Small farmers are believed to earn much more than twenty years ago.","a":"no"},{"s":"Climate change is expected to reduce suitable farmland.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"How is coffee made?","a":"First, the beans are picked. Then they are dried and roasted.","es":"¿Cómo se hace el café?","qau":"e720207f13","aau":"206773f126"},{"q":"What is said about your city?","a":"It is said that it has the best food in the country.","es":"¿Qué se dice de tu ciudad?","qau":"f711a53682","aau":"91a8486e52"},{"q":"Who is believed to be the richest person in the world?","a":"He is believed to be a tech entrepreneur.","es":"¿Quién se cree que es la persona más rica del mundo?","qau":"6002ff6f11","aau":"3ddf6a8120"}],"hw":{"es":"Describe un proceso que conozcas (hacer arepas, fabricar un producto, enviar un paquete) en 6 pasos con voz pasiva y conectores (First, Then, After that, Finally).","kw":["first","then","is","are"],"n":6,"model":"First, the corn is cooked. Then it is ground into dough. After that, salt and water are added. The dough is shaped into small circles. Then the arepas are grilled on both sides. Finally, they are served with cheese and butter."}}]},{"n":12,"title":"Have Something Done","es":"Have/get something done","cover":"u:photo-1593702275687-f8b402bf1fb5","parts":[{"id":"t12p1","topic":12,"part":1,"title":"Services: having things done","es":"Servicios: mandar a hacer algo","acts":["learn","causativeServiceCity","sort","fill","memory","speak"],"tip":"<p>Usamos <b>have + objeto + participio</b> cuando <b>otra persona</b> (un profesional) hace algo <b>por nosotros</b>, normalmente porque le pagamos.</p>\n<p>✂️ <i>I cut my hair.</i> = me lo corté yo mismo 😬<br>\n💈 <i>I <b>had my hair cut</b>.</i> = fui a la peluquería y me lo cortaron.</p>\n<p>⏰ El verbo <b>have</b> cambia de tiempo; el participio no cambia:<br>\n<i>I'm <b>having</b> my car serviced.</i> · <i>She <b>had</b> her nails done.</i> · <i>We've <b>had</b> the house painted.</i> · <i>I'll <b>have</b> it fixed.</i> · <i>You should <b>have</b> your eyes tested.</i></p>\n<p>❓ En preguntas y negativas usa <b>do/does/did</b>: <i>Where <b>do</b> you <b>have</b> your suits made?</i> · <i>I <b>didn't have</b> it repaired.</i></p>\n<p>💡 En español decimos <i>\"me corté el pelo\"</i> aunque lo haya hecho otra persona. ¡En inglés hay que decir <b>had</b>!</p>","tips":["<b>had my hair cut</b>: une las palabras, <i>hædmai hércat</i>.","<b>serviced</b> suena <i>sérvist</i>, terminación en 't'.","<b>tailored</b> suena <i>téilərd</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"have my hair cut","es":"cortarme el pelo (en la peluquería)","img":"u:photo-1593702275687-f8b402bf1fb5","v":"m","au":"a745c0de59"},{"en":"have my car serviced","es":"llevar el carro a mantenimiento","img":"u:photo-1625047509248-ec889cbff17f","v":"m","au":"f586573004"},{"en":"have my eyes tested","es":"hacerme examinar la vista","img":"u:photo-1539036776273-021ec1d78bec","v":"f","au":"90e104106c"},{"en":"have my nails done","es":"hacerme las uñas","img":"u:photo-1632345031435-8727f6897d53","v":"f","au":"16abd9aaf4"},{"en":"have a suit tailored","es":"mandar a hacer un traje a la medida","img":"u:photo-1508188317434-1fd219bb636f","v":"m","au":"c5dc267f89"},{"en":"have the locks changed","es":"mandar a cambiar las cerraduras","img":"u:photo-1562259929-b4e1fd3aef09","v":"m","au":"d5348dc8d7"},{"en":"have groceries delivered","es":"pedir el mercado a domicilio","img":"u:photo-1600728619239-d2a73f7aa541","v":"f","au":"c404506316"},{"en":"have the house painted","es":"mandar a pintar la casa","img":"u:photo-1759406066673-f76869a4e6db","v":"m","au":"e99d84b8fa"},{"en":"have my teeth cleaned","es":"hacerme una limpieza dental","img":"u:photo-1681939282781-341ac4f61996","v":"f","au":"c29db6178f"},{"en":"have a dress dry-cleaned","es":"mandar un vestido a la tintorería","img":"u:photo-1520434901111-8e9bcb42c628","v":"f","au":"52dc1c497d"},{"en":"do it yourself","es":"hazlo tú mismo","img":"u:photo-1426927308491-6380b6a9936f","v":"m","au":"c65cb19efb"},{"en":"a hair salon","es":"una peluquería","img":"u:photo-1600948836101-f9ffda59d250","v":"f","au":"02f82153ab"}],"sentences":[{"en":"I'm having my hair cut on Saturday.","es":"Me voy a cortar el pelo el sábado.","img":"u:photo-1593702275687-f8b402bf1fb5","v":"m","au":"76d54d5ba0"},{"en":"She had her car serviced last week.","es":"Llevó su carro a mantenimiento la semana pasada.","img":"u:photo-1625047509248-ec889cbff17f","v":"f","au":"648da49cb9"},{"en":"We need to have the roof repaired.","es":"Necesitamos mandar a arreglar el techo.","img":"u:photo-1726589004565-bedfba94d3a2","v":"m","au":"68c046456e"},{"en":"Where do you have your suits made?","es":"¿Dónde mandas a hacer tus trajes?","img":"u:photo-1508188317434-1fd219bb636f","v":"f","au":"6745b31067"},{"en":"They've just had their kitchen remodeled.","es":"Acaban de remodelar su cocina (con profesionales).","img":"u:photo-1628745277862-bc0b2d68c50c","v":"m","au":"31b2617ac4"},{"en":"You should have your eyes tested.","es":"Deberías hacerte examinar la vista.","img":"u:photo-1539036776273-021ec1d78bec","v":"f","au":"3910e29ab7"}],"fill":[{"s":"I had my hair ___ yesterday.","a":"cut","o":["cutting","to cut"],"h":"have + objeto + participio","full":"I had my hair cut yesterday.","au":"90ef551133"},{"s":"She is ___ her nails done right now.","a":"having","o":["had","have"],"h":"presente continuo de have","full":"She is having her nails done right now.","au":"026d25a338"},{"s":"We're going to have the house ___.","a":"painted","o":["paint","painting"],"h":"participio","full":"We're going to have the house painted.","au":"e58daa1907"},{"s":"He needs to have his eyes ___.","a":"tested","o":["test","testing"],"h":"participio","full":"He needs to have his eyes tested.","au":"8c0f00b0ed"},{"s":"Did you ___ your car washed?","a":"have","o":["had","having"],"h":"did + have (forma base)","full":"Did you have your car washed?","au":"e98cf625fb"},{"s":"I've ___ the locks changed.","a":"had","o":["have","having"],"h":"present perfect: have had","full":"I've had the locks changed.","au":"755c63a225"}],"sort":{"cats":["I did it myself","Someone did it for me"],"items":[{"w":"I painted my house.","c":"I did it myself","au":"2ca894b882"},{"w":"I had my house painted.","c":"Someone did it for me","au":"811c0b6999"},{"w":"She cut her hair.","c":"I did it myself","au":"c61393b8c1"},{"w":"She had her hair cut.","c":"Someone did it for me","au":"a946646a23"},{"w":"We fixed the sink.","c":"I did it myself","au":"e577f5e7e9"},{"w":"We had the sink fixed.","c":"Someone did it for me","au":"7803e40667"},{"w":"He's cleaning his car.","c":"I did it myself","au":"13c7ed081d"},{"w":"He's having his car cleaned.","c":"Someone did it for me","au":"837841c2cd"},{"w":"I built the website.","c":"I did it myself","au":"bd34832105"},{"w":"I had the website built.","c":"Someone did it for me","au":"ad151538d5"}]},"goal":{"en":"To talk about services using have something done.","es":"Hablar de servicios usando have something done."},"warm":[{"q":"How often do you have your hair cut?","au":"61acde7724","es":"¿Con qué frecuencia te cortas el pelo (en la peluquería)?","ex":"I have it cut once a month."},{"q":"Do you prefer to fix things yourself or to pay a professional?","au":"511d70726c","es":"¿Prefieres arreglar las cosas tú mismo o pagarle a un profesional?","ex":"I prefer to pay a professional. I'm terrible at fixing things."}],"reading":{"title":"The outsourcing generation","img":"u:photo-1600728619239-d2a73f7aa541","text":"Twenty years ago, most middle-class families in the United States did a lot of things themselves. They painted their own walls, washed their own cars and cooked almost every meal. Today, a growing number of busy professionals prefer to have these jobs done by someone else. Jessica, a nurse from Houston, is a typical example. She has her groceries delivered twice a week, has her car washed at a subscription car wash and has her apartment cleaned every other Friday. Last month, she even had her closet organized by a professional. \"I work twelve-hour shifts,\" she explains. \"Having things done for me isn't a luxury; it's how I protect my free time.\" Economists say apps have made these services cheaper and easier to book. However, not everyone agrees with this trend. Her neighbor Frank, a retired electrician, believes people are losing practical skills. \"My grandson had a light bulb changed by a handyman,\" he laughs. \"A light bulb!\" Frank still services his own car and has never had his lawn mowed by anyone else. The debate is interesting: is paying for services a smart use of money, or are we becoming too dependent? Most people, it seems, find a balance somewhere in the middle.","au":"087715a8a3","q":[{"s":"Jessica has her groceries delivered twice a week.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Jessica cleans her apartment herself every Friday.","a":"no"},{"s":"Jessica says having things done is a luxury.","a":"no"},{"s":"Frank is a retired electrician.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Frank has his lawn mowed by a company.","a":"no"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Where do you have your hair cut?","a":"I have it cut at a small barbershop near my house.","es":"¿Dónde te cortas el pelo?","qau":"0204ad2a70","aau":"dda51ec2b5"},{"q":"When did you last have your car serviced?","a":"I had it serviced two months ago.","es":"¿Cuándo llevaste tu carro a mantenimiento por última vez?","qau":"9eeeb5746f","aau":"11d83b1a97"},{"q":"What would you like to have done in your home?","a":"I'd like to have my kitchen remodeled.","es":"¿Qué te gustaría mandar a hacer en tu casa?","qau":"26a5f3a872","aau":"ee47b8c7b1"},{"q":"Do you have your groceries delivered?","a":"Sometimes, when I'm very busy.","es":"¿Pides el mercado a domicilio?","qau":"6372124744","aau":"9ca9007964"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe 6 oraciones sobre servicios que usas o quieres usar: qué mandas a hacer, dónde y con qué frecuencia (have + objeto + participio).","kw":["have","had","done"],"n":6,"model":"I have my hair cut every month. I had my car serviced last week. I'm going to have my apartment painted. I have my suits dry-cleaned. I've never had my nails done. Next year I want to have my kitchen remodeled."}},{"id":"t12p2","topic":12,"part":2,"title":"Get it done & bad experiences","es":"Get it done y malas experiencias","acts":["learn","causativeInsuranceClaim","dialogue","fill","spinWheel","speak"],"tip":"<p>🛠️ <b>get + objeto + participio</b> = igual que <i>have something done</i>, pero más <b>informal</b> y común al hablar: <i>I need to <b>get my phone fixed</b>.</i></p>\n<p>😱 La misma estructura sirve para <b>malas experiencias</b> que <b>nos pasaron</b> (nadie lo pidió): <i>I <b>had my wallet stolen</b>.</i> = me robaron la billetera. · <i>She <b>got her car towed</b>.</i> = le remolcaron el carro.</p>\n<p>👷 Para decir <b>quién</b> lo hace:<br>\n• <b>have + persona + verbo base</b>: <i>I <b>had the mechanic check</b> the brakes.</i><br>\n• <b>get + persona + to + verbo</b>: <i>I <b>got my brother to help</b> me.</i> (lo convencí)</p>\n<p>⚠️ No confundas: <i>I had stolen</i> (yo había robado 😳) ≠ <i>I <b>had my phone stolen</b></i> (me robaron el teléfono).</p>","tips":["<b>towed</b> suena igual que <b>toad</b>: <i>toud</i>.","<b>stolen</b> se dice <i>stóulən</i>.","<b>searched</b> suena <i>sercht</i>, una sílaba."],"vocab":[{"en":"get my phone fixed","es":"mandar a arreglar mi teléfono","img":"u:photo-1639776738932-956082f0b704","v":"m","au":"2452e1b2de"},{"en":"get my visa renewed","es":"renovar mi visa (trámite)","img":"u:photo-1581553673739-c4906b5d0de8","v":"f","au":"ac655b8968"},{"en":"have my wallet stolen","es":"que me roben la billetera","img":"u:photo-1579014134953-1580d7f123f3","v":"m","au":"e04ca5471e"},{"en":"have my flight canceled","es":"que me cancelen el vuelo","img":"u:photo-1746125047145-d6698eef563a","v":"f","au":"383669f103"},{"en":"get my car towed","es":"que me remolquen el carro","img":"u:photo-1730514784243-f0e7f09c9f50","v":"m","au":"3e06239877"},{"en":"have my bag searched","es":"que me revisen el bolso","img":"u:photo-1762965119363-af950b523dca","v":"f","au":"be36c0e7ec"},{"en":"have the mechanic check it","es":"hacer que el mecánico lo revise","img":"u:photo-1625047509248-ec889cbff17f","v":"m","au":"42878c361e"},{"en":"get someone to help","es":"conseguir que alguien ayude","img":"u:photo-1523543659209-5c57c05834aa","v":"f","au":"3e0bc10fba"},{"en":"get my account hacked","es":"que me hackeen la cuenta","img":"u:photo-1562813733-b31f71025d54","v":"m","au":"ab0c7c70e7"},{"en":"have my identity stolen","es":"que me roben la identidad","img":"u:photo-1613243555988-441166d4d6fd","v":"f","au":"4ca03a3502"},{"en":"file a claim","es":"presentar un reclamo","img":"u:photo-1637763723578-79a4ca9225f7","v":"m","au":"3ea168035d"},{"en":"a nightmare trip","es":"un viaje de pesadilla","img":"u:photo-1675299363766-123ac94461c7","v":"f","au":"4590e9ce21"}],"sentences":[{"en":"I had my wallet stolen on the subway.","es":"Me robaron la billetera en el metro.","img":"u:photo-1579014134953-1580d7f123f3","v":"m","au":"e5aef957a4"},{"en":"She got her car towed downtown.","es":"Le remolcaron el carro en el centro.","img":"u:photo-1730514784243-f0e7f09c9f50","v":"f","au":"e55151df30"},{"en":"We had our flight canceled twice.","es":"Nos cancelaron el vuelo dos veces.","img":"u:photo-1675299363766-123ac94461c7","v":"m","au":"e92c9fd5c6"},{"en":"I'll get my phone fixed tomorrow.","es":"Mañana mando a arreglar mi teléfono.","img":"u:photo-1639776738932-956082f0b704","v":"f","au":"6d315c3f97"},{"en":"I had the technician install the software.","es":"Hice que el técnico instalara el software.","img":"u:photo-1604754742629-3e5728249d73","v":"m","au":"70fd468c00"},{"en":"He got his account hacked last month.","es":"Le hackearon la cuenta el mes pasado.","img":"u:photo-1562813733-b31f71025d54","v":"f","au":"3480750dc4"}],"fill":[{"s":"I had my passport ___ at the airport.","a":"stolen","o":["stole","stealing"],"h":"mala experiencia: had + objeto + participio","full":"I had my passport stolen at the airport.","au":"a70fc742be"},{"s":"I'll ___ my brother to help me move.","a":"get","o":["have","make"],"h":"get + persona + to + verbo","full":"I'll get my brother to help me move.","au":"356be746b1"},{"s":"I had the plumber ___ the leak.","a":"fix","o":["fixed","to fix"],"h":"have + persona + verbo base","full":"I had the plumber fix the leak.","au":"3af600d2cd"},{"s":"She got her bike ___ last night.","a":"stolen","o":["steal","stealing"],"h":"get + objeto + participio","full":"She got her bike stolen last night.","au":"79900ecc80"},{"s":"We need to get the contract ___.","a":"translated","o":["translate","translating"],"h":"get + objeto + participio","full":"We need to get the contract translated.","au":"b755d03e22"},{"s":"He had his bag ___ at security.","a":"searched","o":["search","to search"],"h":"participio","full":"He had his bag searched at security.","au":"c9eae07a4d"}],"dialogue":{"title":"A nightmare trip","es":"Un viaje de pesadilla","img":"u:photo-1675299363766-123ac94461c7","lines":[{"who":"Mónica","v":"f","t":"Welcome back! How was Las Vegas?","au":"325412a640"},{"who":"Brian","v":"m","t":"Honestly? A nightmare. First, I had my flight canceled in Denver.","au":"5af26aba43"},{"who":"Mónica","v":"f","t":"Oh no! Did they put you on another one?","au":"21d25573f4"},{"who":"Brian","v":"m","t":"Eventually. Then I had my bag searched for an hour at security.","au":"7073f33cc1"},{"who":"Mónica","v":"f","t":"That sounds exhausting.","au":"487c77af57"},{"who":"Brian","v":"m","t":"It gets worse. On the second night, I had my wallet stolen at a casino.","au":"3ee07e0663"},{"who":"Mónica","v":"f","t":"No way! Did you report it?","au":"ffda4abc05"},{"who":"Brian","v":"m","t":"Yes, I got the hotel manager to call the police, and I'm filing a claim with my insurance.","au":"f587e3412d"}],"q":[{"q":"Where was Brian's flight canceled?","a":"In Denver.","o":["In Las Vegas.","In Phoenix."]},{"q":"What happened on the second night?","a":"He had his wallet stolen.","o":["He had his car towed.","He lost his passport."]},{"q":"Who did Brian get to call the police?","a":"The hotel manager.","o":["Mónica.","His insurance agent."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To describe bad experiences and arrange things with get / have something done.","es":"Describir malas experiencias y gestionar cosas con get / have something done."},"warm":[{"q":"Have you ever had something stolen?","au":"b3b2c92425","es":"¿Alguna vez te han robado algo?","ex":"Yes, I had my bike stolen when I was a student."},{"q":"What is the worst travel experience you have ever had?","au":"ab8cb76085","es":"¿Cuál es la peor experiencia de viaje que has tenido?","ex":"I had my luggage lost on a trip to Mexico."}],"reading":{"title":"When travel goes wrong","img":"u:photo-1675299363766-123ac94461c7","text":"Every traveler has a horror story, but some trips are truly unforgettable. Last summer, Andrés, an accountant from Miami, flew to New Orleans for a weekend festival. Things started badly: he had his flight canceled because of a storm and spent the night on an airport bench. When he finally landed, he discovered that his suitcase had been sent to Dallas. The airline promised to have it delivered to his hotel, but it arrived two days later. On Saturday, he parked his rental car on a street with confusing signs and got it towed. To make things worse, he had his phone stolen while he was paying at the tow yard. Andrés could have gone home angry. Instead, he got the hotel receptionist to help him report the theft, had his bank cards blocked within minutes and got a new phone set up at a local store. He also filed claims with the airline and his travel insurance and eventually got most of his money back. \"I learned two things,\" he says. \"Always buy travel insurance, and always read parking signs twice.\" His experience shows how useful the causative is in English: it lets you describe things that happened to you, even when you didn't do them yourself.","au":"432ad874db","q":[{"s":"Andrés's flight was canceled because of a storm.","a":"yes"},{"s":"His suitcase arrived at the hotel the same day.","a":"no"},{"s":"He had his phone stolen at the tow yard.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The hotel receptionist helped him report the theft.","a":"yes"},{"s":"He didn't get any money back.","a":"no"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Have you ever had your phone stolen?","a":"Yes, I had it stolen on a bus two years ago.","es":"¿Alguna vez te robaron el teléfono?","qau":"3fa2071195","aau":"59d784615b"},{"q":"What do you need to get fixed this month?","a":"I need to get my laptop fixed.","es":"¿Qué necesitas mandar a arreglar este mes?","qau":"59cbee61b5","aau":"0c9300684c"},{"q":"Who do you get to help you when you move?","a":"I get my brothers to help me.","es":"¿A quién le pides ayuda cuando te mudas?","qau":"19f4f924b2","aau":"92c6e9ca59"}],"hw":{"es":"Cuenta una mala experiencia (real o inventada) en 6 oraciones usando had/got + objeto + participio y have/get + persona + verbo.","kw":["had","got","stolen"],"n":6,"model":"Last year I had a terrible week. First, I had my car towed downtown. Then I got my account hacked. I had my credit card blocked immediately. I got my brother to drive me to work. Finally, I had the mechanic check my car before my trip."}}]},{"n":13,"title":"Future Perfect and Continuous","es":"Futuro perfecto y futuro continuo","cover":"u:photo-1676287566973-7e25f18f12a9","parts":[{"id":"t13p1","topic":13,"part":1,"title":"Future continuous: this time tomorrow","es":"Futuro continuo: a esta hora mañana","acts":["learn","futureTimelineRadar","dialogue","fill","oddOneOut","speak"],"tip":"<p>🎬 El <b>futuro continuo</b> describe una acción que estará <b>en progreso</b> en un momento concreto del futuro. Fórmula: <b>will be + verbo-ing</b>.</p>\n<p>🕗 <i><b>This time tomorrow</b>, I'<b>ll be flying</b> to Denver.</i> (en ese momento estaré en pleno vuelo ✈️)<br>\n🚫 <i>Don't call at 9. I'<b>ll be driving</b>.</i></p>\n<p>📅 También se usa para planes que ocurrirán <b>como parte de la rutina</b>: <i>I'll be seeing Ana at the office anyway.</i></p>\n<p>🙏 <b>Will you be + -ing…?</b> es una forma <b>muy cortés</b> de preguntar por los planes de alguien sin presionar: <i><b>Will you be using</b> the car tonight?</i> (suena más amable que <i>Will you use…?</i>)</p>\n<p>➖ Negativo: <i>I <b>won't be working</b> on Friday.</i></p>","tips":["<b>I'll be</b> se contrae y suena <i>ail bi</i>.","<b>won't be</b> suena <i>uóum bi</i>: la 't' casi desaparece.","En <b>flying, driving, working</b> la '-ing' es suave: <i>-in</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"will be flying","es":"estaré volando","img":"u:photo-1539612793508-4539a972242b","v":"f","au":"d529fcb476"},{"en":"will be working","es":"estaré trabajando","img":"u:photo-1544717302-de2939b7ef71","v":"m","au":"8449d17551"},{"en":"will be lying on a beach","es":"estaré tumbado en una playa","img":"u:photo-1780335590030-71f033414f16","v":"f","au":"bb2e5d02cb"},{"en":"this time tomorrow","es":"mañana a esta hora","img":"u:photo-1563861826100-9cb868fdbe1c","v":"m","au":"71107e3369"},{"en":"at 8 p.m. tonight","es":"a las 8 p.m. esta noche","img":"u:photo-1768508949611-694cf58a303a","v":"f","au":"6329e8b9ed"},{"en":"in a few hours","es":"en unas horas","img":"u:photo-1501139083538-0139583c060f","v":"m","au":"8d36becebd"},{"en":"Will you be using…?","es":"¿Vas a usar…? (pregunta cortés)","img":"u:photo-1654119895136-6aad918f412c","v":"f","au":"935e9fc082"},{"en":"to be on the road","es":"estar en la carretera","img":"u:photo-1486673748761-a8d18475c757","v":"m","au":"821401b11f"},{"en":"to be in a meeting","es":"estar en una reunión","img":"u:photo-1758518731706-be5d5230e5a5","v":"f","au":"ae15ddc8fd"},{"en":"to be off duty","es":"estar fuera de servicio","img":"u:photo-1584432810601-6c7f27d2362b","v":"m","au":"d72d3ac0b7"},{"en":"to be on call","es":"estar de turno (disponible)","img":"u:photo-1758691462848-31a39258dbd8","v":"f","au":"4d50e4858f"},{"en":"jet-lagged","es":"con desfase horario","img":"u:photo-1530521954074-e64f6810b32d","v":"m","au":"9727d0eb4d"}],"sentences":[{"en":"This time tomorrow, I'll be flying to Denver.","es":"Mañana a esta hora estaré volando a Denver.","img":"u:photo-1539612793508-4539a972242b","v":"f","au":"19aaeaf3f0"},{"en":"Don't call at nine; I'll be driving.","es":"No llames a las nueve; estaré manejando.","img":"u:photo-1449965408869-eaa3f722e40d","v":"m","au":"95c0dec0ce"},{"en":"Will you be using the car tonight?","es":"¿Vas a usar el carro esta noche?","img":"u:photo-1589123592035-32858c974713","v":"f","au":"684edbfaa1"},{"en":"She'll be presenting at the conference all morning.","es":"Estará presentando en la conferencia toda la mañana.","img":"u:photo-1580894732444-8ecded7900cd","v":"m","au":"23cb993c10"},{"en":"In ten years, we'll be living abroad.","es":"En diez años estaremos viviendo en el exterior.","img":"u:photo-1769230378944-414c18863d00","v":"f","au":"e5a38ebe8c"}],"fill":[{"s":"At 10 a.m. tomorrow I ___ the client.","a":"will be meeting","o":["will have met","meet"],"h":"acción en progreso en un momento futuro","full":"At 10 a.m. tomorrow I will be meeting the client.","au":"e03513b0fa"},{"s":"Don't call me at 8. I ___ dinner.","a":"will be having","o":["will have had","have"],"h":"en progreso a las 8","full":"Don't call me at 8. I will be having dinner.","au":"e817295d8e"},{"s":"___ you be working late tonight?","a":"Will","o":["Are","Do"],"h":"Will you be + -ing","full":"Will you be working late tonight?","au":"59134b6b2e"},{"s":"This time next week, we ___ on a beach in Hawaii.","a":"will be lying","o":["will lie down","are lie"],"h":"en progreso la próxima semana","full":"This time next week, we will be lying on a beach in Hawaii.","au":"7c9edb8773"},{"s":"She won't ___ at the party; she'll be on call.","a":"be dancing","o":["dancing","dance"],"h":"won't be + -ing","full":"She won't be dancing at the party; she'll be on call.","au":"1cae533bac"}],"dialogue":{"title":"Across time zones","es":"Entre zonas horarias","img":"u:photo-1713947506048-80f76419b2fe","lines":[{"who":"Sofía","v":"f","t":"Hi Jake! Can we schedule the call with the Tokyo team for tomorrow?","au":"e043f8ed7d"},{"who":"Jake","v":"m","t":"Sure. What time works for you?","au":"015628aed7"},{"who":"Sofía","v":"f","t":"Not before ten. I'll be dropping the kids off at school.","au":"8d8208dd95"},{"who":"Jake","v":"m","t":"And at eleven I'll be meeting a client downtown. How about two?","au":"f4d5b34c71"},{"who":"Sofía","v":"f","t":"Hmm, at two p.m. here, they'll be sleeping in Tokyo. It'll be four a.m. there.","au":"56532d43b5"},{"who":"Jake","v":"m","t":"Good point. What about six p.m.? They'll be starting their workday.","au":"8c11cf60f8"},{"who":"Sofía","v":"f","t":"Perfect. Will you be using the conference room then?","au":"ad63d8b7ca"},{"who":"Jake","v":"m","t":"No, it's all yours.","au":"43e325350e"}],"q":[{"q":"Why can't Sofía talk before ten?","a":"She'll be dropping off her kids.","o":["She'll be sleeping.","She'll be in Tokyo."]},{"q":"What will Jake be doing at eleven?","a":"Meeting a client downtown.","o":["Flying to Tokyo.","Having lunch."]},{"q":"Why is six p.m. a good time?","a":"The Tokyo team will be starting their workday.","o":["Jake will be off duty.","The office will be empty."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To describe actions in progress at a specific time in the future.","es":"Describir acciones en progreso en un momento específico del futuro."},"warm":[{"q":"What will you be doing this time tomorrow?","au":"5ab33e76ab","es":"¿Qué estarás haciendo mañana a esta hora?","ex":"I'll be working at the office."},{"q":"What will you be doing at eight o'clock tonight?","au":"7e0439e630","es":"¿Qué estarás haciendo a las ocho esta noche?","ex":"I'll be having dinner with my family."}],"reading":{"title":"A day in 2040","img":"u:photo-1580894732444-8ecded7900cd","text":"Futurists love to imagine ordinary days in the years ahead. Picture Daniela, a 38-year-old architect, on a Tuesday in 2040. At seven in the morning, she won't be sitting in traffic, because her self-driving car will be taking her to a client's site while she reviews plans on a transparent screen. At ten, she will be leading a virtual meeting with engineers in Seoul and Berlin, and real-time translation will be helping everyone understand each other. Around noon, a drone will be delivering lunch to her office terrace. In the afternoon, she will probably be working from a coworking space near the beach, since most companies will be offering flexible locations. At eight in the evening, Daniela will be relaxing at home while her kitchen robot is cooking dinner. Of course, not everyone agrees with this optimistic vision. Critics say that many people will still be commuting, struggling with high rents and worrying about job security. Some experts also warn that we will be spending even more time in front of screens. Whatever happens, the future continuous is the perfect tool to talk about it: it lets us zoom in on a precise moment and describe what will be happening right then.","au":"ea874a7337","q":[{"s":"Daniela is an architect.","a":"yes"},{"s":"At seven a.m. she will be driving her car herself.","a":"no"},{"s":"At ten she will be leading a virtual meeting.","a":"yes"},{"s":"A drone will be delivering her lunch.","a":"yes"},{"s":"All experts agree with this optimistic vision.","a":"no"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"What will you be doing at nine tomorrow morning?","a":"I'll be working at the office.","es":"¿Qué estarás haciendo mañana a las nueve de la mañana?","qau":"bc1e9a9f41","aau":"7fe9350cc7"},{"q":"Will you be using your car this weekend?","a":"No, I won't. You can borrow it.","es":"¿Vas a usar tu carro este fin de semana?","qau":"39bce29ce2","aau":"64aafce935"},{"q":"Where do you think you'll be living in ten years?","a":"I think I'll be living in another country.","es":"¿Dónde crees que estarás viviendo en diez años?","qau":"1f625ae911","aau":"52d6251ae1"}],"hw":{"es":"Describe tu día de mañana hora por hora (6 oraciones) usando will be + -ing (At 7 a.m. I'll be...).","kw":["will be","at"],"n":6,"model":"At 6 a.m. I'll be running in the park. At 8 I'll be having breakfast with my kids. At 10 I'll be meeting a client. At noon I'll be having lunch with my team. At 4 p.m. I'll be studying English. At 9 p.m. I'll be watching a series."}},{"id":"t13p2","topic":13,"part":2,"title":"Future perfect: deadlines and predictions","es":"Futuro perfecto: plazos y predicciones","acts":["learn","deadlineKanbanSprint","sort","fill","speed","speak"],"tip":"<p>✅ El <b>futuro perfecto</b> describe una acción que estará <b>terminada antes de</b> un momento del futuro. Fórmula: <b>will have + participio</b>.</p>\n<p>📌 Casi siempre va con <b>by</b> (<i>a más tardar / para</i>): <b>by Friday, by 2030, by then, by the time you arrive</b>.<br>\n<i><b>By Friday</b>, we'<b>ll have finished</b> the report.</i></p>\n<p>🔮 Es perfecto para <b>plazos</b> y <b>predicciones profesionales</b>: <i>By 2035, she'<b>ll have opened</b> her own firm.</i></p>\n<p>⚖️ <b>Comparación:</b><br>\n• <b>will be doing</b> → en progreso en ese momento: <i>At 3 p.m. I'll be writing the report.</i> ✍️<br>\n• <b>will have done</b> → ya terminado antes: <i>By 3 p.m. I'll have written the report.</i> ✅</p>\n<p>⚠️ Después de <b>by the time / when</b> usa <b>presente</b>: <i>By the time you <b>arrive</b> (❌ will arrive)…</i></p>","tips":["<b>I'll have</b> se contrae al hablar: <i>ail əv</i> (incluso <i>I'll've</i>).","<b>by the time</b> se dice rápido: <i>baiðə táim</i>.","<b>deadline</b> suena <i>dédlain</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"will have finished","es":"habrá terminado","img":"u:photo-1758520144658-c87be518b87e","v":"f","au":"c57ec03f11"},{"en":"by Friday","es":"para el viernes (a más tardar)","img":"u:photo-1676287566973-7e25f18f12a9","v":"m","au":"a62845ef88"},{"en":"by the end of the year","es":"para fin de año","img":"u:photo-1598807433318-5b53c43a28e2","v":"f","au":"fadd7c45c7"},{"en":"by then","es":"para entonces","img":"u:photo-1501139083538-0139583c060f","v":"m","au":"0b1551c531"},{"en":"a deadline","es":"una fecha límite","img":"u:photo-1775363949971-0e4919c66856","v":"f","au":"01b36cf6d5"},{"en":"to meet a deadline","es":"cumplir un plazo","img":"u:photo-1758520145147-c30bc656f314","v":"m","au":"c6756d38bf"},{"en":"to miss a deadline","es":"incumplir un plazo","img":"u:photo-1758598497429-6eb3895d5bfa","v":"f","au":"6873197d65"},{"en":"will have been promoted","es":"habrá sido ascendido","img":"u:photo-1758520144658-c87be518b87e","v":"m","au":"302fce49c5"},{"en":"to pay off a loan","es":"terminar de pagar un préstamo","img":"u:photo-1634128222187-18eababc763d","v":"f","au":"ecdcc03d31"},{"en":"to save up","es":"ahorrar (para algo)","img":"u:photo-1768839721719-c5ed97c1fd58","v":"m","au":"5ea0a3a3b3"},{"en":"will have retired","es":"se habrá jubilado","img":"u:photo-1508963493744-76fce69379c0","v":"f","au":"66e919afd1"},{"en":"a career milestone","es":"un hito profesional","img":"u:photo-1658235081483-8f06aa0882cf","v":"m","au":"dbbe00384c"}],"sentences":[{"en":"By Friday, we'll have finished the report.","es":"Para el viernes habremos terminado el informe.","img":"u:photo-1758520145147-c30bc656f314","v":"f","au":"ef426f18ad"},{"en":"By 2030, she'll have paid off her loan.","es":"Para 2030 habrá terminado de pagar su préstamo.","img":"u:photo-1634128222187-18eababc763d","v":"m","au":"e311b27486"},{"en":"Will you have read it by tomorrow?","es":"¿Lo habrás leído para mañana?","img":"u:photo-1495020689067-958852a7765e","v":"f","au":"7b0815ee92"},{"en":"He won't have arrived by then.","es":"No habrá llegado para entonces.","img":"u:photo-1771945029451-da143c6ea0e8","v":"m","au":"f138af66ba"},{"en":"By forty, I'll have started my own business.","es":"A los cuarenta habré empezado mi propio negocio.","img":"u:photo-1753351052617-62818ffc9173","v":"f","au":"4dbd3932b5"}],"fill":[{"s":"By 6 p.m. we ___ the project.","a":"will have finished","o":["will be finishing","will finish"],"h":"terminado antes de un momento","full":"By 6 p.m. we will have finished the project.","au":"a7bea46583"},{"s":"By next year, she ___ from college.","a":"will have graduated","o":["will graduate","graduates"],"h":"by + futuro → will have + participio","full":"By next year, she will have graduated from college.","au":"316acac6d5"},{"s":"Don't worry, I ___ the email by noon.","a":"will have sent","o":["will be sending","have sent"],"h":"terminado antes del mediodía","full":"Don't worry, I will have sent the email by noon.","au":"2723560a0b"},{"s":"At 3 p.m. tomorrow I ___ an interview.","a":"will be having","o":["will have had","have"],"h":"en progreso a las 3","full":"At 3 p.m. tomorrow I will be having an interview.","au":"de553ced4f"},{"s":"By the time you arrive, the movie ___.","a":"will have started","o":["will start","starts"],"h":"antes de que llegues","full":"By the time you arrive, the movie will have started.","au":"ee8e6286b4"},{"s":"___ you have finished by Monday?","a":"Will","o":["Are","Have"],"h":"Will you have + participio","full":"Will you have finished by Monday?","au":"d8c194f543"}],"sort":{"cats":["In progress (will be doing)","Completed (will have done)"],"items":[{"w":"At 9 tomorrow, I'll be driving.","c":"In progress (will be doing)","au":"683a855ff8"},{"w":"By 9 tomorrow, I'll have arrived.","c":"Completed (will have done)","au":"ee5dfbcda0"},{"w":"This time next week, she'll be skiing.","c":"In progress (will be doing)","au":"3376923593"},{"w":"By Monday, he'll have signed the deal.","c":"Completed (will have done)","au":"34b2bb8142"},{"w":"At noon, they'll be having lunch.","c":"In progress (will be doing)","au":"4856565a53"},{"w":"By noon, they'll have eaten.","c":"Completed (will have done)","au":"dacfc9dd3c"},{"w":"In 2030, I'll be running my company.","c":"In progress (will be doing)","au":"8222af73ad"},{"w":"By 2030, I'll have paid off my loan.","c":"Completed (will have done)","au":"780b983fb8"},{"w":"Tonight at 8, we'll be watching the game.","c":"In progress (will be doing)","au":"8215b22b1e"},{"w":"By midnight, the game will have ended.","c":"Completed (will have done)","au":"bcc6b7c45e"}]},"goal":{"en":"To talk about deadlines and make career predictions with the future perfect.","es":"Hablar de plazos y hacer predicciones profesionales con el futuro perfecto."},"warm":[{"q":"What do you want to have achieved by the end of this year?","au":"fd0bbbb2cc","es":"¿Qué quieres haber logrado para fin de año?","ex":"I want to have finished this English course."},{"q":"Do you usually meet your deadlines?","au":"9e990449aa","es":"¿Sueles cumplir tus plazos?","ex":"Yes, I usually do, but sometimes I need an extra day."}],"reading":{"title":"Your five-year plan","img":"u:photo-1758520144658-c87be518b87e","text":"\"Where do you see yourself in five years?\" It's one of the most common interview questions, and many people answer it badly. Career coach Monica Reyes, who works with professionals in Los Angeles, recommends using concrete milestones instead of vague dreams. \"Don't say 'I want to grow,'\" she explains. \"Say 'By 2030, I'll have completed my MBA and I'll have managed at least two international projects.'\" The future perfect makes your plan sound measurable. Reyes asks her clients to build a timeline with deadlines. One client, Jorge, an accountant, wrote: by the end of this year, I'll have passed my CPA exam; by next summer, I'll have paid off my student loan; and in three years, I'll have been promoted to senior manager. He also included what he would be doing day to day, such as mentoring junior staff. Reyes says the exercise works because it turns big ambitions into small, dated steps. If you miss a deadline, you simply adjust the plan. Of course, life is unpredictable. A promotion might come early, or the industry might change completely. Still, people who write clear plans are more likely to reach their goals. By the time you finish this class, you will have learned the perfect grammar to write yours.","au":"74213dc7e7","q":[{"s":"Monica Reyes recommends vague answers about growth.","a":"no"},{"s":"The future perfect makes a plan sound measurable.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Jorge is an accountant.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Jorge plans to pay off his student loan by next summer.","a":"yes"},{"s":"According to Reyes, missing a deadline means the plan has failed.","a":"no"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"What will you have done by the end of this year?","a":"I'll have finished this English course.","es":"¿Qué habrás hecho para fin de año?","qau":"f470d62638","aau":"a1f0e5f2ce"},{"q":"Where do you see yourself in five years?","a":"By then, I'll have been promoted to manager.","es":"¿Dónde te ves en cinco años?","qau":"e218550ac8","aau":"9d0d903343"},{"q":"Will you have finished your project by Friday?","a":"Yes, I'll have finished it by Thursday.","es":"¿Habrás terminado tu proyecto para el viernes?","qau":"8cd24c598f","aau":"76206cb6fc"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe tu plan de 5 años con 6 metas usando will have + participio y by (by next year, by 2030, by the time I'm 40...).","kw":["will have","by"],"n":6,"model":"By the end of this year, I'll have finished this course. By next June, I'll have saved enough money for a car. By 2028, I'll have been promoted. By 2029, I'll have visited New York. By the time I'm 40, I'll have bought a house. By 2031, I'll have started my own business."}}]},{"n":14,"title":"The Future Perfect Continuous","es":"El futuro perfecto continuo","cover":"u:photo-1613936360976-8f35cf0e5461","parts":[{"id":"t14p1","topic":14,"part":1,"title":"How long by then?","es":"¿Cuánto tiempo para entonces?","acts":["learn","milestoneOdometerRoll","dialogue","fill","unscramble","speak"],"tip":"<p>⏳ El <b>futuro perfecto continuo</b> mide <b>cuánto tiempo</b> habrá durado una actividad cuando llegue un momento futuro. Fórmula: <b>will have been + verbo-ing</b> + <b>for</b> (duración).</p>\n<p>📏 <i><b>By June</b>, I'<b>ll have been working</b> here <b>for ten years</b>.</i> (empecé en el pasado, sigo, y en junio cumpliré 10 años)</p>\n<p>😮‍💨 También explica <b>causas</b> de un estado futuro: <i>She'll be exhausted — she'<b>ll have been driving</b> all day.</i></p>\n<p>❓ Pregunta: <i><b>How long will</b> you <b>have been</b> living here <b>by</b> December?</i></p>\n<p>💡 En español solemos decir <b>\"llevaré…\"</b>: <i>En junio <b>llevaré</b> diez años trabajando aquí.</i> ¡Esa es la pista para usar este tiempo!</p>","tips":["Contráelo al hablar: <i>I'll have been</i> → <i>ail əv bin</i>.","<b>for</b> en frases de duración suena débil: <i>fər</i>.","<b>exhausted</b> se pronuncia <i>igzóstid</i> (la 'h' no suena)."],"vocab":[{"en":"will have been working","es":"habrá estado trabajando","img":"u:photo-1544717302-de2939b7ef71","v":"f","au":"ebc96340a1"},{"en":"for ten years","es":"durante diez años","img":"u:photo-1607482369189-a53b6e71fa48","v":"m","au":"16e929bec3"},{"en":"by next June","es":"para junio del próximo año","img":"u:photo-1676287566973-7e25f18f12a9","v":"f","au":"db433a1b0d"},{"en":"will have been living","es":"habrá estado viviendo","img":"u:photo-1609220136736-443140cffec6","v":"m","au":"10d8098745"},{"en":"will have been studying","es":"habrá estado estudiando","img":"u:photo-1741699428220-65f37f3fbbcb","v":"f","au":"436442acd5"},{"en":"will have been waiting","es":"habrá estado esperando","img":"u:photo-1613018274564-bec35a774995","v":"m","au":"e8afc6aa55"},{"en":"will have been running","es":"habrá estado corriendo","img":"u:photo-1613936360976-8f35cf0e5461","v":"f","au":"fc3022cba9"},{"en":"a work anniversary","es":"un aniversario laboral","img":"u:photo-1758520144658-c87be518b87e","v":"m","au":"573e4ab555"},{"en":"three days in a row","es":"tres días seguidos","img":"u:photo-1633526543814-9718c8922b7a","v":"f","au":"03a82d4752"},{"en":"non-stop","es":"sin parar","img":"u:photo-1461773518188-b3e86f98242f","v":"m","au":"d8e3d5c7ca"},{"en":"exhausted","es":"agotado","img":"u:photo-1493836512294-502baa1986e2","v":"m","au":"376933ab5c"},{"en":"a milestone","es":"un hito","img":"u:photo-1789899594273-1e8031a233d0","v":"f","au":"a49c7add72"}],"sentences":[{"en":"By June, I'll have been working here for ten years.","es":"En junio llevaré diez años trabajando aquí.","img":"u:photo-1758520144658-c87be518b87e","v":"f","au":"d40781d499"},{"en":"She'll have been studying for six hours by midnight.","es":"A medianoche llevará seis horas estudiando.","img":"u:photo-1741699428220-65f37f3fbbcb","v":"m","au":"d408119a5b"},{"en":"We'll have been living in Austin for a year.","es":"Llevaremos un año viviendo en Austin.","img":"u:photo-1588993608283-7f0eda4438be","v":"f","au":"705b95dfd9"},{"en":"They'll have been running for three hours.","es":"Llevarán tres horas corriendo.","img":"u:photo-1613936360976-8f35cf0e5461","v":"m","au":"2736657617"},{"en":"How long will you have been waiting?","es":"¿Cuánto tiempo llevarás esperando?","img":"u:photo-1613018274564-bec35a774995","v":"f","au":"1961e7fff6"},{"en":"He'll be exhausted; he'll have been driving all night.","es":"Estará agotado; habrá manejado toda la noche.","img":"u:photo-1449965408869-eaa3f722e40d","v":"m","au":"aace315929"}],"fill":[{"s":"By May, I ___ English for two years.","a":"will have been studying","o":["will be studied","am studying"],"h":"duración hasta mayo","full":"By May, I will have been studying English for two years.","au":"7077a2ee6a"},{"s":"By 2027, they ___ in Denver for a decade.","a":"will have been living","o":["will been living","have been living"],"h":"will have been + -ing","full":"By 2027, they will have been living in Denver for a decade.","au":"be927c9ecb"},{"s":"When she retires, she ___ for 40 years.","a":"will have been teaching","o":["will be teach","has been teaching"],"h":"duración hasta un punto futuro","full":"When she retires, she will have been teaching for 40 years.","au":"5787b69bc2"},{"s":"How long ___ you have been working here by June?","a":"will","o":["do","are"],"h":"How long will you have been…?","full":"How long will you have been working here by June?","au":"7b11742599"},{"s":"By the time the plane lands, we ___ for 14 hours.","a":"will have been flying","o":["will have flying","are flying"],"h":"estructura completa","full":"By the time the plane lands, we will have been flying for 14 hours.","au":"352a8b1adb"},{"s":"He'll be tired because he ___ all day.","a":"will have been working","o":["will have been work","will working"],"h":"causa de un estado futuro","full":"He'll be tired because he will have been working all day.","au":"814d00bf86"}],"dialogue":{"title":"Planning a work anniversary","es":"Planeando un aniversario laboral","img":"u:photo-1758520144658-c87be518b87e","lines":[{"who":"Carmen","v":"f","t":"Did you know that next month Mr. Peterson will have been working here for thirty years?","au":"c006b14ad9"},{"who":"Ray","v":"m","t":"Thirty years? Wow, that's a real milestone. We should throw him a party.","au":"03f0cb5dd0"},{"who":"Carmen","v":"f","t":"Definitely. By then, he'll have been running the sales team for twenty of those years.","au":"87344eb01a"},{"who":"Ray","v":"m","t":"Let's make a video with messages from former employees.","au":"5516d7834f"},{"who":"Carmen","v":"f","t":"Great idea. I'll have been collecting messages for two weeks by the party.","au":"37acb77a83"},{"who":"Ray","v":"m","t":"And I'll order a cake. How many people are we expecting?","au":"935fdab187"},{"who":"Carmen","v":"f","t":"About fifty. Don't tell him, okay? It's a surprise.","au":"4d75d7832f"},{"who":"Ray","v":"m","t":"My lips are sealed!","au":"551b73aee2"}],"q":[{"q":"How long will Mr. Peterson have been working there?","a":"Thirty years.","o":["Twenty years.","Fifty years."]},{"q":"What will Carmen have been doing for two weeks?","a":"Collecting messages.","o":["Ordering cakes.","Running the sales team."]},{"q":"How many people are they expecting?","a":"About fifty.","o":["About thirty.","About twenty."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To express how long an activity will have lasted at a future moment.","es":"Expresar cuánto tiempo habrá durado una actividad en un momento futuro."},"warm":[{"q":"How long have you been studying English?","au":"2ae6abc81b","es":"¿Cuánto tiempo llevas estudiando inglés?","ex":"I've been studying English for three years."},{"q":"What activity have you been doing for many years?","au":"b49cb4cba6","es":"¿Qué actividad llevas muchos años haciendo?","ex":"I've been playing soccer since I was a kid."}],"reading":{"title":"A milestone worth celebrating","img":"u:photo-1758520144658-c87be518b87e","text":"Next March, Rosa Delgado will have been working as a nurse at a children's hospital in Phoenix for twenty-five years. She arrived from Guatemala at nineteen, speaking almost no English, and started as a cleaning assistant on the night shift. While she was working, she studied at a community college, and by the time she was twenty-six she had become a registered nurse. Her colleagues are now organizing a surprise celebration. By the day of the party, they will have been collecting photos and messages from former patients for over two months. One of those former patients, Kevin, is now a pediatric doctor at the same hospital. \"By then, I'll have been working with Rosa for six years,\" he says, \"and I still learn something from her every week.\" Rosa doesn't plan to retire soon. In fact, she has just started a master's degree in nursing education. \"When I finish, I will have been studying part-time for three years,\" she says with a smile. \"I'll be tired, but happy.\" Her story is a perfect example of the future perfect continuous: it measures the duration of an activity up to a future point and often explains why someone will feel tired, proud or experienced at that moment.","au":"830cec1d40","q":[{"s":"By next March, Rosa will have been working as a nurse for twenty-five years.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Rosa started at the hospital as a doctor.","a":"no"},{"s":"Kevin was once one of Rosa's patients.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Rosa is planning to retire next year.","a":"no"},{"s":"Rosa's master's degree will take three years part-time.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"How long will you have been working at your company by next year?","a":"By next year, I'll have been working there for five years.","es":"¿Cuánto tiempo llevarás trabajando en tu empresa el próximo año?","qau":"0bb653d879","aau":"3d8ebc03b8"},{"q":"How long will you have been studying English by December?","a":"I'll have been studying it for two years.","es":"¿Cuánto tiempo llevarás estudiando inglés en diciembre?","qau":"a4ba86160d","aau":"7e3a214608"},{"q":"Why will you be tired tonight?","a":"Because I'll have been working all day.","es":"¿Por qué estarás cansado esta noche?","qau":"4181e2dbc3","aau":"53e377c37f"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe 6 oraciones sobre actividades de tu vida usando will have been + -ing + for/since (trabajo, estudios, vivienda, deportes, relaciones).","kw":["will have been","for"],"n":6,"model":"By next June, I'll have been working at my company for eight years. By December, I'll have been studying English for a year. Next month, we'll have been living in this apartment for three years. By the end of the race, I'll have been running for two hours. By Christmas, my parents will have been married for thirty years. Tonight I'll be tired because I'll have been working since six."}},{"id":"t14p2","topic":14,"part":2,"title":"Result or duration?","es":"¿Resultado o duración?","acts":["learn","perfectContinuousRailSwitch","sort","fill","listenChoose","speak"],"tip":"<p>⚖️ ¿<b>Futuro perfecto</b> o <b>futuro perfecto continuo</b>? Pregúntate qué quieres destacar:</p>\n<p>✅ <b>Resultado / cantidad</b> (¿cuánto? ¿cuántos?) → <b>will have + participio</b><br>\n<i>By Friday, she'<b>ll have answered 200 emails</b>.</i></p>\n<p>⏳ <b>Duración / proceso</b> (¿cuánto tiempo?) → <b>will have been + -ing</b><br>\n<i>By Friday, she'<b>ll have been answering</b> emails <b>for five hours straight</b>.</i></p>\n<p>🧱 <b>Verbos de estado</b> (<b>know, be, own, believe, love</b>) <b>no</b> van en continuo: <i>Next month I'<b>ll have known</b> her for ten years.</i> (❌ <i>will have been knowing</i>)</p>\n<p>🔑 Pistas: números y cantidades → perfecto · <b>for / since / all day / non-stop</b> → continuo.</p>","tips":["Al hablar, enfatiza la cantidad: <i>three CHAPters</i>, <i>twenty MILES</i>.","<b>since</b> suena <i>sins</i>, corto.","<b>long-haul</b> se pronuncia <i>long jol</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"will have written three chapters","es":"habrá escrito tres capítulos","img":"u:photo-1515378791036-0648a3ef77b2","v":"f","au":"bb43a6c374"},{"en":"will have been writing for months","es":"llevará meses escribiendo","img":"u:photo-1488190211105-8b0e65b80b4e","v":"m","au":"fedd318eb3"},{"en":"will have saved $10,000","es":"habrá ahorrado 10.000 dólares","img":"u:photo-1768839721719-c5ed97c1fd58","v":"f","au":"cd3082e16b"},{"en":"will have been saving for years","es":"llevará años ahorrando","img":"u:photo-1633158829875-e5316a358c6f","v":"m","au":"6c8953735a"},{"en":"will have run 20 miles","es":"habrá corrido 20 millas","img":"u:photo-1766970096331-78c8af007a3b","v":"f","au":"b6d3b92ebf"},{"en":"will have been training since May","es":"llevará entrenando desde mayo","img":"u:photo-1778828494354-9b717d36dc99","v":"m","au":"87467b241a"},{"en":"a completed result","es":"un resultado terminado","img":"u:photo-1758520144658-c87be518b87e","v":"f","au":"24647fa038"},{"en":"an ongoing activity","es":"una actividad en curso","img":"u:photo-1529792083865-d23889753466","v":"m","au":"40153a4e2d"},{"en":"to hit a target","es":"alcanzar una meta","img":"u:photo-1596008194705-2091cd6764d4","v":"f","au":"0e7e493040"},{"en":"to keep track of","es":"llevar la cuenta de","img":"u:photo-1576243345690-4e4b79b63288","v":"m","au":"993e9edbb2"},{"en":"a long-haul flight","es":"un vuelo de larga distancia","img":"u:photo-1539612793508-4539a972242b","v":"f","au":"12caf1cedd"},{"en":"a fundraising campaign","es":"una campaña de recaudación","img":"u:photo-1560220604-1985ebfe28b1","v":"m","au":"a012a7dbab"}],"sentences":[{"en":"By December, I'll have saved ten thousand dollars.","es":"Para diciembre habré ahorrado diez mil dólares.","img":"u:photo-1768839721719-c5ed97c1fd58","v":"f","au":"89f506ebdd"},{"en":"By then, I'll have been saving for two years.","es":"Para entonces llevaré dos años ahorrando.","img":"u:photo-1633158829875-e5316a358c6f","v":"m","au":"09aa132533"},{"en":"She'll have written three books by 2030.","es":"Habrá escrito tres libros para 2030.","img":"u:photo-1488190211105-8b0e65b80b4e","v":"f","au":"396e6b3c75"},{"en":"By noon, he'll have been training for four hours.","es":"Al mediodía llevará cuatro horas entrenando.","img":"u:photo-1778828494354-9b717d36dc99","v":"m","au":"ba1594e092"},{"en":"We'll have raised fifty thousand dollars by Friday.","es":"Para el viernes habremos recaudado cincuenta mil dólares.","img":"u:photo-1560220604-1985ebfe28b1","v":"f","au":"ef400d1421"}],"fill":[{"s":"By Friday, she ___ 200 emails.","a":"will have answered","o":["will have been answering","will answer"],"h":"cantidad (resultado) → futuro perfecto","full":"By Friday, she will have answered 200 emails.","au":"ac1dde51a6"},{"s":"By Friday, she ___ emails for five hours straight.","a":"will have been answering","o":["will have answered","answers"],"h":"duración → continuo","full":"By Friday, she will have been answering emails for five hours straight.","au":"b7cc88909d"},{"s":"By the time we arrive, we ___ for 12 hours.","a":"will have been driving","o":["will have driven","drive"],"h":"duración (for 12 hours)","full":"By the time we arrive, we will have been driving for 12 hours.","au":"48cd764f1e"},{"s":"By the end of the trip, we ___ 900 miles.","a":"will have driven","o":["will have been driving","drive"],"h":"cantidad (900 miles)","full":"By the end of the trip, we will have driven 900 miles.","au":"561382f521"},{"s":"By June, they ___ the house.","a":"will have sold","o":["will have been selling","sold"],"h":"acción completa","full":"By June, they will have sold the house.","au":"c191a8bc44"},{"s":"I ___ him for ten years next month.","a":"will have known","o":["will have been knowing","am knowing"],"h":"know es verbo de estado: sin continuo","full":"I will have known him for ten years next month.","au":"8eff75e210"}],"sort":{"cats":["Result (will have done)","Duration (will have been doing)"],"items":[{"w":"will have read five books","c":"Result (will have done)","au":"b6002fa229"},{"w":"will have been reading all day","c":"Duration (will have been doing)","au":"2eb9f77b94"},{"w":"will have visited 12 countries","c":"Result (will have done)","au":"ded195ba9a"},{"w":"will have been traveling for a year","c":"Duration (will have been doing)","au":"4b1c0cb234"},{"w":"will have painted three rooms","c":"Result (will have done)","au":"e88d2911ed"},{"w":"will have been painting since 8 a.m.","c":"Duration (will have been doing)","au":"175f3e437e"},{"w":"will have finished the course","c":"Result (will have done)","au":"2291f62dbd"},{"w":"will have been studying for months","c":"Duration (will have been doing)","au":"5102162892"},{"w":"will have known her for years","c":"Result (will have done)","au":"9694107a97"},{"w":"will have been waiting for an hour","c":"Duration (will have been doing)","au":"017c31e934"}]},"goal":{"en":"To choose between the future perfect and the future perfect continuous.","es":"Elegir entre el futuro perfecto y el futuro perfecto continuo."},"warm":[{"q":"What are you saving money for?","au":"03fe1cf689","es":"¿Para qué estás ahorrando dinero?","ex":"I'm saving money for a trip to Europe."},{"q":"What is a big goal you are working on right now?","au":"921f9fc89b","es":"¿En qué gran meta estás trabajando ahora?","ex":"I'm working on getting a promotion."}],"reading":{"title":"Two ways to measure a goal","img":"u:photo-1766970096331-78c8af007a3b","text":"Fitness apps have taught millions of people to measure their progress in two different ways, and English grammar does exactly the same. Take Mike, a 45-year-old teacher from Portland who is training for his first marathon in November. His app tells him two kinds of information. The first is about results: by race day, he will have run more than 600 miles in training and will have completed four long runs of twenty miles. Those are numbers you can count, so we use the future perfect. The second is about duration: by race day, he will have been training for eight months and will have been waking up at five a.m. almost every weekend. That's an ongoing activity, so we use the future perfect continuous. Mike's wife, Laura, is working on a different goal. She is writing a novel. By the end of the year, she will have written twelve chapters, but she will have been writing for almost three years. Notice the logic: quantity and completion go with \"will have done,\" while \"how long\" goes with \"will have been doing.\" Remember, too, that state verbs such as know, own or believe do not use the continuous form: by November, Mike will have known his coach for a year.","au":"b8102313f5","q":[{"s":"Mike is training for his first marathon.","a":"yes"},{"s":"By race day, Mike will have run more than 600 miles.","a":"yes"},{"s":"\"He will have been training for eight months\" describes a result.","a":"no"},{"s":"Laura will have been writing her novel for about three years.","a":"yes"},{"s":"We say \"Mike will have been knowing his coach for a year.\"","a":"no"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"How much money will you have saved by December?","a":"I'll have saved about two thousand dollars.","es":"¿Cuánto dinero habrás ahorrado para diciembre?","qau":"54be2e3cc5","aau":"b7b49954e9"},{"q":"How long will you have been saving by then?","a":"I'll have been saving for a year.","es":"¿Cuánto tiempo llevarás ahorrando para entonces?","qau":"092b3b1af9","aau":"ac7d29dfa7"},{"q":"How many books will you have read by the end of the year?","a":"I'll have read about ten books.","es":"¿Cuántos libros habrás leído para fin de año?","qau":"2d0f4f594b","aau":"23025f57a5"}],"hw":{"es":"Elige una meta personal (ahorrar, entrenar, estudiar, escribir) y escribe 6 oraciones: 3 con el resultado (will have + participio) y 3 con la duración (will have been + -ing).","kw":["will have","will have been"],"n":6,"model":"By December, I'll have saved three thousand dollars. By then, I'll have been saving for ten months. By June, I'll have finished level B2. I'll have been studying English for two years. By my birthday, I'll have run three races. I'll have been training since January."}}]},{"n":15,"title":"Artificial Intelligence and Employment","es":"La inteligencia artificial y el empleo","cover":"u:photo-1777383975764-bec6f5cabf00","parts":[{"id":"t15p1","topic":15,"part":1,"title":"Class","es":"Debate: ¿la IA destruirá o transformará el empleo?","acts":["learn","aiArgumentForge","dialogue","fill","matchLines","speak"],"tip":"<p>En un debate de nivel <b>C1</b> no basta con decir <i>I think</i>. Usa estructuras que muestren que <b>piensas con matices</b>:</p>\n<p>🧠 <b>Presentar una postura</b>: <i>It could be argued that…</i> (se podría argumentar que…) · <i>There is a strong case for…</i> (hay buenos argumentos a favor de…) · <i>I would argue that…</i></p>\n<p>🤝 <b>Conceder</b> (reconocer el punto del otro): <b>While it is true that</b> AI saves time, <b>it</b> also… · <b>Admittedly,</b> … · <b>Granted,</b> …</p>\n<p>⚖️ <b>Contrastar</b>: <b>Nevertheless,</b> … · <b>Even so,</b> … · <b>That said,</b> … (van al inicio de la oración + coma).</p>\n<p>🏁 <b>Concluir</b>: <b>On balance,</b> the benefits <b>outweigh</b> the risks. · <b>All things considered,</b> …</p>\n<p>⚠️ <b>Despite</b> va con sustantivo o -ing (<i>despite the risks</i>), nunca con sujeto + verbo. Para eso usa <b>although</b>.</p>","tips":["<b>automation</b> lleva el acento en la tercera sílaba: <i>o-to-MÉI-shon</i>.","<b>outweigh</b> suena <i>aut-UÉI</i>: la 'gh' no se pronuncia.","En <b>It could be argued</b> une las palabras: <i>it-kud-bi-ÁR-guiud</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"automation","es":"automatización","img":"u:photo-1777383975764-bec6f5cabf00","v":"f","au":"b2cab9b443"},{"en":"job displacement","es":"desplazamiento laboral (pérdida de empleos)","img":"u:photo-1718220216044-006f43e3a9b1","v":"m","au":"a9fac26c83"},{"en":"to reskill workers","es":"recapacitar a los trabajadores","img":"u:photo-1719159381981-1327b22aff9b","v":"f","au":"4aaa86c000"},{"en":"the gig economy","es":"la economía de trabajos por encargo","img":"u:photo-1548695607-9c73430ba065","v":"m","au":"5cf97c1728"},{"en":"to augment human work","es":"potenciar (complementar) el trabajo humano","img":"u:photo-1758691462774-f01ed567f2c4","v":"f","au":"35d563365b"},{"en":"productivity gains","es":"aumentos de productividad","img":"u:photo-1652211955967-99c892925469","v":"m","au":"1ee0452db9"},{"en":"a skills gap","es":"una brecha de habilidades","img":"u:photo-1618758993113-2447833402d6","v":"f","au":"76c3c33d63"},{"en":"a safety net","es":"una red de protección (social)","img":"u:photo-1443933223857-9ca346228f72","v":"m","au":"1c6185bf8f"},{"en":"to outweigh","es":"superar (en peso o importancia)","img":"u:photo-1612012060851-20f943c02d3d","v":"f","au":"08ab6afe97"},{"en":"It could be argued that…","es":"Se podría argumentar que…","img":"#It could be argued that…","v":"m","au":"f6e3cf6314"},{"en":"While it is true that…, …","es":"Si bien es cierto que…, …","img":"#While it is true that…, …","v":"f","au":"406a32a8d2"},{"en":"On balance, …","es":"Sopesándolo todo / En términos generales, …","img":"#On balance, …","v":"m","au":"d25390ec43"}],"sentences":[{"en":"It could be argued that automation will create more jobs than it destroys.","es":"Se podría argumentar que la automatización creará más empleos de los que destruye.","img":"u:photo-1777383975764-bec6f5cabf00","v":"f","au":"1598cf5026"},{"en":"While it is true that AI boosts productivity, many workers fear job displacement.","es":"Si bien es cierto que la IA aumenta la productividad, muchos trabajadores temen perder su empleo.","img":"u:photo-1647964366344-bc680baf64e2","v":"m","au":"48725eb510"},{"en":"Governments should invest heavily in reskilling programs.","es":"Los gobiernos deberían invertir mucho en programas de recapacitación.","img":"u:photo-1719159381981-1327b22aff9b","v":"f","au":"903e295ba8"},{"en":"On balance, the benefits of AI seem to outweigh the risks.","es":"Sopesándolo todo, los beneficios de la IA parecen superar los riesgos.","img":"u:photo-1612012060851-20f943c02d3d","v":"m","au":"5c9ccc6959"},{"en":"AI is more likely to augment human work than to replace it entirely.","es":"Es más probable que la IA potencie el trabajo humano a que lo reemplace por completo.","img":"u:photo-1758691462774-f01ed567f2c4","v":"f","au":"1df3589d15"},{"en":"Without a stronger safety net, the transition could be painful for many families.","es":"Sin una red de protección más fuerte, la transición podría ser dolorosa para muchas familias.","img":"u:photo-1758523418820-a492bf647c63","v":"m","au":"befe8685a0"}],"fill":[{"s":"___ it is true that AI saves time, it also raises ethical concerns.","a":"While","o":["Despite","However"],"h":"concesión: While it is true that…, …","full":"While it is true that AI saves time, it also raises ethical concerns.","au":"deea682f5f"},{"s":"It could be ___ that machines will never fully replace human creativity.","a":"argued","o":["arguing","argue"],"h":"could be + participio (voz pasiva)","full":"It could be argued that machines will never fully replace human creativity.","au":"17cb180713"},{"s":"On ___, I believe the advantages outweigh the drawbacks.","a":"balance","o":["weigh","whole"],"h":"expresión fija para concluir","full":"On balance, I believe the advantages outweigh the drawbacks.","au":"94e6b6b34f"},{"s":"The potential gains far ___ the short-term costs.","a":"outweigh","o":["overweight","outrun"],"h":"superar en importancia","full":"The potential gains far outweigh the short-term costs.","au":"75805c3851"},{"s":"Many companies are investing in ___ their workforce instead of laying people off.","a":"reskilling","o":["reskill","reskilled"],"h":"después de preposición → -ing","full":"Many companies are investing in reskilling their workforce instead of laying people off.","au":"f2a75de6f4"},{"s":"Low-skilled workers are particularly ___ to automation.","a":"vulnerable","o":["vulnerability","sensible"],"h":"colocación: vulnerable to","full":"Low-skilled workers are particularly vulnerable to automation.","au":"38a5ea0c7e"},{"s":"___, critics point out that not everyone can retrain at fifty.","a":"Nevertheless","o":["Although","Despite"],"h":"conector + coma al inicio de la oración","full":"Nevertheless, critics point out that not everyone can retrain at fifty.","au":"2d65d307d5"}],"dialogue":{"title":"Will robots take our jobs?","es":"¿Nos quitarán el trabajo los robots?","img":"u:photo-1758518731706-be5d5230e5a5","lines":[{"who":"Maya","v":"f","t":"Honestly, I think AI is the biggest threat to employment we've ever faced. Entire professions could disappear.","au":"a25c0c161a"},{"who":"Ethan","v":"m","t":"I see where you're coming from, but history suggests otherwise. Every technological revolution has created more jobs than it destroyed.","au":"37fc5b4f02"},{"who":"Maya","v":"f","t":"That may have been the case with tractors or computers, but AI can learn. It isn't just replacing muscles; it's replacing minds.","au":"3e4d518e36"},{"who":"Ethan","v":"m","t":"Granted, the pace is faster this time. Even so, AI tends to augment workers rather than replace them entirely.","au":"3b830437d4"},{"who":"Dr. Ruiz","v":"f","t":"If I may jump in, I think you're both partly right. The real issue isn't whether jobs will change, but who pays for the transition.","au":"eafec7fbf0"},{"who":"Maya","v":"f","t":"Exactly. Without serious reskilling programs, older workers will simply be left behind.","au":"588f3659df"},{"who":"Ethan","v":"m","t":"On that point, I couldn't agree more. Companies that profit from automation should help fund retraining.","au":"bae547bc98"},{"who":"Dr. Ruiz","v":"f","t":"So, on balance, this debate is less about technology and more about policy.","au":"67b009b022"}],"q":[{"q":"What is Maya's main concern?","a":"That AI could make entire professions disappear.","o":["That AI is too expensive.","That robots are dangerous drivers."]},{"q":"What argument does Ethan use?","a":"Past technological revolutions created more jobs than they destroyed.","o":["AI will never learn anything new.","Workers prefer robots to people."]},{"q":"What do Maya and Ethan finally agree on?","a":"Companies should help fund retraining.","o":["AI should be banned.","Older workers should retire early."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To debate the impact of artificial intelligence on jobs, using language to argue, concede and conclude.","es":"Debatir el impacto de la inteligencia artificial en el empleo, usando lenguaje para argumentar, conceder y concluir."},"warm":[{"q":"Has technology ever changed the way you work or study?","au":"2afd0565b3","es":"¿Alguna vez la tecnología ha cambiado tu forma de trabajar o estudiar?","ex":"Yes, definitely. Since my company adopted AI tools, I spend far less time writing reports and more time talking to clients."},{"q":"Which jobs do you think are safest from automation?","au":"6889165d30","es":"¿Qué trabajos crees que están más a salvo de la automatización?","ex":"I'd say jobs that require empathy and judgment, like nurses, teachers, or therapists, are the hardest to automate."}],"reading":{"title":"Will AI Take Your Job?","img":"u:photo-1777383975764-bec6f5cabf00","text":"Few topics generate as much anxiety in today's workplace as artificial intelligence. Software can now draft reports, analyze medical scans, and answer customer questions in seconds, and many workers understandably wonder whether their jobs will survive the decade. Pessimists point out that, unlike earlier machines, AI performs cognitive tasks, not just physical ones. Accountants, translators, and paralegals, they argue, are no longer safe. If companies can cut costs by automating these roles, it is hard to see why they would not. Optimists, however, take a longer view. Every major technological shift, from the steam engine to the personal computer, destroyed some jobs while creating entirely new ones that no one could have predicted. Many economists suggest that AI is more likely to transform jobs than to eliminate them, taking over repetitive tasks and freeing people to focus on judgment, creativity, and human contact. While it is true that new jobs will appear, the transition may be painful. A fifty-year-old warehouse worker cannot easily become a data scientist. This is why the debate increasingly focuses on policy: who should pay for reskilling, and how should the safety net adapt? On balance, the real question is not whether AI will change work, since it already has, but whether societies will manage that change fairly. Technology itself is neutral; the outcomes depend on the choices we make.","au":"4f24fc8687","q":[{"s":"Pessimists believe AI only affects physical jobs.","a":"no"},{"s":"Optimists point to earlier technological revolutions as evidence.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Many economists suggest AI will mainly transform jobs rather than eliminate them.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The article says older workers can easily retrain as data scientists.","a":"no"},{"s":"The author concludes that the outcomes depend on our choices.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Do you think AI will create more jobs than it destroys?","a":"It could be argued that AI will create new jobs. While it is true that some roles will disappear, on balance I think the job market will adapt.","es":"¿Crees que la IA creará más empleos de los que destruirá?","qau":"dbcc79e56d","aau":"c4466b3e17"},{"q":"Who should pay for reskilling workers?","a":"In my view, the responsibility should be shared between governments and the companies that profit from automation.","es":"¿Quién debería pagar la recapacitación de los trabajadores?","qau":"5bf16deee4","aau":"25bb339d51"},{"q":"Would you trust an AI to make important decisions at work?","a":"To a certain extent, yes, but I believe a human should always have the final say.","es":"¿Confiarías en que una IA tome decisiones importantes en el trabajo?","qau":"96a6c72f8b","aau":"422091ec4a"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe un ensayo corto de opinión (120–150 palabras): ¿la inteligencia artificial es una amenaza o una oportunidad para el empleo? Usa al menos tres expresiones de debate (It could be argued that…, While it is true that…, On balance…).","kw":["It could be argued","While it is true","On balance"],"n":7,"model":"Artificial intelligence is often portrayed as a threat to employment, but I believe it is better understood as an opportunity, provided we manage it wisely. It could be argued that AI will eliminate millions of jobs, especially in administrative and customer service roles. While it is true that some positions will disappear, history shows that new technologies also create professions that did not exist before. Moreover, AI can take over repetitive tasks, allowing workers to focus on creative and interpersonal work. However, this transition will not happen automatically. Governments and companies should invest in reskilling programs and strengthen the safety net for those who are displaced. On balance, the benefits of AI outweigh the risks, but only if no one is left behind."}}]},{"n":16,"title":"Globalization: Benefits vs. Drawbacks","es":"Globalización: beneficios y desventajas","cover":"u:photo-1606185540834-d6e7483ee1a4","parts":[{"id":"t16p1","topic":16,"part":1,"title":"Class","es":"Debate: ¿la globalización nos beneficia a todos?","acts":["learn","globeRebuttalDuel","sort","listenChoose","dialogue","speak"],"tip":"<p>En un debate C1 debes <b>presentar las posturas de otros</b> antes de dar la tuya:</p>\n<p>👍 <b>Proponents argue that…</b> / <b>Supporters maintain that…</b> (los defensores sostienen que…)<br>👎 <b>Critics contend that…</b> / <b>Opponents claim that…</b> (los críticos sostienen que…)</p>\n<p>🥊 <b>Rebatir</b> (refutar) con elegancia: <i>That argument <b>overlooks</b>…</i> (pasa por alto…) · <i><b>This is not to say that</b> trade is harmful, but…</i> · <i><b>However compelling</b> the data may be, …</i> (por muy convincente que sea…)</p>\n<p>➕ <b>Añadir</b> un argumento paralelo: <b>By the same token,</b> … (del mismo modo) · <b>Furthermore,</b> …</p>\n<p>⚠️ Un buen contraargumento responde <b>directamente</b> a lo que dijo el otro. Atacar a la persona o cambiar de tema <b>no</b> es rebatir.</p>","tips":["<b>contend</b> lleva el acento al final: <i>con-TÉND</i>.","<b>homogenization</b>: <i>ho-MÁ-ye-ni-SÉI-shon</i>; respira y dila por partes.","<b>double-edged</b> suena <i>dábol-éyd</i>: la 'd' final casi no se oye."],"vocab":[{"en":"global supply chains","es":"cadenas de suministro globales","img":"u:photo-1606185540834-d6e7483ee1a4","v":"f","au":"1ffc2fdc5d"},{"en":"outsourcing","es":"tercerización (llevar trabajo al exterior)","img":"u:photo-1766066014237-00645c74e9c6","v":"m","au":"76b2dd6404"},{"en":"cultural homogenization","es":"homogeneización cultural","img":"u:photo-1765350657278-337911751097","v":"f","au":"56ff8fdee1"},{"en":"emerging economies","es":"economías emergentes","img":"u:photo-1772626375392-11cbe79c05c2","v":"m","au":"bf758438fd"},{"en":"to lift people out of poverty","es":"sacar a la gente de la pobreza","img":"u:photo-1758687126877-b37052a20a4d","v":"f","au":"b3fe47083b"},{"en":"a free trade agreement","es":"un tratado de libre comercio","img":"u:photo-1664463760781-f159dfe3af30","v":"m","au":"59e76625d8"},{"en":"local industries","es":"industrias locales","img":"u:photo-1528717384022-f8d665c86909","v":"f","au":"2f958dd3e8"},{"en":"interdependence","es":"interdependencia","img":"u:photo-1776057441344-38e0587ad1e6","v":"m","au":"b6d75db3cb"},{"en":"a double-edged sword","es":"un arma de doble filo","img":"#a double-edged sword ⚔️","v":"f","au":"0983f78007"},{"en":"Proponents argue that…","es":"Los defensores sostienen que…","img":"#Proponents argue that…","v":"m","au":"3b8acde0b0"},{"en":"Critics contend that…","es":"Los críticos sostienen que…","img":"#Critics contend that…","v":"f","au":"e4d30b369e"},{"en":"By the same token, …","es":"Del mismo modo / Por la misma razón, …","img":"#By the same token, …","v":"m","au":"dc692f372a"}],"sentences":[{"en":"Proponents argue that globalization has lifted millions of people out of poverty.","es":"Los defensores sostienen que la globalización ha sacado a millones de personas de la pobreza.","img":"u:photo-1758687126877-b37052a20a4d","v":"f","au":"46affddcc5"},{"en":"Critics contend that outsourcing has hollowed out many local industries.","es":"Los críticos sostienen que la tercerización ha debilitado muchas industrias locales.","img":"u:photo-1515178047238-5376b3c1484e","v":"m","au":"1e4d750a0d"},{"en":"Global supply chains proved fragile during the pandemic.","es":"Las cadenas de suministro globales demostraron ser frágiles durante la pandemia.","img":"u:photo-1606185540834-d6e7483ee1a4","v":"f","au":"6d22342a67"},{"en":"In many ways, globalization is a double-edged sword.","es":"En muchos sentidos, la globalización es un arma de doble filo.","img":"#a double-edged sword ⚔️","v":"m","au":"f2466f0d8f"},{"en":"By the same token, cultural exchange can enrich local traditions.","es":"Del mismo modo, el intercambio cultural puede enriquecer las tradiciones locales.","img":"u:photo-1777794817535-98136533a744","v":"f","au":"8dac66c603"}],"fill":[{"s":"Critics ___ that free trade benefits large corporations more than workers.","a":"contend","o":["content","contented"],"h":"sostener (una opinión)","full":"Critics contend that free trade benefits large corporations more than workers.","au":"d5477e980f"},{"s":"Globalization has helped ___ millions of people out of poverty.","a":"lift","o":["rise","arise"],"h":"colocación: lift people out of poverty","full":"Globalization has helped lift millions of people out of poverty.","au":"b9c77f8186"},{"s":"That argument ___ the environmental cost of shipping goods worldwide.","a":"overlooks","o":["oversees","overtakes"],"h":"pasar por alto","full":"That argument overlooks the environmental cost of shipping goods worldwide.","au":"c7bc93885c"},{"s":"This is not ___ say that trade is inherently harmful.","a":"to","o":["for","that"],"h":"This is not to say that…","full":"This is not to say that trade is inherently harmful.","au":"c4848aaf8e"},{"s":"Many small towns have become heavily ___ on a single foreign company.","a":"dependent","o":["depending","dependence"],"h":"colocación: dependent on","full":"Many small towns have become heavily dependent on a single foreign company.","au":"faa5e090fc"},{"s":"___ compelling the economic data may be, it doesn't capture the human cost.","a":"However","o":["Although","Despite"],"h":"However + adjetivo + may be","full":"However compelling the economic data may be, it doesn't capture the human cost.","au":"540e40a70a"}],"sort":{"cats":["Benefit","Drawback"],"items":[{"w":"cheaper consumer goods","c":"Benefit","au":"d2f9427180"},{"w":"access to new markets","c":"Benefit","au":"053ed152c9"},{"w":"transfer of technology","c":"Benefit","au":"9860383eb3"},{"w":"foreign investment","c":"Benefit","au":"7b1e78dcbf"},{"w":"cultural exchange","c":"Benefit","au":"3d42cb2293"},{"w":"job outsourcing","c":"Drawback","au":"a13c9d8a7e"},{"w":"cultural homogenization","c":"Drawback","au":"56ff8fdee1"},{"w":"exploitation of cheap labor","c":"Drawback","au":"f010d9845d"},{"w":"fragile supply chains","c":"Drawback","au":"df2e20cbfc"},{"w":"the environmental cost of shipping","c":"Drawback","au":"b19a50958d"}]},"dialogue":{"title":"Is globalization good for us?","es":"¿Es buena para nosotros la globalización?","img":"u:photo-1606185540834-d6e7483ee1a4","lines":[{"who":"Sofia","v":"f","t":"Thanks to globalization, I can buy a phone designed in California, assembled in Asia, and delivered to Phoenix in two days. That's remarkable.","au":"ad6afdd7a9"},{"who":"Daniel","v":"m","t":"Remarkable for consumers, perhaps. But my hometown in Ohio lost its main factory when production moved overseas.","au":"ae1e39456e"},{"who":"Sofia","v":"f","t":"I'm sorry to hear that. Still, proponents argue that trade has lifted hundreds of millions of people out of poverty.","au":"5e4460db70"},{"who":"Daniel","v":"m","t":"I don't deny that. My point is that the gains haven't been shared evenly.","au":"5ea578e94a"},{"who":"Grace","v":"f","t":"What worries me is the cultural side. City centers are starting to look the same, with the same chains and the same brands.","au":"3470a4889f"},{"who":"Sofia","v":"f","t":"By the same token, though, you can now find Peruvian, Korean, and Ethiopian food in almost any American city.","au":"ee5f46df8c"},{"who":"Grace","v":"f","t":"Fair point. So maybe the question isn't \"globalization, yes or no,\" but how to manage it more fairly.","au":"58b17731f8"},{"who":"Daniel","v":"m","t":"Exactly. It's a double-edged sword, and we need policies that protect the people who get hurt.","au":"b89dd264fa"}],"q":[{"q":"Why does Daniel feel negatively about globalization?","a":"His hometown lost its main factory.","o":["He can't buy imported phones.","He dislikes foreign food."]},{"q":"What is Grace's main concern?","a":"Cultural homogenization.","o":["The price of phones.","Shipping delays."]},{"q":"What do they finally conclude?","a":"Globalization should be managed more fairly.","o":["Globalization should be stopped completely.","Globalization has no drawbacks."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To weigh the benefits and drawbacks of globalization and rebut other people's arguments politely.","es":"Sopesar los beneficios y desventajas de la globalización y rebatir los argumentos de otros con respeto."},"warm":[{"q":"How many things around you right now were made in another country?","au":"e75d461b21","es":"¿Cuántas cosas a tu alrededor ahora mismo se fabricaron en otro país?","ex":"Almost everything! My phone, my laptop, and even my coffee come from different parts of the world."},{"q":"Do you prefer international brands or local businesses? Why?","au":"d319ce4e14","es":"¿Prefieres las marcas internacionales o los negocios locales? ¿Por qué?","ex":"It depends. I buy electronics from international brands, but I prefer local businesses for food and clothes."}],"reading":{"title":"Globalization: Who Wins, Who Loses?","img":"u:photo-1606185540834-d6e7483ee1a4","text":"Look at the label on your shirt, the parts in your phone, or the coffee in your cup, and you will see globalization at work. Over the past few decades, falling trade barriers and cheaper shipping have connected economies as never before. Proponents argue that this interdependence has been remarkably beneficial. Consumers enjoy cheaper goods and greater choice, companies reach new markets, and emerging economies have attracted investment that helped lift hundreds of millions of people out of poverty. Cultural exchange, they add, has made the world more open: music, food, and ideas now travel across borders in seconds. Critics contend that these gains have come at a price. When factories moved overseas in search of cheaper labor, some manufacturing towns in the United States and Europe lost their economic backbone. Others point to the environmental cost of shipping goods around the planet and to fragile supply chains, which were dramatically exposed during the pandemic. There are cultural concerns, too: as global brands spread, local traditions and small businesses may struggle to compete. However compelling each side may be, the debate is rarely as simple as \"for\" or \"against.\" Most economists accept that trade increases overall wealth; the real disagreement is about how that wealth is distributed. Globalization, in short, is a double-edged sword. The challenge for the coming decades is to keep its benefits while protecting the communities and environments that have paid the highest price.","au":"1c3630abf4","q":[{"s":"According to proponents, globalization has helped reduce poverty in emerging economies.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Critics say that all manufacturing towns have benefited equally.","a":"no"},{"s":"The pandemic revealed weaknesses in global supply chains.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Most economists believe trade reduces overall wealth.","a":"no"},{"s":"The author describes globalization as a double-edged sword.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Has globalization been more positive or negative for your country?","a":"On balance, I'd say it has been positive, although critics contend that some local industries have suffered.","es":"¿La globalización ha sido más positiva o negativa para tu país?","qau":"7231b1518f","aau":"420ff41dc8"},{"q":"Should governments protect local industries from foreign competition?","a":"To some extent, yes. Protection may save jobs, but by the same token, it can raise prices for consumers.","es":"¿Deberían los gobiernos proteger las industrias locales de la competencia extranjera?","qau":"6c562758ac","aau":"05192d9b4a"},{"q":"Is cultural homogenization a real threat?","a":"I think it is a genuine concern; however, global exchange can also enrich local traditions.","es":"¿Es la homogeneización cultural una amenaza real?","qau":"9c94ae1fb9","aau":"4faef0d70d"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe un ensayo corto (120–150 palabras) que presente los beneficios y las desventajas de la globalización y termine con tu conclusión. Usa Proponents argue, Critics contend y By the same token.","kw":["Proponents argue","Critics contend","By the same token"],"n":7,"model":"Globalization has transformed the way we live, work, and consume, yet its effects remain hotly debated. Proponents argue that open trade has lowered prices, created jobs in emerging economies, and helped lift millions of people out of poverty. By the same token, it has allowed cultures to exchange music, food, and ideas more freely than ever before. Critics contend, however, that the benefits have not been shared fairly. Many manufacturing towns have lost their main employers, and global supply chains have proved fragile in times of crisis. There is also a risk that small local businesses cannot compete with multinational brands. In my view, globalization is a double-edged sword. Rather than rejecting it, we should manage it more fairly, protecting both workers and the environment."}}]},{"n":17,"title":"The Impact of Social Media on Mental Health","es":"El impacto de las redes sociales en la salud mental","cover":"u:photo-1758598304329-c250b67437bb","parts":[{"id":"t17p1","topic":17,"part":1,"title":"Class","es":"Debate: redes sociales y bienestar mental","acts":["learn","feedFallacyFlag","fill","dialogue","quizShow","speak"],"tip":"<p>Cuando hablamos de <b>salud y ciencia</b>, un hablante C1 es <b>prudente</b>: no exagera la evidencia.</p>\n<p>🔬 <b>Citar evidencia con cautela</b>: <i>Many studies suggest that…</i> · <i>There is growing evidence that…</i> · <i>Research <b>indicates</b> a link between…</i></p>\n<p>🧩 <b>Verbos suaves</b>: <i>may <b>contribute to</b></i>, <i>can <b>exacerbate</b></i>, <i><b>tend to</b> + verbo</i>, <i>is <b>associated with</b></i> — en lugar de <i>causes</i>.</p>\n<p>🚫 <b>Evitar simplificar</b>: <i><b>It would be simplistic to claim that</b> social media alone causes depression.</i> · <i>A <b>correlation</b> does not necessarily imply <b>causation</b>.</i></p>\n<p>⚖️ <b>Equilibrar</b>: <i>On the one hand…, on the other hand…</i></p>\n<p>💙 Tema sensible: habla con respeto y sin juzgar. Si alguien está pasando un mal momento, lo mejor es hablar con una persona de confianza o un profesional.</p>","tips":["<b>exacerbate</b>: <i>ig-SÁ-ser-beit</i>; la 'x' suena como 'gs'.","<b>well-being</b> se dice <i>uel-BÍ-ing</i>, en dos partes claras.","<b>causation</b> suena <i>ko-SÉI-shon</i>, distinto de <b>correlation</b> (<i>co-re-LÉI-shon</i>)."],"vocab":[{"en":"mental well-being","es":"bienestar mental","img":"u:photo-1522075782449-e45a34f1ddfb","v":"f","au":"aa8fffc4c6"},{"en":"social comparison","es":"comparación social","img":"u:photo-1758598304329-c250b67437bb","v":"m","au":"a74b5ca922"},{"en":"fear of missing out (FOMO)","es":"miedo a perderse algo (FOMO)","img":"u:photo-1758272133641-e26014accac9","v":"f","au":"4b46239148"},{"en":"doomscrolling","es":"consumir sin parar noticias negativas","img":"u:photo-1585577517704-f3d6f8023665","v":"m","au":"b829750dee"},{"en":"screen time","es":"tiempo frente a la pantalla","img":"u:photo-1624625021869-c08eef7f1ccf","v":"f","au":"ffe66c86f9"},{"en":"a sense of belonging","es":"un sentido de pertenencia","img":"u:photo-1529156069898-49953e39b3ac","v":"m","au":"9ca80755ad"},{"en":"cyberbullying","es":"ciberacoso","img":"u:photo-1742575423248-713941c3d554","v":"f","au":"25f6790c37"},{"en":"to curate an image","es":"cuidar (fabricar) una imagen","img":"u:photo-1713812956759-371b4e8fc468","v":"m","au":"adfee79968"},{"en":"correlation, not causation","es":"correlación, no causalidad","img":"#correlation ≠ causation","v":"f","au":"92e58169ca"},{"en":"to exacerbate","es":"agravar / empeorar","img":"u:photo-1758687127236-0da5ff52f4bc","v":"m","au":"6c8593e7b2"},{"en":"There is growing evidence that…","es":"Hay cada vez más evidencia de que…","img":"#There is growing evidence that…","v":"f","au":"eaff2fd7fe"},{"en":"It would be simplistic to claim that…","es":"Sería simplista afirmar que…","img":"#It would be simplistic to claim that…","v":"m","au":"c946f5f44b"}],"sentences":[{"en":"Many studies suggest a link between heavy social media use and anxiety.","es":"Muchos estudios sugieren una relación entre el uso intensivo de redes sociales y la ansiedad.","img":"u:photo-1758598304329-c250b67437bb","v":"f","au":"a99273365b"},{"en":"It would be simplistic to claim that social media alone causes depression.","es":"Sería simplista afirmar que las redes sociales por sí solas causan depresión.","img":"u:photo-1518644730709-0835105d9daa","v":"m","au":"d6b28ff61a"},{"en":"For many isolated people, online communities provide a sense of belonging.","es":"Para muchas personas aisladas, las comunidades en línea brindan un sentido de pertenencia.","img":"u:photo-1706806594968-06036c7c8064","v":"f","au":"94c608406a"},{"en":"Doomscrolling late at night can exacerbate stress and disrupt sleep.","es":"Consumir noticias negativas hasta tarde puede agravar el estrés y alterar el sueño.","img":"u:photo-1585577517704-f3d6f8023665","v":"m","au":"3e58db3b1b"},{"en":"Users tend to compare their everyday lives with other people's highlight reels.","es":"Los usuarios tienden a comparar su vida cotidiana con los mejores momentos de los demás.","img":"u:photo-1713812956759-371b4e8fc468","v":"f","au":"db6cad0b05"}],"fill":[{"s":"There is ___ evidence that excessive screen time affects sleep quality.","a":"growing","o":["grown","growth"],"h":"cada vez más evidencia","full":"There is growing evidence that excessive screen time affects sleep quality.","au":"29f2cbb984"},{"s":"Social media may ___ to feelings of loneliness in some teenagers.","a":"contribute","o":["attribute","distribute"],"h":"contribuir a","full":"Social media may contribute to feelings of loneliness in some teenagers.","au":"2f6b2dbab0"},{"s":"A correlation does not necessarily imply ___.","a":"causation","o":["causing","cause of"],"h":"causalidad","full":"A correlation does not necessarily imply causation.","au":"f49b229882"},{"s":"Constant notifications can ___ existing anxiety.","a":"exacerbate","o":["exaggerate","exasperate"],"h":"agravar (no exagerar)","full":"Constant notifications can exacerbate existing anxiety.","au":"af7045ae31"},{"s":"It would be simplistic ___ that all online interaction is harmful.","a":"to claim","o":["claiming","claim"],"h":"It would be + adjetivo + to + verbo","full":"It would be simplistic to claim that all online interaction is harmful.","au":"7e8a5c8296"},{"s":"Many influencers ___ a carefully edited image of their lives.","a":"curate","o":["cure","care"],"h":"cuidar / fabricar una imagen","full":"Many influencers curate a carefully edited image of their lives.","au":"61a6d9e082"},{"s":"On the ___ hand, online support groups have helped many people.","a":"other","o":["another","others"],"h":"On the other hand","full":"On the other hand, online support groups have helped many people.","au":"0a6f486b0b"}],"dialogue":{"title":"Unplug or log in?","es":"¿Desconectarse o seguir conectado?","img":"u:photo-1624625021869-c08eef7f1ccf","lines":[{"who":"Chloe","v":"f","t":"I deleted Instagram last month, and honestly, I feel calmer. I'd stopped comparing myself to everyone's perfect vacations.","au":"1c491d6a0c"},{"who":"Marcus","v":"m","t":"Good for you, but I'd be careful about generalizing. For me, online groups were a lifeline when I moved to Seattle and didn't know anyone.","au":"da5f40c3fb"},{"who":"Chloe","v":"f","t":"I'm not saying it's all bad. I just think the platforms are designed to keep us hooked.","au":"e07e03257a"},{"who":"Dr. Patel","v":"m","t":"There's some truth in that. Many studies suggest a link between heavy use and anxiety, especially among teenagers.","au":"6668be50b8"},{"who":"Marcus","v":"m","t":"A link, sure. But isn't it possible that anxious people simply spend more time online?","au":"1e4909e9d8"},{"who":"Dr. Patel","v":"m","t":"That's a fair question. Correlation isn't causation, and the research is still evolving.","au":"571ecaabf6"},{"who":"Chloe","v":"f","t":"So what would you recommend, Doctor?","au":"b4be57dafa"},{"who":"Dr. Patel","v":"m","t":"Rather than quitting altogether, be intentional: set limits, mute what makes you feel worse, and check in with real people.","au":"4f3cc3264a"}],"q":[{"q":"Why did Chloe delete Instagram?","a":"She kept comparing herself to others.","o":["Her phone was broken.","She had too many followers."]},{"q":"How did social media help Marcus?","a":"Online groups supported him when he moved.","o":["It helped him get a promotion.","It made him famous."]},{"q":"What does Dr. Patel recommend?","a":"Using social media intentionally and setting limits.","o":["Quitting all technology forever.","Spending more time online."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To discuss how social media affects mental health, citing evidence carefully and avoiding simplistic claims.","es":"Hablar de cómo las redes sociales afectan la salud mental, citando la evidencia con cautela y evitando afirmaciones simplistas."},"warm":[{"q":"How much time do you think you spend on social media each day?","au":"ca245d6d6a","es":"¿Cuánto tiempo crees que pasas en redes sociales cada día?","ex":"Probably around two hours, although I'd rather not check my screen time report!"},{"q":"How do you usually feel after scrolling for a long time?","au":"dd2d2c2421","es":"¿Cómo te sueles sentir después de pasar mucho tiempo deslizando la pantalla?","ex":"To be honest, I often feel a bit tired and distracted, as if I'd wasted time."}],"reading":{"title":"Scrolling Toward Unhappiness?","img":"u:photo-1585577517704-f3d6f8023665","text":"Most of us check our phones dozens of times a day, often without noticing. As social media has become part of everyday life, researchers, parents, and users themselves have begun to ask a difficult question: is it harming our mental health? There is growing evidence that heavy use is associated with anxiety, poor sleep, and low self-esteem, particularly among teenagers. Many studies suggest that constant social comparison plays a role. When users scroll through other people's highlight reels, from filtered photos to dream vacations, their own ordinary lives can seem disappointing. Late-night doomscrolling and the fear of missing out may exacerbate the problem. However, it would be simplistic to claim that social media alone causes these difficulties. A correlation is not the same as causation: people who are already struggling may simply spend more time online. Moreover, social platforms can offer genuine benefits. For people who feel isolated because of illness, disability, or distance, online communities can provide support, information, and a sense of belonging. Perhaps the most useful question is not whether social media is good or bad, but how we use it. Experts commonly recommend setting time limits, turning off non-essential notifications, and paying attention to how certain accounts make us feel. Technology companies, too, face growing pressure to design products that protect users' well-being rather than simply capture their attention. And if you or someone you know is having a hard time, talking to a trusted person or a professional is always a good first step.","au":"9d46d43c7f","q":[{"s":"Research has proven that social media is the only cause of anxiety in teenagers.","a":"no"},{"s":"Social comparison is mentioned as a possible factor.","a":"yes"},{"s":"People who are already struggling may spend more time online.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The article says online communities offer no real benefits.","a":"no"},{"s":"Experts recommend turning off non-essential notifications.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Does social media do more harm than good?","a":"It would be simplistic to say it's all harmful. Many studies suggest risks, but it can also provide a sense of belonging.","es":"¿Las redes sociales hacen más daño que bien?","qau":"2e043b4ef1","aau":"99b64f01ed"},{"q":"Should there be age limits for social media?","a":"I think there is a strong case for age limits, although they would be difficult to enforce.","es":"¿Debería haber límites de edad para las redes sociales?","qau":"318c711173","aau":"30ec820a73"},{"q":"How can people use social media in a healthier way?","a":"They could set time limits, mute accounts that make them feel worse, and spend more time with people face-to-face.","es":"¿Cómo pueden las personas usar las redes sociales de una forma más sana?","qau":"bb9d6d91ae","aau":"648f9a476e"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe un ensayo corto (120–150 palabras): ¿las redes sociales hacen más daño que bien a la salud mental? Presenta ambos lados con lenguaje prudente (Many studies suggest…, It would be simplistic…, On the other hand…).","kw":["Many studies suggest","It would be simplistic","On the other hand"],"n":7,"model":"Social media has become an inseparable part of modern life, and its impact on mental health is a growing concern. Many studies suggest that heavy use is linked to anxiety, poor sleep, and low self-esteem, especially among young people. Constant social comparison and the fear of missing out may exacerbate these problems. On the other hand, it would be simplistic to claim that social media is purely harmful. For people who feel isolated, online communities can offer support and a sense of belonging. Moreover, a correlation does not necessarily imply causation. In my opinion, the key lies in how we use these platforms. Setting time limits, muting negative content, and prioritizing real-life relationships can help us enjoy the benefits while reducing the risks."}}]},{"n":18,"title":"Justice and Fairness (Are we in a fair society?)","es":"Justicia y equidad: ¿vivimos en una sociedad justa?","cover":"u:photo-1662516201865-8633915e668a","parts":[{"id":"t18p1","topic":18,"part":1,"title":"Class","es":"Debate: ¿qué hace justa a una sociedad?","acts":["learn","justiceNuanceDial","fill","dialogue","typeSentence","speak"],"tip":"<p>En temas delicados como la justicia, el hablante C1 <b>matiza</b> (<i>hedging</i>): evita los absolutos y respeta otras posturas.</p>\n<p>🎚️ <b>Cambia los absolutos</b>: <i>all → many / most</i> · <i>always → often / tend to</i> · <i>never → rarely / seldom</i> · <i>is → can be / may be</i></p>\n<p>🧭 <b>Matizadores</b>: <b>To a certain extent</b> (hasta cierto punto) · <b>To some degree</b> · <b>Arguably</b> (podría decirse que) · <b>In many cases</b> · <b>Broadly speaking</b></p>\n<p>🔍 <b>Definir antes de opinar</b>: <i><b>It depends on how we define</b> fairness: equal treatment or equal results?</i></p>\n<p>🙂 <b>Discrepar con respeto</b>: <i>That is not entirely accurate.</i> · <i>I'm not entirely convinced.</i> · <i>I see it slightly differently.</i></p>\n<p>⚠️ Ojo: se dice <b>to a certain ext<u>ent</u></b> (no <i>extend</i>) y <b>tend to</b> + verbo (<i>tend to receive</i>).</p>","tips":["<b>meritocracy</b> lleva el acento en <i>me-ri-TÓ-cra-si</i>.","<b>due process</b> suena <i>du PRÁ-ses</i> en inglés americano.","<b>entirely</b>: <i>en-TÁIER-li</i>; no digas <i>en-ti-ré-li</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"equality of opportunity","es":"igualdad de oportunidades","img":"u:photo-1630037278864-12b795cd512a","v":"f","au":"ce91133870"},{"en":"equality of outcome","es":"igualdad de resultados","img":"#equality of outcome =","v":"m","au":"401b9f4271"},{"en":"the rule of law","es":"el Estado de derecho","img":"u:photo-1662516201865-8633915e668a","v":"f","au":"94d1f2e2aa"},{"en":"meritocracy","es":"meritocracia","img":"u:photo-1495674817798-4455f189de69","v":"m","au":"e1c98b0e09"},{"en":"access to justice","es":"acceso a la justicia","img":"u:photo-1562564055-71e051d33c19","v":"f","au":"fb7fe1d96f"},{"en":"systemic inequality","es":"desigualdad estructural","img":"u:photo-1627927518258-b67557570840","v":"m","au":"a94c58e08b"},{"en":"a level playing field","es":"igualdad de condiciones","img":"u:photo-1546717003-caee5f93a9db","v":"f","au":"049a26f7fb"},{"en":"to redistribute wealth","es":"redistribuir la riqueza","img":"u:photo-1534951009808-766178b47a4f","v":"m","au":"22db37f9ce"},{"en":"due process","es":"el debido proceso","img":"u:photo-1767972463877-b64ba4283cd0","v":"f","au":"1de6cee2e2"},{"en":"It depends on how we define…","es":"Depende de cómo definamos…","img":"#It depends on how we define…","v":"m","au":"e798c92ac5"},{"en":"To a certain extent, …","es":"Hasta cierto punto, …","img":"#To a certain extent, …","v":"f","au":"b6ea82654f"},{"en":"That is not entirely accurate.","es":"Eso no es del todo exacto.","img":"#That is not entirely accurate.","v":"m","au":"a5390750b8"}],"sentences":[{"en":"To a certain extent, our society rewards talent and hard work.","es":"Hasta cierto punto, nuestra sociedad recompensa el talento y el trabajo duro.","img":"u:photo-1495674817798-4455f189de69","v":"f","au":"07a80ab650"},{"en":"Critics argue that equality of opportunity is impossible without a level playing field.","es":"Los críticos sostienen que la igualdad de oportunidades es imposible sin igualdad de condiciones.","img":"u:photo-1630037278864-12b795cd512a","v":"m","au":"f1a930dadd"},{"en":"The rule of law means that no one is above the law.","es":"El Estado de derecho significa que nadie está por encima de la ley.","img":"u:photo-1662516201865-8633915e668a","v":"f","au":"d85c48256d"},{"en":"Access to justice often depends on whether you can afford a good lawyer.","es":"El acceso a la justicia a menudo depende de si puedes pagar un buen abogado.","img":"u:photo-1562564055-71e051d33c19","v":"m","au":"df94926f28"},{"en":"It depends on how we define fairness: equal treatment or equal results.","es":"Depende de cómo definamos la equidad: trato igual o resultados iguales.","img":"u:photo-1612012060851-20f943c02d3d","v":"f","au":"dfed3a598b"}],"fill":[{"s":"To a certain ___, the system works for most people.","a":"extent","o":["extend","degree of"],"h":"To a certain extent","full":"To a certain extent, the system works for most people.","au":"7a0312fa51"},{"s":"In a true meritocracy, success would depend ___ effort and talent.","a":"on","o":["of","from"],"h":"depend on","full":"In a true meritocracy, success would depend on effort and talent.","au":"6aad147a31"},{"s":"That is not ___ accurate; some groups face additional barriers.","a":"entirely","o":["entire","total"],"h":"discrepar con respeto","full":"That is not entirely accurate; some groups face additional barriers.","au":"0a2c61387d"},{"s":"Everyone has the right to due ___.","a":"process","o":["progress","procedure"],"h":"el debido proceso","full":"Everyone has the right to due process.","au":"c97ea77592"},{"s":"A fair society should provide a level playing ___.","a":"field","o":["ground","floor"],"h":"a level playing field","full":"A fair society should provide a level playing field.","au":"1a59456e06"},{"s":"Wealth inequality has grown in some countries, ___ progress in reducing extreme poverty.","a":"despite","o":["although","however"],"h":"despite + sustantivo","full":"Wealth inequality has grown in some countries, despite progress in reducing extreme poverty.","au":"6481547cbd"},{"s":"___ speaking, fairness means treating similar cases alike.","a":"Broadly","o":["Broad","Large"],"h":"generalizar con cautela","full":"Broadly speaking, fairness means treating similar cases alike.","au":"a975168dec"}],"dialogue":{"title":"Is our society fair?","es":"¿Es justa nuestra sociedad?","img":"u:photo-1662516201865-8633915e668a","lines":[{"who":"Nina","v":"f","t":"I'd say we live in a fairly just society. Anyone who works hard can get ahead.","au":"ae376af3e8"},{"who":"Jordan","v":"m","t":"To a certain extent, yes. But it depends on where you start. A kid from a wealthy suburb has advantages that a kid in a struggling neighborhood doesn't.","au":"8999fb367a"},{"who":"Nina","v":"f","t":"Sure, but there are scholarships and public schools. The opportunities are there.","au":"735d74f7c9"},{"who":"Luis","v":"m","t":"That's not entirely accurate. In many places, schools are partly funded by local property taxes, so poorer areas often get less.","au":"bcf2f15f00"},{"who":"Nina","v":"f","t":"I hadn't thought about that. Still, I don't believe the answer is to make everyone's outcomes identical.","au":"112c50b2dd"},{"who":"Jordan","v":"m","t":"Neither do I. I'm arguing for equality of opportunity, not equality of outcome.","au":"f9c1aa4e0b"},{"who":"Luis","v":"m","t":"And for equal treatment under the law. Justice shouldn't depend on whether you can afford a good lawyer.","au":"df175b363a"},{"who":"Nina","v":"f","t":"On that, I think we all agree. A fair society starts with a level playing field.","au":"c50d65c587"}],"q":[{"q":"What is Nina's initial view?","a":"Society is fairly just and hard work pays off.","o":["Society is completely unfair.","Hard work is useless."]},{"q":"What point does Luis make about schools?","a":"Schools in poorer areas often receive less funding.","o":["All schools receive the same money.","Private schools are free."]},{"q":"What do they all agree on?","a":"A fair society needs a level playing field.","o":["Everyone should earn exactly the same.","Laws are unnecessary."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To discuss fairness and justice in society with nuance, hedging claims and respecting different views.","es":"Hablar de justicia y equidad en la sociedad con matices, suavizando afirmaciones y respetando otras posturas."},"warm":[{"q":"Do you think hard work is always rewarded? Why or why not?","au":"3ff73a51c9","es":"¿Crees que el trabajo duro siempre se recompensa? ¿Por qué sí o por qué no?","ex":"Not always. Hard work matters, but connections, luck, and where you start in life also play a big role."},{"q":"What does the word 'fair' mean to you?","au":"75c1e64715","es":"¿Qué significa para ti la palabra 'justo'?","ex":"For me, 'fair' means that everyone follows the same rules and has a real chance to succeed."}],"reading":{"title":"What Makes a Society Fair?","img":"u:photo-1662516201865-8633915e668a","text":"Almost everyone agrees that a society should be fair. The difficulty begins when we try to define what fairness actually means. For some, fairness is about equality of opportunity. In this view, a just society guarantees the same basic rights and chances to everyone, and then rewards people according to their effort and talent. This ideal of meritocracy is deeply rooted in American culture, where the belief that anyone can succeed through hard work remains powerful. Others argue that this picture is incomplete. Children do not start life on a level playing field: family income, the quality of local schools, and access to healthcare can shape a person's prospects long before they apply for their first job. From this perspective, a fair society must actively reduce these gaps, for example through public education or targeted support programs. A third group warns against going too far. If governments try to equalize outcomes, they say, people may lose the incentive to work hard and innovate, and individual freedom could be restricted. For them, fairness means equal treatment under the law, not identical results. Whatever their differences, most people share certain principles: the rule of law, due process, and equal access to justice. In practice, however, the quality of legal representation can still depend on what a person can afford. So, are we living in a fair society? To a certain extent, the answer depends on how we define fairness, and perhaps on where we happen to stand on the playing field.","au":"d5f6e31346","q":[{"s":"The text says everyone defines fairness in exactly the same way.","a":"no"},{"s":"Meritocracy rewards people according to effort and talent.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Some argue that family income can affect a child's prospects.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The third group supports making everyone's income identical.","a":"no"},{"s":"The author suggests the answer depends partly on how we define fairness.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Do we live in a fair society?","a":"To a certain extent, yes, but it depends on how we define fairness. Not everyone starts on a level playing field.","es":"¿Vivimos en una sociedad justa?","qau":"add3431a9c","aau":"c4a81d4a9b"},{"q":"Is equality of opportunity more important than equality of outcome?","a":"In my view, equality of opportunity matters more, although some support is needed for those who start with disadvantages.","es":"¿Es más importante la igualdad de oportunidades que la igualdad de resultados?","qau":"8021f08fc6","aau":"4ecc0de790"},{"q":"Is a true meritocracy possible?","a":"It's an attractive ideal, but it is not entirely realistic while access to education remains unequal.","es":"¿Es posible una verdadera meritocracia?","qau":"a6f6e1642e","aau":"9900e65ebb"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe un ensayo corto (120–150 palabras): ¿vivimos en una sociedad justa? Matiza tus afirmaciones (To a certain extent…, In many cases…, It depends on…) y presenta al menos dos posturas con respeto.","kw":["To a certain extent","It depends on","level playing field"],"n":7,"model":"Whether we live in a fair society is a complex question, and the answer largely depends on how we define fairness. To a certain extent, modern democracies are fairer than ever: laws protect basic rights, and education is available to most people. In many cases, talent and effort are rewarded. However, it would be inaccurate to claim that everyone starts on a level playing field. Family income, neighborhood, and access to healthcare can shape a person's opportunities from an early age. Some people believe the government should actively reduce these gaps, while others worry that too much intervention could limit freedom and discourage effort. In my view, a fair society should guarantee equality of opportunity and equal treatment under the law, rather than identical outcomes for everyone."}}]},{"n":19,"title":"Traditional Education vs. Online Learning","es":"Educación tradicional vs. aprendizaje en línea","cover":"u:photo-1758270705290-62b6294dd044","parts":[{"id":"t19p1","topic":19,"part":1,"title":"Class","es":"Debate: ¿aula o pantalla?","acts":["learn","eduEssayRedPen","dialogue","unscramble","memory","speak"],"tip":"<p>Para <b>comparar y contrastar</b> dos modelos como un hablante C1:</p>\n<p>↔️ <b>Whereas / While</b> + cláusula: <i><b>Whereas</b> classrooms offer structure, online courses offer flexibility.</i></p>\n<p>🔄 <b>Conversely,</b> / <b>In contrast,</b> / <b>On the other hand,</b> + oración completa (al inicio, con coma).</p>\n<p>🚫 <b>Unlike</b> + sustantivo: <i><b>Unlike</b> traditional classes, online courses…</i> (¡nunca <i>unlike to</i>!).</p>\n<p>📏 <b>Comparativos avanzados</b>: <i>far more flexible than</i> · <i>not nearly as expensive as</i> · <i><b>The more</b> you participate, <b>the more</b> you learn.</i></p>\n<p>✍️ En un texto argumentativo, cada oración debe <b>apoyar la idea principal</b> del párrafo (coherencia) y los conectores deben tener <b>lógica</b>: <i>therefore</i> = consecuencia, <i>however</i> = contraste.</p>","tips":["<b>asynchronous</b>: <i>ei-SÍN-cro-nos</i>.","<b>whereas</b> suena <i>uer-ÁS</i>, con el acento al final.","<b>tuition</b> se dice <i>tu-Í-shon</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"face-to-face instruction","es":"enseñanza presencial","img":"u:photo-1758685848208-e108b6af94cc","v":"f","au":"0aca92c31a"},{"en":"asynchronous courses","es":"cursos asincrónicos (a tu ritmo)","img":"u:photo-1559163304-2bd8f8600164","v":"m","au":"54b31fddc7"},{"en":"self-discipline","es":"autodisciplina","img":"u:photo-1544717302-de2939b7ef71","v":"f","au":"802b2998e3"},{"en":"the digital divide","es":"la brecha digital","img":"u:photo-1763809677809-d8ff6f7ad1d0","v":"m","au":"e3c04388f0"},{"en":"peer interaction","es":"interacción entre compañeros","img":"u:photo-1758270704763-22072a90d3b6","v":"f","au":"3e47e17ebb"},{"en":"blended learning","es":"aprendizaje mixto (semipresencial)","img":"u:photo-1758270705290-62b6294dd044","v":"m","au":"12efedef7b"},{"en":"to foster critical thinking","es":"fomentar el pensamiento crítico","img":"u:photo-1758270704787-615782711641","v":"f","au":"518d87fb14"},{"en":"tuition fees","es":"costos de matrícula","img":"u:photo-1741637335289-c99652d3155f","v":"m","au":"b118061bfa"},{"en":"to drop out","es":"abandonar los estudios","img":"u:photo-1757193714692-44cdf07a5377","v":"f","au":"cf2b85a99c"},{"en":"flexibility","es":"flexibilidad","img":"u:photo-1758522484755-93e3286fdfc4","v":"m","au":"0553c170d6"},{"en":"Whereas…, …","es":"Mientras que…, …","img":"#Whereas…, …","v":"f","au":"ca6c35b5b0"},{"en":"Conversely, …","es":"Por el contrario, …","img":"#Conversely, …","v":"m","au":"29d0554808"}],"sentences":[{"en":"Whereas traditional classes offer structure, online courses offer flexibility.","es":"Mientras que las clases tradicionales ofrecen estructura, los cursos en línea ofrecen flexibilidad.","img":"u:photo-1758685848208-e108b6af94cc","v":"f","au":"97f26af68d"},{"en":"Online learning requires a great deal of self-discipline.","es":"Aprender en línea requiere mucha autodisciplina.","img":"u:photo-1544717302-de2939b7ef71","v":"m","au":"fdc062f279"},{"en":"The digital divide means that not every student has reliable internet access.","es":"La brecha digital implica que no todos los estudiantes tienen acceso confiable a internet.","img":"u:photo-1763809677809-d8ff6f7ad1d0","v":"f","au":"1e6c780ab8"},{"en":"Many universities now favor blended learning.","es":"Muchas universidades ahora prefieren el aprendizaje mixto.","img":"u:photo-1758270705290-62b6294dd044","v":"m","au":"c1112ecaca"},{"en":"Conversely, face-to-face instruction can foster stronger peer interaction.","es":"Por el contrario, la enseñanza presencial puede fomentar una interacción más fuerte entre compañeros.","img":"u:photo-1758270704787-615782711641","v":"f","au":"1413bd46e1"},{"en":"The more flexible a course is, the easier it is to combine with a full-time job.","es":"Cuanto más flexible es un curso, más fácil es combinarlo con un trabajo de tiempo completo.","img":"u:photo-1758522484755-93e3286fdfc4","v":"m","au":"b0caa95153"}],"fill":[{"s":"___ online courses are flexible, traditional classes provide a fixed routine.","a":"Whereas","o":["Despite","Unlike"],"h":"contraste entre dos cláusulas","full":"Whereas online courses are flexible, traditional classes provide a fixed routine.","au":"01acc78f0a"},{"s":"Students are more likely to ___ out if they feel isolated.","a":"drop","o":["fall","give"],"h":"phrasal verb: abandonar los estudios","full":"Students are more likely to drop out if they feel isolated.","au":"5a4fc1cc57"},{"s":"Universities should do more to bridge the digital ___.","a":"divide","o":["division","distance"],"h":"la brecha digital","full":"Universities should do more to bridge the digital divide.","au":"e8ad38bf3b"},{"s":"Seminars are designed to ___ critical thinking.","a":"foster","o":["force","forge"],"h":"fomentar","full":"Seminars are designed to foster critical thinking.","au":"befae01cee"},{"s":"___ in-person classes, online courses can be taken from anywhere.","a":"Unlike","o":["Whereas","Unlike to"],"h":"unlike + sustantivo","full":"Unlike in-person classes, online courses can be taken from anywhere.","au":"12b67a8de6"},{"s":"The more you participate, the ___ you learn.","a":"more","o":["most","much"],"h":"the more…, the more…","full":"The more you participate, the more you learn.","au":"02cf7781cd"},{"s":"Online degrees are often not nearly ___ expensive as traditional ones.","a":"as","o":["so much","than"],"h":"not nearly as… as","full":"Online degrees are often not nearly as expensive as traditional ones.","au":"60b65eba87"}],"dialogue":{"title":"Campus or laptop?","es":"¿Campus o portátil?","img":"u:photo-1741637335289-c99652d3155f","lines":[{"who":"Emma","v":"f","t":"I completed my master's degree entirely online while working full-time. I couldn't have done it any other way.","au":"8d0a2bc2e6"},{"who":"Ryan","v":"m","t":"That's impressive, but I think you missed something essential: the debates in class, the coffee after the lecture, the networking.","au":"c64defe480"},{"who":"Emma","v":"f","t":"I had video seminars and group projects. Conversely, in my undergraduate classes, three hundred students just sat and took notes.","au":"118ab9d72b"},{"who":"Ryan","v":"m","t":"Fair enough, huge lectures aren't ideal. Still, online learning demands a level of self-discipline that many students simply don't have.","au":"9bec38fbce"},{"who":"Ms. Torres","v":"f","t":"As a teacher, I've seen both sides. Dropout rates do tend to be higher in fully online courses.","au":"5f9176ba86"},{"who":"Emma","v":"f","t":"But isn't that partly because online students are often older and juggling jobs and families?","au":"7d3553c9fd"},{"who":"Ms. Torres","v":"f","t":"That's a valid point. Personally, I think blended learning offers the best of both worlds.","au":"b450906554"},{"who":"Ryan","v":"m","t":"I could live with that, as long as students still meet face-to-face regularly.","au":"7fbb2509e2"}],"q":[{"q":"How did Emma complete her master's degree?","a":"Online, while working full-time.","o":["On campus","full-time.","She didn't finish it."]},{"q":"What does Ryan think online students miss?","a":"Class debates and networking.","o":["Cheaper tuition.","Free laptops."]},{"q":"What does Ms. Torres recommend?","a":"Blended learning.","o":["Only online classes.","Only large lectures."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To compare and contrast traditional and online education, building coherent arguments with accurate linkers.","es":"Comparar y contrastar la educación tradicional y en línea, construyendo argumentos coherentes con conectores precisos."},"warm":[{"q":"Have you ever taken an online course? How was your experience?","au":"1485e05f33","es":"¿Alguna vez has tomado un curso en línea? ¿Cómo fue tu experiencia?","ex":"Yes, I took an online marketing course. It was flexible, but I needed a lot of self-discipline to finish it."},{"q":"What do you remember most about your school classroom?","au":"e72fc0c8f9","es":"¿Qué es lo que más recuerdas del salón de clases de tu colegio?","ex":"I remember the noise, my friends, and one teacher who made history fascinating."}],"reading":{"title":"The Classroom or the Screen?","img":"u:photo-1559163304-2bd8f8600164","text":"Not long ago, earning a degree meant moving to a college town, attending lectures, and sitting exams in a crowded hall. Today, a nurse in Denver can study for a master's degree at midnight, after her shift, from her kitchen table. Online learning has expanded dramatically, and so has the debate about its value. Supporters highlight flexibility and access. Asynchronous courses allow students to learn at their own pace, which is especially valuable for working adults and parents. Online programs can also be more affordable, since students save on commuting, housing, and sometimes tuition fees. For people who live far from a university, the internet may be the only realistic route to higher education. Critics, conversely, emphasize what is lost. Face-to-face instruction offers immediate feedback, spontaneous discussion, and the kind of peer interaction that fosters critical thinking and builds professional networks. Online learning also demands considerable self-discipline, and dropout rates in some fully online courses tend to be higher. Moreover, the digital divide means that students without reliable internet or a quiet place to study may be left further behind. Whereas early debates presented the two models as rivals, many educators now favor blended learning, which combines the structure and human connection of the classroom with the flexibility of digital tools. The question, then, may not be which model is better, but which combination best serves each learner. After all, a good education depends less on the medium than on the quality of the teaching and the motivation of the student.","au":"14678f3530","q":[{"s":"Asynchronous courses let students learn at their own pace.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Online programs are always more expensive than traditional ones.","a":"no"},{"s":"Critics say face-to-face classes help build professional networks.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The digital divide affects all students equally.","a":"no"},{"s":"Many educators now favor a combination of both models.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Is online learning as effective as traditional education?","a":"It depends on the student. Whereas some learners thrive online, others need the structure of a classroom.","es":"¿Es el aprendizaje en línea tan eficaz como la educación tradicional?","qau":"92bd7ce5c0","aau":"5466c34342"},{"q":"What are the main advantages of studying online?","a":"The main advantages are flexibility, lower costs, and access for people who live far from a university.","es":"¿Cuáles son las principales ventajas de estudiar en línea?","qau":"eb5988cd81","aau":"133a1bdde0"},{"q":"Will universities still exist in thirty years?","a":"I believe they will, but they'll probably rely far more on blended learning than they do today.","es":"¿Seguirán existiendo las universidades dentro de treinta años?","qau":"84d2968cfe","aau":"a9d20161b0"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe un ensayo corto (120–150 palabras) comparando la educación tradicional y la educación en línea. Usa whereas, conversely y una estructura comparativa (far more…, not nearly as… as).","kw":["whereas","conversely","far more"],"n":7,"model":"The debate between traditional education and online learning has intensified in recent years. Whereas traditional classrooms offer structure, immediate feedback, and valuable peer interaction, online courses provide the flexibility that many adults need. For working parents, studying at night from home is far more realistic than attending lectures every morning. Online programs can also be more affordable, since students save on transportation and housing. Conversely, studying alone requires a great deal of self-discipline, and some students feel isolated and eventually drop out. In addition, the digital divide means that not everyone has reliable internet access. In my opinion, neither model is perfect. Blended learning, which combines face-to-face sessions with online activities, offers the best of both worlds. Ultimately, the quality of the teaching matters more than the format."}}]},{"n":20,"title":"The Future of Democracy","es":"El futuro de la democracia","cover":"u:photo-1782998307726-f93ec14eda24","parts":[{"id":"t20p1","topic":20,"part":1,"title":"Class","es":"Debate: ¿cómo será la democracia del futuro?","acts":["learn","demoTownHall","fill","listenChoose","dialogue","speak"],"tip":"<p>En un <b>town hall</b> (foro ciudadano) o mesa redonda, el lenguaje del <b>moderador</b> y de la <b>concesión</b> es clave:</p>\n<p>🤝 <b>Conceder</b> antes de discrepar: <b>Granted,</b> technology helps… <b>but</b> … · <b>I take your point, but</b> … · <b>Fair enough, however</b> …</p>\n<p>🎙️ <b>Moderar</b>: <i>Could you <b>elaborate on</b> that?</i> (¿podría ampliar?) · <i>Let's <b>get back to</b> the question.</i> · <i>Please let her <b>finish</b>.</i> · <i>We <b>haven't heard from</b> you yet.</i> · <i>Let's focus on <b>the argument, not the person</b>.</i> · <i>Do you have a <b>source</b> for that?</i></p>\n<p>🔮 <b>Hipótesis</b> sobre el futuro: <i><b>If</b> citizens <b>were</b> better informed, polarization <b>might</b> decrease.</i></p>\n<p>⚖️ Tema político: en esta clase <b>no hay bando correcto</b>. Practica presentar ideas de forma <b>neutral</b>, con datos generales y respeto.</p>","tips":["<b>accountable</b>: <i>a-KÁUN-ta-bol</i>.","<b>citizenry</b> suena <i>SÍ-ti-sen-ri</i>.","<b>polarization</b>: <i>po-la-ri-SÉI-shon</i>; la 'z' suena como una 's' zumbada."],"vocab":[{"en":"voter turnout","es":"participación electoral","img":"u:photo-1782998307726-f93ec14eda24","v":"f","au":"e62c8d4598"},{"en":"civic engagement","es":"participación cívica","img":"u:photo-1560220604-1985ebfe28b1","v":"m","au":"55009c70be"},{"en":"political polarization","es":"polarización política","img":"u:photo-1736795467589-95b256b18066","v":"f","au":"7e223f985e"},{"en":"misinformation","es":"desinformación","img":"u:photo-1592890288564-76628a30a657","v":"m","au":"f57bef4eea"},{"en":"checks and balances","es":"pesos y contrapesos","img":"u:photo-1520525003249-2b9cdda513bc","v":"f","au":"4817d43bf1"},{"en":"freedom of the press","es":"libertad de prensa","img":"u:photo-1565140834639-60452b8b0ae5","v":"m","au":"7204e4eadb"},{"en":"to hold leaders accountable","es":"exigir cuentas a los líderes","img":"u:photo-1565946606128-949cfcbebd3e","v":"f","au":"b3d31ed619"},{"en":"a well-informed citizenry","es":"una ciudadanía bien informada","img":"u:photo-1495020689067-958852a7765e","v":"m","au":"bc21870199"},{"en":"a citizens' assembly","es":"una asamblea ciudadana","img":"u:photo-1626287935075-3275d2d9025e","v":"f","au":"3462cf18f8"},{"en":"to erode trust","es":"erosionar la confianza","img":"u:photo-1663045579290-4785a5c424fe","v":"m","au":"55f7a0d0c7"},{"en":"Granted, …","es":"Es cierto que… / Concedo que…","img":"#Granted, …","v":"f","au":"219f9d6f80"},{"en":"I take your point, but…","es":"Entiendo tu punto, pero…","img":"#I take your point, but…","v":"m","au":"2eac249c82"}],"sentences":[{"en":"Low voter turnout may weaken the legitimacy of an election.","es":"Una baja participación electoral puede debilitar la legitimidad de una elección.","img":"u:photo-1782998307726-f93ec14eda24","v":"f","au":"5f71b607af"},{"en":"Misinformation often spreads faster than corrections on social media.","es":"La desinformación suele difundirse más rápido que las correcciones en redes sociales.","img":"u:photo-1592890288564-76628a30a657","v":"m","au":"36dcffaf53"},{"en":"A free press helps citizens hold leaders accountable.","es":"Una prensa libre ayuda a los ciudadanos a exigir cuentas a sus líderes.","img":"u:photo-1565140834639-60452b8b0ae5","v":"f","au":"0be88f8c4a"},{"en":"Checks and balances prevent any single branch from becoming too powerful.","es":"Los pesos y contrapesos impiden que una sola rama del poder se vuelva demasiado poderosa.","img":"u:photo-1520525003249-2b9cdda513bc","v":"m","au":"cb7e49d1fb"},{"en":"Granted, technology could make it easier for citizens to participate.","es":"Es cierto que la tecnología podría facilitar la participación ciudadana.","img":"u:photo-1560220604-1985ebfe28b1","v":"f","au":"555af468e0"},{"en":"Political polarization can erode trust in public institutions.","es":"La polarización política puede erosionar la confianza en las instituciones públicas.","img":"u:photo-1736795467589-95b256b18066","v":"m","au":"d26e32a011"}],"fill":[{"s":"A free press is essential to hold leaders ___.","a":"accountable","o":["accounted","countable"],"h":"hold someone accountable","full":"A free press is essential to hold leaders accountable.","au":"1a763f3235"},{"s":"___, online voting could increase turnout among young people.","a":"Granted","o":["Grant","Granting"],"h":"conceder un punto","full":"Granted, online voting could increase turnout among young people.","au":"61bcca0b8f"},{"s":"I take your ___, but security remains a serious concern.","a":"point","o":["idea","reason"],"h":"I take your point, but…","full":"I take your point, but security remains a serious concern.","au":"aa76641949"},{"s":"Misinformation can ___ public trust in elections.","a":"erode","o":["erupt","eject"],"h":"erosionar","full":"Misinformation can erode public trust in elections.","au":"64cf3f341e"},{"s":"Many democracies have seen a decline in civic ___.","a":"engagement","o":["engage","engaging"],"h":"participación cívica","full":"Many democracies have seen a decline in civic engagement.","au":"ac847f372a"},{"s":"Could you ___ on that point, please?","a":"elaborate","o":["elaborated","explain"],"h":"pedir que alguien amplíe su idea","full":"Could you elaborate on that point, please?","au":"d44251f226"},{"s":"If citizens ___ better informed, polarization might decrease.","a":"were","o":["are","will be"],"h":"hipótesis: If + pasado, … might","full":"If citizens were better informed, polarization might decrease.","au":"c6ffabfad1"}],"dialogue":{"title":"Town hall: Is democracy in trouble?","es":"Foro ciudadano: ¿está en problemas la democracia?","img":"u:photo-1565946606128-949cfcbebd3e","lines":[{"who":"Kim","v":"f","t":"Welcome, everyone. Tonight's question is whether democracy is getting stronger or weaker. Andre, would you like to start?","au":"e8ec5c0cc5"},{"who":"Andre","v":"m","t":"Thank you. I'm genuinely worried. Polarization seems to be rising, and misinformation spreads faster than ever.","au":"cc9a174469"},{"who":"Lucia","v":"f","t":"I take your point, but I'd argue democracy is more resilient than we think. Look at how many young people are organizing online.","au":"f0852283f5"},{"who":"Andre","v":"m","t":"Granted, there's a lot of energy online. But clicking \"like\" isn't the same as voting or showing up to a city council meeting.","au":"6b9e9be6e5"},{"who":"Kim","v":"f","t":"Lucia, how would you respond to that?","au":"7aba065633"},{"who":"Lucia","v":"f","t":"Participation is changing shape, not disappearing. Some cities now let residents vote on how to spend part of the local budget.","au":"6a3cf08f14"},{"who":"Andre","v":"m","t":"That's encouraging. If more people felt their vote made a difference, trust might start to recover.","au":"511c8d7cec"},{"who":"Kim","v":"f","t":"So, to sum up: concern about polarization, but also new forms of civic engagement. Thank you both.","au":"f6105ecd4a"}],"q":[{"q":"What worries Andre?","a":"Rising polarization and misinformation.","o":["High taxes.","Too many elections."]},{"q":"What example does Lucia give?","a":"Residents voting on part of the local budget.","o":["Banning social media.","Canceling elections."]},{"q":"What is the moderator's role in this debate?","a":"To give turns and summarize the views.","o":["To win the argument.","To vote for one side."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To discuss the challenges and future of democracy in a neutral way, conceding points and moderating a discussion.","es":"Hablar de los retos y el futuro de la democracia de forma neutral, concediendo puntos y moderando una discusión."},"warm":[{"q":"Why do you think some people don't vote?","au":"0e7760c2aa","es":"¿Por qué crees que algunas personas no votan?","ex":"I think some people feel that their vote won't make a difference, and others simply don't have enough information."},{"q":"Where do you get most of your news?","au":"dfe21c8e22","es":"¿De dónde sacas la mayoría de tus noticias?","ex":"Mostly from news apps and podcasts, but I try to compare several sources before I believe something."}],"reading":{"title":"Is Democracy Ready for the Future?","img":"u:photo-1520525003249-2b9cdda513bc","text":"Democracy has survived wars, economic crises, and technological revolutions. Yet many political scientists believe it now faces a distinctive set of challenges, and that the way societies respond will shape the coming decades. The first challenge is information. A healthy democracy depends on a well-informed citizenry, but the digital environment makes it easy for misinformation to spread faster than corrections. When citizens cannot agree on basic facts, constructive debate becomes difficult. The second is polarization. In several countries, surveys suggest that people increasingly view those with different political opinions not merely as opponents but as enemies. This can erode trust in elections, courts, and the press, the very institutions that provide checks and balances. A third concern is participation. Voter turnout varies widely, and some citizens, particularly younger ones, say they feel their voices are not heard. Not everyone is pessimistic, however. Optimists point out that technology also creates new forms of civic engagement. Citizens can follow legislative debates live, contact their representatives directly, and organize community projects in hours rather than months. Some cities have experimented with participatory budgeting, allowing residents to decide how part of the public budget is spent. Others have tried citizens' assemblies, in which randomly selected residents study an issue and make recommendations. Granted, none of these innovations is a cure-all. But they suggest that democracy is not a finished product; it is a system that can adapt. Its future may depend less on any single leader or party than on whether ordinary citizens remain willing to listen, participate, and hold leaders accountable.","au":"392bd50531","q":[{"s":"The article argues that misinformation can make constructive debate difficult.","a":"yes"},{"s":"According to the text, polarization tends to increase trust in institutions.","a":"no"},{"s":"Some younger citizens feel their voices are not heard.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Participatory budgeting lets residents decide how part of the public budget is spent.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The author believes democracy is a finished product that cannot change.","a":"no"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"What is the biggest challenge for democracy today?","a":"Many experts point to misinformation, since a democracy depends on a well-informed citizenry.","es":"¿Cuál es el mayor reto para la democracia hoy?","qau":"b45bec9d04","aau":"ec62d8feb3"},{"q":"Could technology strengthen democracy?","a":"Granted, it can spread misinformation, but it can also make it easier for citizens to participate and hold leaders accountable.","es":"¿Podría la tecnología fortalecer la democracia?","qau":"99ec72a682","aau":"cead2f302f"},{"q":"Should voting be compulsory?","a":"I take the point that it would increase turnout, but I believe people should be free to choose.","es":"¿Debería ser obligatorio votar?","qau":"6dfaa57334","aau":"87dc7f898d"},{"q":"How can we reduce polarization?","a":"Perhaps by listening to people we disagree with and focusing on shared problems rather than labels.","es":"¿Cómo podemos reducir la polarización?","qau":"5c52437eca","aau":"5b9dc37c3c"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe un ensayo corto (120–150 palabras): ¿cómo podemos fortalecer la democracia en el futuro? Mantén un tono neutral (sin partidos ni políticos), concede un punto (Granted…, I take the point that…) y propone dos ideas concretas.","kw":["Granted","hold leaders accountable","civic engagement"],"n":7,"model":"Democracy faces significant challenges, but I believe it can be strengthened if citizens and institutions adapt. One of the most serious problems is misinformation, which spreads quickly online and makes it hard to agree on basic facts. Granted, technology is partly responsible for this, yet it can also be part of the solution. First, schools could teach media literacy so that young people learn to evaluate sources critically. Second, local governments could expand civic engagement through initiatives such as participatory budgeting or citizens' assemblies, which give ordinary people a real voice. A free press and independent courts are also essential to hold leaders accountable. Ultimately, the future of democracy does not depend on a single election, but on our willingness to listen, participate, and respect those who disagree."}}]},{"n":21,"title":"Space Exploration: Progress or Vanity?","es":"Exploración espacial: ¿progreso o vanidad?","cover":"u:photo-1457364887197-9150188c107b","parts":[{"id":"t21p1","topic":21,"part":1,"title":"Class","es":"Debate: ¿vale la pena explorar el espacio?","acts":["learn","spaceCountdown","dialogue","fill","raceGame","speak"],"tip":"<p>Para <b>formular hipótesis</b> con estilo C1 usamos la <b>inversión</b> en las condicionales (más formal, típica de debates y ensayos):</p>\n<p>🚀 <b>Had</b> + sujeto + participio = <i>If… had…</i> → <i><b>Had we not explored</b> space, we wouldn't have GPS.</i> (Si no hubiéramos explorado…)</p>\n<p>🪐 <b>Were</b> + sujeto + <b>to</b> + verbo = <i>If… were to…</i> → <i><b>Were we to colonize</b> Mars, we would face ethical questions.</i> (Si llegáramos a…)</p>\n<p>🛰️ <b>Should</b> + sujeto + verbo = <i>If… ever…</i> → <i><b>Should humanity need</b> a second home, …</i> (Si alguna vez…)</p>\n<p>🔀 <b>Condicional mixta</b> (pasado → presente): <i>If we <b>hadn't explored</b> space, we <b>wouldn't have</b> satellite TV <b>today</b>.</i></p>\n<p>⚠️ En la inversión <b>no</b> se usa <i>if</i>: ❌ <i>If had we…</i> · ✅ <i>Had we…</i></p>","tips":["<b>Mars</b> suena <i>MARS</i>, con 'r' americana suave.","<b>satellite</b>: <i>SÁ-te-lait</i>; la 't' del medio suena casi como una 'r' suave.","<b>breakthrough</b>: <i>BRÉIK-zru</i>; la 'gh' final no suena."],"vocab":[{"en":"space exploration","es":"exploración espacial","img":"u:photo-1592561199818-6b69d3d1d6e2","v":"f","au":"785eecb17d"},{"en":"a crewed mission","es":"una misión tripulada","img":"u:photo-1457364887197-9150188c107b","v":"m","au":"db6af277f6"},{"en":"satellite technology","es":"tecnología satelital","img":"u:photo-1770370419338-f9a813302baa","v":"f","au":"5acd2df5ad"},{"en":"the private space industry","es":"la industria espacial privada","img":"u:photo-1457364887197-9150188c107b","v":"m","au":"7cae7e78b6"},{"en":"a vanity project","es":"un proyecto de vanidad","img":"#a vanity project 🪞","v":"f","au":"feea00f143"},{"en":"pressing problems on Earth","es":"problemas urgentes en la Tierra","img":"u:photo-1657069345471-c54f2432b79c","v":"m","au":"9e633ecec6"},{"en":"to colonize Mars","es":"colonizar Marte","img":"u:photo-1630694093867-4b947d812bf0","v":"f","au":"1be6621b2f"},{"en":"scientific breakthroughs","es":"avances científicos","img":"u:photo-1518152006812-edab29b069ac","v":"m","au":"88f99a39fb"},{"en":"a waste of resources","es":"un desperdicio de recursos","img":"u:photo-1744130400729-c4aee523f490","v":"f","au":"3a01f7d8d9"},{"en":"spin-off technologies","es":"tecnologías derivadas","img":"u:photo-1694813646391-4c505039c2ee","v":"m","au":"8dbff5703e"},{"en":"Were we to…, …","es":"Si llegáramos a…, …","img":"#Were we to…, …","v":"f","au":"1846148eaa"},{"en":"Had we not…, …","es":"Si no hubiéramos…, …","img":"#Had we not…, …","v":"m","au":"4be0ac9b52"}],"sentences":[{"en":"Had we not explored space, we wouldn't have GPS or accurate weather forecasts.","es":"Si no hubiéramos explorado el espacio, no tendríamos GPS ni pronósticos del tiempo precisos.","img":"u:photo-1770370419338-f9a813302baa","v":"f","au":"081109b867"},{"en":"Were we to colonize Mars, we would face enormous ethical questions.","es":"Si llegáramos a colonizar Marte, enfrentaríamos enormes preguntas éticas.","img":"u:photo-1630694093867-4b947d812bf0","v":"m","au":"d478ea361e"},{"en":"Critics see private space tourism as a vanity project for billionaires.","es":"Los críticos ven el turismo espacial privado como un proyecto de vanidad para multimillonarios.","img":"u:photo-1457364887197-9150188c107b","v":"f","au":"aa97b370ab"},{"en":"Some argue the money should be spent on pressing problems on Earth.","es":"Algunos sostienen que el dinero debería gastarse en problemas urgentes en la Tierra.","img":"u:photo-1657069345471-c54f2432b79c","v":"m","au":"4da188effa"},{"en":"Space research has led to many scientific breakthroughs.","es":"La investigación espacial ha llevado a muchos avances científicos.","img":"u:photo-1518152006812-edab29b069ac","v":"f","au":"fcbdb34eaf"},{"en":"Should humanity ever need a second home, Mars might be the only option.","es":"Si la humanidad alguna vez necesitara un segundo hogar, Marte podría ser la única opción.","img":"u:photo-1592561199818-6b69d3d1d6e2","v":"m","au":"44f2c34931"}],"fill":[{"s":"___ we to invest more in space, we might discover new resources.","a":"Were","o":["Was","If"],"h":"inversión: Were + sujeto + to…","full":"Were we to invest more in space, we might discover new resources.","au":"4cbbc211c8"},{"s":"Had NASA not ___ satellites, weather forecasts would be far less accurate.","a":"launched","o":["launch","launching"],"h":"Had + sujeto + not + participio","full":"Had NASA not launched satellites, weather forecasts would be far less accurate.","au":"a11031f079"},{"s":"Space tourism is often criticized as a ___ project.","a":"vanity","o":["vain","vanished"],"h":"a vanity project","full":"Space tourism is often criticized as a vanity project.","au":"d0a72e53d6"},{"s":"Many everyday products come from ___ technologies developed for space.","a":"spin-off","o":["spin-out","spinning"],"h":"tecnologías derivadas","full":"Many everyday products come from spin-off technologies developed for space.","au":"296884fa1a"},{"s":"___ humanity ever need to leave Earth, we should be prepared.","a":"Should","o":["Would","Could"],"h":"Should + sujeto = si alguna vez","full":"Should humanity ever need to leave Earth, we should be prepared.","au":"2e4e2c7c13"},{"s":"If we hadn't explored space, we ___ have satellite TV today.","a":"wouldn't","o":["won't","didn't"],"h":"condicional mixta","full":"If we hadn't explored space, we wouldn't have satellite TV today.","au":"85af99982a"},{"s":"Some argue it is a waste of ___ when so many people are struggling.","a":"resources","o":["sources","recourses"],"h":"desperdicio de recursos","full":"Some argue it is a waste of resources when so many people are struggling.","au":"001bfb53f6"}],"dialogue":{"title":"Mars or Earth first?","es":"¿Primero Marte o la Tierra?","img":"u:photo-1457364887197-9150188c107b","lines":[{"who":"Olivia","v":"f","t":"Every time I see a rocket launch, I feel proud of what humanity can do. Space exploration inspires people.","au":"65055fb5b0"},{"who":"Sam","v":"m","t":"Inspiration is lovely, but billions of dollars could go to fighting poverty or climate change right here on Earth.","au":"3e0c4e1cad"},{"who":"Olivia","v":"f","t":"Had we not invested in space, though, we wouldn't have the weather satellites that help us track hurricanes and climate change.","au":"19b22a8dc0"},{"who":"Sam","v":"m","t":"Fair enough, satellites are useful. My problem is with billionaires flying tourists to the edge of space. That's a vanity project.","au":"3fafdbdc9d"},{"who":"Diego","v":"m","t":"I'd distinguish between the two. Scientific research is one thing; luxury space tourism is quite another.","au":"30a95ea584"},{"who":"Olivia","v":"f","t":"Even so, private companies have made launches much cheaper, which benefits scientific missions too.","au":"c51f130668"},{"who":"Diego","v":"m","t":"True. Were governments to set clear rules, public and private efforts could complement each other.","au":"77461de879"},{"who":"Sam","v":"m","t":"All right, I'll concede that. Science, yes. Joyrides for the ultra-rich, not so much.","au":"dd4adfa1c5"}],"q":[{"q":"Why does Olivia support space exploration?","a":"It inspires people and gives us useful technology.","o":["It makes rockets more expensive.","It replaces all other science."]},{"q":"What does Sam call space tourism?","a":"A vanity project.","o":["A scientific breakthrough.","A cheap vacation."]},{"q":"What distinction does Diego make?","a":"Between scientific research and luxury space tourism.","o":["Between Mars and the Moon.","Between rich and poor countries."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To debate whether space exploration is worth the cost, using inverted conditionals to express hypotheses.","es":"Debatir si la exploración espacial vale lo que cuesta, usando condicionales invertidas para expresar hipótesis."},"warm":[{"q":"Would you travel to space if you had the chance?","au":"182cd28e63","es":"¿Viajarías al espacio si tuvieras la oportunidad?","ex":"I'd love to see Earth from orbit, but I'm not sure I'd be brave enough to sit on top of a rocket!"},{"q":"What do you think is the most important invention of the last hundred years?","au":"bf4a3fafc7","es":"¿Cuál crees que es el invento más importante de los últimos cien años?","ex":"I'd say the internet, because it has changed how we work, learn, and communicate."}],"reading":{"title":"Reaching for the Stars: Progress or Vanity?","img":"u:photo-1592561199818-6b69d3d1d6e2","text":"When the first humans walked on the Moon in 1969, millions of people watched in awe. More than half a century later, space exploration is back in the headlines, but this time the conversation is more divided. Supporters argue that space programs produce benefits far beyond the launch pad. Satellite technology underpins GPS navigation, weather forecasting, and global communications. Research carried out for space missions has contributed to spin-off technologies in fields such as medical imaging and water purification. Had we not invested in space, they point out, many everyday conveniences would not exist. Observing Earth from orbit has also become essential for monitoring climate change and natural disasters. Skeptics are not convinced. With so many pressing problems on Earth, including hunger, disease, and climate change, they argue that spending vast sums on rockets is hard to justify. Their criticism has sharpened with the rise of the private space industry: when billionaires fly to the edge of space for a few minutes, critics see a vanity project rather than a contribution to science. Supporters respond that private companies have dramatically reduced launch costs through reusable rockets, which benefits scientific missions too. Some even argue that, were we to face a global catastrophe, a human presence on Mars could one day help ensure our survival. Perhaps the most balanced position distinguishes between purposes. Scientific exploration that expands knowledge and protects our planet seems easy to defend; space tourism for the very rich is far more controversial. Either way, the question is not simply whether we should look up at the stars, but who should pay and who should benefit.","au":"3ad7a6bcf6","q":[{"s":"Satellite technology supports GPS and weather forecasting.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Space research has led to useful spin-off technologies.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Skeptics believe space spending is easy to justify.","a":"no"},{"s":"Reusable rockets have made launches more expensive.","a":"no"},{"s":"The author distinguishes between scientific exploration and space tourism.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Is space exploration a waste of money?","a":"I don't think so. Had we not explored space, we wouldn't have GPS or modern weather forecasts.","es":"¿Es la exploración espacial un desperdicio de dinero?","qau":"b218b1a85a","aau":"677eb76d71"},{"q":"Should private companies lead space exploration?","a":"They can reduce costs, but were they to control space completely, profit might matter more than science.","es":"¿Deberían las empresas privadas liderar la exploración espacial?","qau":"989fe7c52e","aau":"63c557c7af"},{"q":"Should humans try to colonize Mars?","a":"It's an exciting idea, but I think we should solve pressing problems on Earth first.","es":"¿Deberían los seres humanos intentar colonizar Marte?","qau":"e4be7b6ae5","aau":"4fe5a28a54"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe un ensayo corto (120–150 palabras): exploración espacial, ¿progreso o vanidad? Usa al menos una condicional invertida (Had we not…, Were we to…, Should…).","kw":["Had we not","Were we to","pressing problems"],"n":7,"model":"Space exploration divides opinion, but in my view it represents genuine progress, provided it serves science rather than vanity. Had we not invested in space programs, we would not have GPS, accurate weather forecasts, or satellites that monitor climate change. Many spin-off technologies, from medical imaging to water filters, also originated in space research. However, critics make a fair point: with so many pressing problems on Earth, public money must be spent responsibly. Space tourism for billionaires is difficult to defend as a priority. Were we to focus on scientific missions that protect our planet and expand knowledge, few people would object to the cost. On balance, I believe space exploration is worthwhile, as long as its benefits are shared by humanity as a whole."}}]}],"letters":{"A":"6d717a50cb","B":"80c0feee5f","C":"d87275787d","D":"82c3a5fb2d","E":"9f7b646ba8","F":"d60431768d","G":"7cba883078","H":"c26de21099","I":"11b70e698d","J":"7280c01c88","K":"8f887ac900","L":"8e684bf3bf","M":"ab15838f42","N":"adbb42df84","O":"7b127b9991","P":"61fb4061f6","Q":"5e7027877b","R":"b634d637b4","S":"5b84a3506b","T":"77a78fbc1b","U":"df6d7e37af","V":"354ccded81","W":"d3d0b1df88","X":"64808c2c00","Y":"5724debb9c","Z":"9d81304034"},"praise":{"Awesome!":"98561b5346","Great job!":"a88a2d51d2","Perfect!":"9abc262823","Excellent!":"54f1859c38","Well done!":"b93b9f5f0f","You got it!":"1a9de5fa28","Fantastic!":"d5bfd68ea5","Nice work!":"aa2b15da71"},"retry":{"Try again.":"e4bbac6f81","Almost! Listen again.":"2ace7bd775","Not quite. You can do it!":"8b4c184411"}};
